hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"30061","(30061) Ibn Aliya narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Burda, who said: I sat with a sheikh from The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were in the Kufa Mosque and he spoke to me. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, or the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O people, repent to God and ask forgiveness from Him, for I repent to God. And I ask for forgiveness a hundred times every day. He said: I said: Oh God, I ask for your forgiveness two times. He said: This is what I say to you. (Nasa’i 10278. Ahmad 260)"
"30062","(30062) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, a partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, who said: Who I ask forgiveness from God, who there is no god but Him, the Ever-Living, the Self-Subsisting, and I repent to Him three times. He will be forgiven, even if he fled from the advance."
"30063","(30063) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said: Whoever says, “I ask forgiveness from God, there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Self-Subsisting, and I repent to Him three times,” will be forgiven, even if he fled from the onslaught."
"30064","(30064) Abu Dawud Al-Hafari narrated to us Omar bin Saad, on the authority of Yunus bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Abdullah Bin Amr, he said: Whoever says, Glory be to God, the Great, and praise be to Him, a palm tree will be planted for him in Paradise. \n(Tabarani 352, Ahmad 239)"
"30065","Abu Abdul Rahman narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying:\n(30065) Suleiman bin Hayyan narrated to us, Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Muadh, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The son of Adam did not do any work that saved him from the Fire than the remembrance of God. They said: O Messenger of God, not even jihad in the way of God? He said: Not even jihad in the way of God, unless you strike with your sword until it breaks, then strike with it until it breaks, then You beat it until it breaks."
"30066","(30066) Zayd bin Hubab told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told us, he said: Amr bin Qais Al-Kindi informed me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, that a Bedouin said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: O Messenger of God, the laws of Islam have It has increased, so tell me something about it that I can cling to. He said: Your tongue continues to be moist with the remembrance of God. (Tirmidhi 2329. Ahmad 188)"
"30067","(30067) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Ayoub Al-Ansari, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever says there is no god but God alone, without any partner, he has no partner. Sovereignty, to Him belongs all praise, in His hand is goodness, and He has power over all things ten times, be to Him as equal to ten slaves, or Neck (Muslim 2071, Ahmad 422)"
"30068","(30068) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja, on the authority of al-Bara’ ibn Azib, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who says there is no god but God alone, without any partner, to him belongs the kingdom, and to Him is praise. And He has power over all things. It was like freeing slaves. (Ahmad 2851 Hakim 501)"
"30069","(30069) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of Bishr bin Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: The remembrance of God In the morning and the evening is greater than smashing swords in the way of God, and giving money as a weapon."
"30070","(30070) Yahya bin Wadh narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Qaraz, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever loves to enjoy the gardens of Paradise, let him remember God often. (Tabarani 326)"
"30071","(30071) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, on the authority of Mu’adh, who said: Because I remember Allah from A morning until the sun rises is more beloved to me than being led to wage jihad in the path of God than a morning until the sun rises."
"30072","(30072) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Mu’awiyah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Darda’, he said: Those whose tongues are still wet from the remembrance of God will enter Paradise and they laugh."
"30073","(30073) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Misra, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Amr bin Maymoun, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym, on the authority of Abdullah, said: Whoever says ten times: There is no god but Allah alone, no Your partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is Able over all things. Be to Him the equal of four slaves. I see him saying: Who is born? Ismail."
"30074","(30074) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, she said: Who said A hundred times in the morning and a hundred times in the evening: There is no god but Allah alone, without any partner. To Him belongs the kingdom, and to Him is praise, and He is He has power over all things. No one will come on the Day of Resurrection with anything like what he was brought with, except those who said the like of them, or more."
"30075","(30075) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Muadh bin Jabal said: If only Two men carrying one of them on the horses in the way of God, while the other remembers God. He would be better, or have a greater reward. The remembrancer"
"30076","(30076) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Mufaddal, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith. Ibn Hisham, on the authority of Ka’b, said: Moses said: O Lord, direct me to a deed that, if I do it, will be a thank you for what you have done for me. He said: O Moses, say: There is no god but Allah, or he said: There is no god but Allah alone, there is no partner with Him. To Him belongs the kingdom, and to Him is praise, and He is upon Him. He has power over all things. He said: It is as if Moses intended to do something to relieve his body of what he was commanded to do. He said: So he said to him: O Moses, if the seven heavens and the seven earths were placed on a palm, and La ilaha illa Allah were placed on a palm, it would prevail. Here"
"30077","(30077) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salim, who said: It was said to Abu Al-Darda’: Abu Sa’ad bin Munabbih put in his wealth A hundred freed, and he said: A hundred freed is a man’s wealth for a lot. Shall I not inform you of something better than that, out of belief that the night will remain? And the day, and your tongue will never cease to be moist from the remembrance of God."
"30078","(30078) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Jahil, he said : Whoever says after the afternoon prayer: There is no god but Allah, to Him belongs all praise and He has power over all things, they will fight on behalf of the one who said it, as in the case of those who said it. Tomorrow"
"30079","(30079) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Muslim, a client of Suwayd ibn Juhail, on the authority of Suwayd, said: He was one of the companions of Omar, then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Waki’."
"30080","(30080) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Saad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: The servant is what He mentioned God, and he was in prayer."
"30081","(30081) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Masruq, who said: As long as a man’s heart remembers God, he is in peace. Prayer, even if it is in the market."
"30082","(30082) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: As long as a man’s heart remembers God, then he In prayer, even if he is in the market, and if he moves his lips with it, that is better."
"30083","(30083) Marhum bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Naama al-Saadi, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: Muawiyah went out to meet a group in the mosque and said: He did not make you sit. They said: We sat to remember God. And we praise Him for what He has guided us to Islam and who has bestowed upon us with it. He said: By God, we have not made you sit except that one. They said: By God, we have not made you sit. Except that, and he said: I did not make you swear to be an orphan of yours, and there is no one in your position as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He has fewer hadiths than me, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to a group of his companions and said: What Did he make you sit? They said: We sat remembering God and praising Him for what He has guided us to Islam and for bestowing it on us. He said: God has not made you sit except that. They said: By God, we did not sit with anyone except that one. He said: I did not make you swear to be an oath out of concern for you, but rather Gabriel came to me. So he told me that God is proud of you among the angels. (Muslim 2075. Tirmidhi 3379)"
"30084","(30084) Zayd bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, he said: Ubaad bin The silent one: Because I am more beloved to me than being among a people who remember God from the time they pray the morning prayer until the sun rises. On the mounts of horses I will strive in the way of God until the sun rises, and I will be among a people who remember when they pray. The afternoon prayer until the sun sets is more beloved to me than being on horses, striving in the cause of God until the sun sets."
"30085","(30085) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, who said: If a man spent the night giving If someone else spent the night reading the Qur’an or remembering God Almighty, you would have thought that that was the case, or he would have said: Remembering God is better."
"30086","(30086) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Abu al-Wazi’ Jabir al-Rasi, on the authority of Abu Barzah, he said: If there were two men, one of them holding dinars in his lap to give away, and the other remembering God, the remembrance of God would be better."
"30087","(30087) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Tha’labah ibn Amr narrated to me, on the authority of Amr ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: If two men came, one from the east and the other from the west, with one of them, there would be no He puts none of it except in truth, and the other remembers God, until they meet on the same path. He was the one who remembers God. The best of them"
"30088","(30088) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is nothing more beloved to God than gratitude. And the remembrance."
"30089","(30089) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, Ammar bin Ruzaiq narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aghar Abu Muslim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa`id bear witness to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: No Muslim people sat. A gathering in which they remember God, except that the angels surround them and mercy covers them, and tranquility descends upon them. And God remembered them among those with him. (Tirmidhi 3378 and Ibn Majah 3791)"
"30090","(30090) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas informed me, he said: Sumayy, the servant of Abu Bakr, informed me, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever says on a day a hundred times: No. There is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. He is just. ten slaves, and a hundred good deeds were recorded for him, and a hundred bad deeds were erased from him, and it was for him a protection from Satan His day continued until nightfall, and no one brought anything better than what he brought except he who said more. (Bukhari 3293, Muslim 2071)"
"30091","(30091) Affan narrated to us, Aban bin Yazid Al-Attar narrated to us, his leaders narrated to us, he said: Abu Al-Aliyah Al-Rihihi narrated, on the authority of The hadith of Suhail bin Hanzala Al-Abashmi, that he said: No people ever gathered to remember God except that a herald called from the heavens: Arise. You will be forgiven. Your bad deeds have been changed into good deeds."
"30092","(30092) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, who said: There was a woman from Hamdan. She recites the tasbih and counts pebbles, or stones. So she passed by Abdullah, and it was said to him: This woman recites the tasbih and counts the pebbles. Or the night prayers? So he called her and said: To her: Are you the one who glorifies God and chants? She said: Yes, I will do it. He said: Shall I not guide you to something better than that? You will say: God is Greatest, and praise be to God. A lot, and Glory be to God, morning and evening."
"30093","(30093) Affan narrated to us, Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Aghar Abi Muslim, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding what he narrates, on the authority of his Lord, he said: Whoever remembers Me to himself I have mentioned it to myself, and whoever mentions Me in a gathering of people, I have mentioned it in a gathering more and better than them. (Ahmad 354, Ibn Hibban 328)"
"30094","(30094) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, who said: If the servant praises God in good things, and He praises Him in the prosperity. Then adversity befell him, so he called upon God. The angels said: A well-known voice from a weak person, so they will intercede for him. And if the servant does not remember God in the good times, nor praise Him in the good things, and harm befalls him, then he supplicates to God, the angels say: An objectionable voice."
"30095","(30095) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Asbagh bin Zaid, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, he said: God He gives charity every day, and nothing is better than his remembrance."
"30096","(30096) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Whoever says on the day: There is no god but God is alone, there is no partner to Him. To Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. Be to Him the justice of four slaves. He frees them from the descendants of Ishmael."
"30097","(30097) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of al-Bara’ Ibn Aazib, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who says there is no god but God alone, with no partner, to him belongs dominion. To Him belongs all praise, and He has power over all things. Ten times, it is as equal to the name of His name. (Nasa’i 9953. Tabarani 1717)"
"30098","(30098) Muhammad ibn Ubaid narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, on the authority of Abu Ra’afah, a man from the Ansar. On the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, he said: Whoever says a hundred times today: There is no god but Allah alone, there is no partner with Him. To Him belongs the kingdom and to Him. Praise be to Him, and He has power over all things. No one from the people of the world has brought anything better than what He has brought, except the person Yazeed. Aliyah"
"30099","(30099) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, that Omar went out to draw water and ascended the pulpit and said: {Ask forgiveness of your Lord. Indeed, He is ever Forgiving. He sends down rain upon you from the heavens, and provides you with wealth and children, and makes for you Gardens and He makes for you rivers, and {Ask forgiveness of your Lord; indeed, He is ever Forgiving.} Then he descended, and it was said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, If I had asked for rain, he would have said: I have asked for the glories of the heavens from which the drops descend."
"30100","(30100) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Issa bin Hafs, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father, he said: We went out with Omar. Ibn Al-Khattab: We ask for water, nothing more than seeking forgiveness."
"30101","(30101) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, that Suleiman bin Dawud went out With the people seeking water, he passed by an ants lying on their backs, raising their legs to the heavens, and they said, O God, we are We are a creation of your creation. We are indispensable to your provision. Either you provide us with water or you destroy us. So Solomon said to the people: Return. You have been given water by the claims of others."
"30102","(30102) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Peace and blessings of God be upon him. He seeks refuge in these words: Remove the affliction, Lord of people, and heal, You are the Healer. There is no cure except Your healing, a cure that does not depart. Illness, she said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became ill due to the illness in which he died, I took his hand and began to wipe it. And I say it, she said: So he took his hand from hers and said: O God, forgive me and join me with a comrade, she said: So it was like this. The last I heard from him."
"30103","(30103) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He acknowledged the hadith of Abu Muawiyah, except that he did not say: When it became heavy. (Muslim 1722 and Ibn Majah 3520)"
"30104","(30104) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say to the sick person: Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal, You are the healer. There is no cure except your healing, a cure that cannot be cured. He leaves an illness. Sufyan said: I mentioned it to Mansour and he told me, on the authority of Abraham, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 5750 and Muslim 1722)"
"30105","(30105) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was When he entered upon a sick person, he, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Remove the affliction, Lord of people, and heal. You are the Healer. There is no healer but You."
"30106","(30106) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Rabbah, on the authority of Amrah, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to say to the sick person: With a slug on his finger, in the name of God our land will be raised, with each other’s saliva he will be healed. We are sick, by the permission of our Lord."
"30107","(30107) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ziyad bin Thuwaib, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me while I was complaining, and he said: Shall I not perform ruqyah for you with a ruqyah that Gabriel taught me? : In the name of God, I promote you, and God will heal you from every evil that harms you, from the evil of blowers at the knot, and from the evil of the envier when he envies you."
"30108","(30108) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever enters upon a sick person, his death will not be present, and he says: I ask God The Great, Lord of the Great Throne, may Heal you seven times. He has been healed."
"30109","(30109) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, he said: Umair ibn Hani informed me, he said: I heard Junada ibn Abi Umayyah says: I heard Ubad ibn al-Samit narrating, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that Gabriel shunned him while he was unwell and said: In the name of God, I protect you from every disease that harms you, from every envier when he envies, and from every Eye, and the name of God will heal you."
"30110","(30110) Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, Zakaria ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, Samak narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Hatib, he said: I took a pot of ours and my hands were burned, so my mother went with me to a man sitting in the grave, and she said to him: Oh Messenger of God, and he said: I am at your service and I am happy with you. Then she brought me closer to him and he began to breathe and speak. I do not know what that was, so I asked My mother, what did he say after that? She said: He used to say: Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal, You are the Healer. There is no healer but You."
"30111","(30111) Ubaidah bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to seek refuge with Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein with these words: I seek refuge with the perfect words of God from evil. Every devil and wild beast and every evil eye is a mother. He said: And Abraham used to seek refuge with it in Ishmael and Isaac."
"30112","(30112) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge with Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein, then he mentioned something similar to it, but he did not He says: And evil."
"30113","(30113) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali, who said: I complained, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me and I was saying: Oh God, if my time has come, then have mercy on me. Late, so heal me, or heal me, and if it is an affliction, then give me patience. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: How did you say? He said: So I told him, so he wiped me with his hand, then said: Oh God, heal him, or make him well, and I never complained of that pain after that."
"30114","(30114) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifi, on the authority of Omar Ibn Abdullah Ibn Ka'b, on the authority of Nafi' Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Othman Ibn Abi Al-Aas Al-Thaqafi, who said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I was suffering from pain that almost made me weak, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: Keep your right hand on him. Then say: In the name of God, I seek refuge in God’s glory and power from the evil I befall, seven times, so I did, and God Almighty healed me."
"30115","(30115) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Abi Habib, he said: Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us about pain. Both and the fever, this supplication: In the name of God the Great, I seek refuge in God Almighty from the evil of every race of fire, and from the evil of the heat of the Fire."
"30116","(30116) Muhammad bin Al-Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Al-Fudayl bin Amr, who said: A man came to Ali. He said: So-and-so is suspicious. He said: You would be pleased if he was healed. He said: Yes. He said: Say: O Forbearing, O Generous, heal three times."
"30117","(30117) Ahmad bin Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained, and Gabriel comforted him and said: In the name of God, I give you ruqyah from everything that harms you. Every envious and evil eye, and God will heal you."
"30118","(30118) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa`id, on the authority of Amra bint Abd al-Rahman, who said: Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, complained that Abu Bakr entered upon her while she was a Jew and said: Perform ruqyah for her with a letter. God"
"30119","(30119) Affan narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Whenever he visited a sick person, he would say: Remove the affliction, Lord of people, and heal, You are the Healer. There is no healer but You, a healer who does not leave behind an illness. (Bukhari 5742, Abu Dawud 3886)"
"30120","(30120) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim, on the authority of Ali bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to the village of Banu Muawiyah and I followed He followed her until he appeared over her and prayed eight rak'ahs at length, then he left and said: O Hudhaifa, it has been too long for you. I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: I asked God about it three times and He gave me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to He appeared before my nation other than it, so he gave it to me, and I asked him not to destroy it with years, so he gave it to me, and I asked him not to He made her misfortune clear, so he prevented me from doing so."
"30121","(30121) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Raja’ Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed a prayer one day, but he prolonged it. When he left, I said: O Messenger of God, you have prolonged it. Today is the prayer. He said: I prayed a prayer of hope and fear, and I asked God for three for my nation, and He gave me two and answered me. One, I asked him not to let an enemy from other than them rule over them, so he gave it to me, and I asked him not to let them drown by drowning. So he gave it to me, and I asked him not to share anything with them, and she responded to me. (احمد ۲۴۰۔ ابن خزیمہ ۱۲۱۸)"
"30122","(30122) Abu Asama narrated to us, Sulayman bin Al-Mughiriya narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, On the authority of Suhayb, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed, he would whisper something and would not tell us about it, so we said: O Messenger By God, when you pray, you touch something that we cannot understand. He said, “Have you thought about it?” I said: Yes. He said: I mentioned one of the prophets who was given soldiers from his people. He looked at them and said: Who will reward them? These, he said: Then it was said to him: Choose for your people one of three things: either an enemy from other than them will dominate them, or hunger, or Death. He said: So he presented that to his people. He said: They said: You are the Prophet of God, so choose for us. He said: So he stood up to pray. He said: And they were When they become terrified, they begin to pray, so he prayed and said: O God, whether you give power over them from someone else, no, or hunger, no, but death, he said. So He imposed death upon them, and seventy thousand of them died within three days. He said: Then what you hear whispered to me that I say: Oh God. By You I try and by You I reach my foundation, and there is no power or strength except by You. (Nasa’i 10450. Ahmad 333)"
"30123","(30123) Ibn Numayr told us, Othman bin Hakim told us, Aamir bin Saad told us, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God One day, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he approached from the highest place and, as he passed by the mosque of Banu Mu’awiyah, he entered and kneeled in it. We prayed two rak'ahs and we prayed with him, and he prayed to his Lord for a long time, then he turned to us and said: I asked my Lord for three, and He gave me two and replied. Ali alone. I asked my Lord not to destroy my nation with the Sunnah, and He gave it to me. I asked Him not to destroy my nation. By drowning, so he gave it to me, and I asked him not to share his share with them, but he denied it to me. (Muslim 2216. Ahmad 181)"
"30124","(30124) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd, on the authority of al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah, that Abu Bakr was He says: Oh God, make the best of my life its last, the best of my deeds its last, and the best of my days the day I meet you. He said: And it was Omar says: O God, protect me with Your rope, bless me with Your bounty, and make me preserve Your command."
"30125","(30125) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Jami’ ibn Shaddad, on the authority of his father, he said: It was the first thing he spoke. With it, Omar said: Oh God, I am weak, so strengthen me, and I am strong, so soften me, and I am stingy, so make me hot."
"30126","(30126) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hassan bin Faid Al-Absi, on the authority of Omar, that He used to pray: Oh God, put richness in my heart and my desire for what you have and bless me with what you have provided for me and make me rich from what you have. It was forbidden to me."
"30127","(30127) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, that he used to say: Oh God I seek Your forgiveness for my sin, and I seek Your guidance for the guidance of my affairs, and I repent to You, so have mercy on me. Indeed, You are my Lord, O God, so make My desire is for You, and place wealth in my breast, and bless for me what You have bestowed upon me, and accept from me, for You are my Lord."
"30128","(30128) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: A man in Omar’s presence said, O God Make me a little, he said, and he said: Omar: What is this that you are praying for? He said: I heard God saying: And few of My servants are thankful, so I pray that He makes me one of those few. He said: So he said: Omar: Everyone is more knowledgeable than Omar."
"30129","(30129) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: I heard Omar saying, O God, grant us health. And pardon us."
"30130","(30130) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Tuamah bin Abdullah, on the authority of a man who is said to be Mikail, a sheikh from among the people of Khorasan, he said: When Omar got up at night, he would say: You may see my position and know my need, so take me back from you, O God, in my need, healed. Successful, responding and responding to me. You have forgiven me and have mercy on me. So when he finished his prayer, he said: Oh God, I do not see anything of this world. It lasts, and I do not see a situation in it that is right. Oh God, make me speak it with knowledge and keep silent with wisdom. Oh God, do not multiply it. Of this world and he transgresses, and do not give me less of it or I forget, for what is little and sufficient is better than what is greater and more pleasing to him."
"30131","(30131) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Sulaym ibn Hanzala, on the authority of Omar, that he used to say: Oh God, I I seek refuge in You lest you take me by surprise, or leave me in your heedlessness, or make me among the heedless."
"30132","(30132) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali, that it was He supplicates: Oh God, make us steadfast in the word of justice, with satisfaction and truth, and the uprightness of the Book, guided, guided, and contented. Satisfied, not going astray, nor being led astray."
"30133","(30133) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abi Al-Walid, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of Ali, that He used to say in his supplication: Oh God, I ask you by your mercy with which you encompass all things, and by your might with which you have humbled Through it all things, and through it He submitted all things to you, and through it He subdued all things for you, and through Your might by which You conquered all things. anything, and by your greatness with which you have conquered all things, and by your authority with which you have filled all things, and by your infinite power Nothing is established for it, and with your light that illuminated everything for it, and with your knowledge that encompassed all things, and with your name that With Him everything begins, and with Your face that remains after the annihilation of everything, O Light, O Holy, O Light, O Holy, three times. O the first of the firsts and the last of the last, O God, O Most Merciful, O Most Merciful, forgive me the sins that bring down vengeance, and forgive For me are the sins that violate my right, and forgive me the sins that cause remorse, and forgive me the sins that withhold an oath, and forgive me the sins that lead to remorse. Which changes the blessings, and forgive me the sins that inflict calamities, and ward off enemies, and forgive me the sins that withhold rain. heavens, hasten annihilation, darken the air, reject supplications, and forgive me the sins that are returned to the Fire."
"30134","(30134) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Asadi, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ali, who said: He used to say: Oh God. The Defender of the praiseworthy, the builder of buildings, the anchor of anchorages, the tyrant of hearts despite their wretched nature. And He who is happy with it, and who extends mercy to the righteous, make the honors of your prayers, the nights of your blessings, the compassions of your compassion, and the affections of your prayers. Your mercy upon Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, the Conqueror of that which was sealed, and the Seal of that which preceded, and the One who unites truth with truth, and destroys the enmities of falsehoods as You have burdened him with, so carry out Your command, seeking Your pleasure, not giving up on his footing, nor being dissuaded from resolve, guarding To Your covenant, I will continue to carry out Your command, until He gives me a cover for my heart. The blessings of God connect to God and His causes, and You guide the hearts, after the battles of temptations and sins and the paths of the eminent people’s clarifiers. To the circles of judgements, for He is Your Trustee, the Trustworthy, and Your witness on the Day of Judgment, and Your Resurrection as a mercy to the worlds. O God, make clear Make room for him with You, and give him, after His satisfaction, the satisfaction of obtaining Your reward which is due, and Your greatest reward is that which is caused, O God. Fulfill your promise to him by sending him a mission. Acceptance of intercession. The just witness, satisfactory to the article, one with a just logic and an orator. A chapter, a proof, and a great proof. Oh God, make us obedient listeners, loyal friends, and companions. Oh God, grant him our peace, and return his peace to us."
"30135","(30135) Ubaidah bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Muhammad al-Basri, on the authority of a man called Salim, who said: He was one of Prayers for Ali: Oh God, make me among those whose deeds You are pleased with, whose hopes are shortened, whose life is prolonged, and which you revive after death. You are good and you have provided, O God. I ask you for a blessing that will never run out, a joy that will never turn away, and the companionship of your Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s peace and blessings be upon him and Abraham, in the highest heaven of eternity. Oh God, grant me compassion, and fill my heart with reverence for him, and shed tears for him. My eyes, and my skin shivers and my side shivers, and I find benefit in my heart. Oh God, purify my heart of hypocrisy. And my chest is from deceit, and my deeds are from hypocrisy, and my eyes are from treachery, and my tongue is from lies, and bless me in my hearing. And my heart, and accept my repentance. Indeed, You are the Forgiving, the Most Merciful. O God, I seek refuge in Your honorable face, for which the seven heavens shine. And through him the darknesses were revealed and the affairs of the ancients and the lasts were made right for him, lest Your wrath descend upon me, or Your wrath descend upon me, or I follow my desires other than guidance from You, or I say to those who disbelieve {These are better guided than those who believe in a way} O God, be Be kind to me, compassionate and merciful to my need, O God, forgive me, O Forgiver, and have mercy on me, O Most Merciful, and have mercy on me, O Most Merciful. And pardon me, O Forbearing One. O God, grant me increase and diligence in worship, and instruct me in the guidance of the past. Good news, pain and joy, anxiety. O Lord, grant me at the time of death freshness and joy, refreshment for eyes, and comfort. Death! On the Day of Resurrection, it will be a position by which your face will be brightened, your position will be confirmed, your eyes will be pleased with it, and your faith will be revealed with it. And you look at me with your face in a way that I will complete the honor with it in the highest companion in the highest of the two upper towers, for your blessing will be complete. Good deeds, O God, I am weak from the weakness You created me to the weakness of what I become, so whatever You want, not whatever We want, so He willed for me to be upright."
"30136","(30136) Affan told us, Shu’abi told us, Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir told me, he said: I heard Raba’i bin Kharash, on the authority of Ali, He said: There are no words more beloved to God than a servant saying: O God, there is no god but You, O God, I worship no one but You, O God, there is no god but You. I associate something with You. O God, I have wronged myself, so forgive me my sins. No one forgives sins except You."
"30137","(30137) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad and Al-Alamimah, saying: Abdullah said: Indeed, in the Book of Allah You have given me that whenever a sin befalls a servant, he recites them, then asks God for forgiveness, unless He forgives him. themselves, until the end of the verse, and “whoever does evil or wrongs himself”"
"30138","(30138) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: It was one of Abdullah’s supplications, “May God reconcile matters between us.” Guide us to the paths of Islam and bring us out of darkness into light, and turn away from us immoral acts, both apparent and hidden, and bless us. In our hearing, and in our sight, and in our hearts, and in our wives, and in our offspring, and turn to us and to them. Indeed, You are the Forgiving, the Merciful, and make us For He has bestowed upon you, thankful, praising and declaring it, and completed it upon us."
"30139","(30139) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: Abdullah used to say, Oh God Reconcile matters between us, then he mentioned something like the hadith of Al-A'mash."
"30140","(30140) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mas’udi, on the authority of Awn ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Abi Fakhita, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Zaid, he said: Abdullah said: God Almighty says: Whoever has a covenant with Me should stand up. They said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, So teach us, he said: Say: O God, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the visible. I make a covenant with You in this. The life of this world: If you leave me to do my work, you bring me closer to evil and distance me from good, and I only trust in your mercy. So make it for me a covenant with you that you will fulfill for me until the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, you will not break your promise."
"30141","(30141) Affan narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, Ata bin Al-Sa’ib narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, that Ibn Masoud was When he supplicates for his companions, he says: O God, guide us, and make it easy for us to be guided, O God, make easy for us easy and avoid hardship, and make us O God, grant us good health and happiness, and clothe us with fine silk and silk, and adorn us with bracelets to the God of Truth. O God, make us thankful. We praise Your grace, saying, “And repent to us. Indeed, You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.”"
"30142","(30142) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi’s answer, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, who said: Abdullah said, “The one who loves to speak to God is The servant says, “O God, I am an accustomed to blessings and I am an accustomed to sin, so forgive me. No one can forgive sins except You.”"
"30143","(30143) Ja’far ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ma’in, who said: Abdullah used to pray and say, “O God, help me.” The ravages of the world, the calamities of eternity, and the calamities of the nights and days, protect me from the evil of what the wrongdoers do on earth, O God. Accompany me on my journey, and leave me behind in my presence, and to you, and love me, and in the eyes of people, and venerate me, and in yourself. So remember me, and in myself for you, humiliate me, and spare me from evil morals, O Most Merciful, to whom do you entrust me, you are my Lord, To someone far away, he frowns upon me, or to someone near, my command has befallen him."
"30144","(30144) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: Whenever Abdullah strove In supplications, he said: O God, I ask you of your bounty which you have bestowed upon me, your good test which you have tested me, and your blessings which You have blessed me to admit me to Paradise. Oh God, admit me to Paradise with your mercy, forgiveness and grace."
"30145","(30145) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud said: No servant has ever supplicated with these supplications except that God has expanded his livelihood upon him. O man of manna, He will not be bestowed upon you. O Possessor of Majesty and Honor, O Possessor of Tallness, there is no god but You, the Supporter of the refugees, the Neighbor of the refugees, and the refuge of the fearful. You wrote me down with you in the Mother of the Book as wretched, so remove from me the name of wretchedness, and make me happy with you, even if you were You wrote me down in the Mother of the Book, depriving me of my livelihood, so erase my deprivation, and deprive me of my livelihood, and establish me with You, happy and prosperous. For good, for you say in your Book {Allah erases whatever He wills and establishes it, and with Him is the mother of the Book}."
"30146","(30146) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said, Abdullah was asked: What are the supplications? What you prayed for last night. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to you: Ask and it will be given to you. He said: I said, O God, I ask of you. A faith that does not waver, a bliss that never ends, and the accompaniment of your Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the highest level of Paradise. Eternal Paradise"
"30147","(30147) Hushaym told us, Husayn told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Yaqzan, Husayn bin Yazid Al-Thaalabi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, that he used to say: When he finished praying: O God, I ask you for the reasons for your mercy and the confirmation of your forgiveness. And I ask You for the spoils of all righteousness and safety from all sin. Oh God, I ask You to win the Garden and protection from the Fire. Oh God, do not leave a sin except that You forgive it, nor leave a worry except that You relieve it, nor leave a need except that You fulfill it."
"30148","(30148) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, He was praying, O God, clothe us with the garb of piety, make us adhere to the word of piety, make us among the possessors of the end, and make us a nation. When You are satisfied, and let us enter the Garden of refuge, and make us among those who are righteous and pious, and believe in good deeds, and forbid the soul from desire, And make us among those whom You facilitate ease and avoid hardship, and make us among those who remember so that remembrance benefits him. O God, make Our efforts will be thanked, and our sins will be forgiven, grant us good fortune and joy, clothe us with fine fabric and silk, and make for us bracelets of gold. And pearls and silk."
"30149","(30149) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he said: O God, forgive us and have mercy on us. And protect us, guide us, and provide for us. He said: Then they said to him: If only you would give us more. He said: I seek refuge in God lest I be among those who wander."
"30150","(30150) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Ammarah bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Yahya bin Rashid, He said: We performed Hajj, and when we had finished our pilgrimage, we said: If only we had come to Ibn Umar and he spoke to us, then he came to us and he came out to us and sat between us, and he remained silent. So that we might ask him, we remained silent so that he might speak to us, but when the silence was prolonged, he said: What is the matter with you that you do not speak? Do you not say: Glory be to God and praise be to God? There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except in Allah. The good deed is multiplied ten times to seven hundred times. If you do more good, God will increase you."
"30151","(30151) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar used to say: Oh God, no Take away faith from me just as you gave it to me."
"30152","(30152) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Barda, on the authority of his father, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: My Lord With what You have bestowed upon me, I will never be a supporter of criminals. So when he prayed, he said: I have not prayed a prayer except that I hope that it will be As an expiation for what he said to her while he was bowing."
"30153","(30153) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Musa, that he used to say about His supplication: Oh God, I ask you of all the good that I should ask of you, and I seek refuge in you from all of the evil. I should seek refuge in you from it."
"30154","(30154) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: He used to say: Oh God, I ask you by the light of your face with which the heavens and the earth shine. That you place me in your protection, your protection, your neighbourhood, and under your shelter."
"30155","(30155) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Hajaj Al-Asadi said: I heard a sheikh walking around behind the house and saying: Oh God, protect me from my self-indulgence, but I did not know who he was. When he left, I followed him and asked about him. They said: Abdul Rahman bin Awf."
"30156","(30156) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Thamamah bin Hazn, who said, I heard a sheikh saying: O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of He mixes with others. He said: I said: Who is this sheikh? He said: Abu Darda’."
"30157","(30157) They narrated[corrupt] Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Urwah ibn Amir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about And he said: It is the most correct omen, and do not turn away a Muslim. If you see any bird that you dislike, then say: Oh God, no. He brings good deeds except You, and does not remove evil deeds except You, and there is no power nor strength except in Allah."
"30158","(30158) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Urwa bin Amir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked Peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the authority of the bird, then he mentioned something like the hadith of Abu Muawiyah, except that he said: There is no power nor strength except by crying."
"30159","(30159) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, who said: Ka’b said to Abdullah bin Amr: Do you fly? He said: Yes. He said: So what do you say? He said: I say: Oh God, there is no bird but Your bird, and there is no good except Your goodness, and there is no Lord other than You. He said: You. The most learned Arabs."
"30160","(30160) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The vision is from God, and the dream is from Satan, so if one of you sees something he hates, Let him vent his anger and seek refuge from its evil, for it will not harm him. (Bukhari 5747, Muslim 1772)"
"30161","(30161) Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If one of you sees a vision and hates it, then let him spit on his left side three times. And let him seek refuge in God from Satan three times, and turn away from the side he used to be upon. (Muslim 1772 and Abu Dawud 4983)"
"30162","(30162) Zayd ibn Harun told us, Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Nakha’i, he said: Whenever one of them saw In a dream he disliked, he said: I seek refuge with what the angels of God and His Messenger have sought refuge with from the evil of what I saw in my dream. Something happens to me that I hate in this world and the hereafter."
"30163","(30163) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Abd al-Malik bin Abi Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ali, a man from Banu Kael, he said: Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari addressed us and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us one day and said: O people, beware of this polytheism, for it is more hidden than the crawling of an ant. So whoever wanted to say said: How can we beware of it when it is Is it more hidden than the crawl of an ant, O Messenger of God? He said, “Say: O God, we seek refuge in You from associating anything with You that we know, and we seek Your forgiveness for what we do not know.”\n(Bukhari 509. Ahmed 403)"
"30164","(30164) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Al-Mughirah bin Mu’aqib, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh God, I take A promise that you will fulfill to me on the Day of Resurrection. You will not break your promise, for I am only a human being. Which of the Muslims have you harmed? If she curses you, or says, I hit you, or insults you, then make it a prayer for him, and make it a purification for him, and an offering by which you may draw near. See you on the Day of Resurrection (Ahmad 449, Abu Ali 1257)"
"30165","(30165) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Omar ibn Qays, on the authority of Amr ibn Abi Qurayh, on the authority of Salman, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I am from the descendants of Adam, so whichever servant of your nation I curse, I curse, or I curse, I curse. Other than its being, so make it a blessing upon him. (Bukhari 234, Abu Dawud 4626)"
"30166","(30166) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: O God, whichever believer I curse, or inflict upon him, or flog him, make it for him purity and reward. (Muslim 2008, Ahmed 391)"
"30167","(30167) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Oh God, it is only good news, so whichever man among the Muslims you curse, curse, or flog, make him Pure and merciful. (Muslim 2007, Ahmed 390)"
"30168","(30168) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Similar to it, except that he said: purification and reward. (Muslim 2007, Dharmi 2766)"
"30169","(30169) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: He asked permission to enter the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon two men, and he treated them harshly and reviled them. She said: I said: O Messenger of God, whoever does good to you will not do it. These are better than you. He said: Did you not know what you promised your Lord? She said to him: What did you promise your Lord? He said: I said: O God, whichever believer you have insulted, cursed, or lashed, grant him forgiveness and recovery, and so on. And so on\n(Muslim 2007, Ahmed 45)"
"30170","(30170) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of some of his sheikhs, he said: When the matter came to him, he He marveled at him. He said: Praise be to God, the Benefactor and Favorite, by whose grace good deeds are completed, and when the matter comes to him from what he dislikes, He said: Praise be to God in every situation. (Ibn Majah 3803)"
"30171","(30171) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, who said: God is ashamed to His servant extends his hand to Him, asks Him for anything good, and He returns them both disappointed. (Abu Dawud 1483. Tirmidhi 3556)"
"30172","(30172) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aghar, Abu Muslim, who testified to Abu Hurairah. And Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, they said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God gives until a third of night, then He descends to the lowest heaven and says: Is there anyone who seeks forgiveness? Is there anyone who repents? Is there any need? Is there anyone who asks? Until dawn breaks. (Bukhari 6321, Muslim 523)"
"30173","(30173) Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanam, on the authority of Abu Dhar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God says: O My servants, all of you are guilty except those whom I have pardoned. So ask forgiveness from Me and I will forgive you, and whoever knows that I am capable of forgiving him, I will forgive him, and I do not care, O My servants. All of you are lost except those whom I have guided, so seek guidance from Me and I will guide you. O My servants, all of you are poor except those whom I have enriched. So ask of Me and I will give you.\n(Tirmidhi 2495. Ahmad 154)"
"30174","(30174) Yahya bin Ali told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, who said: Abdullah bin Rawahih said: Oh God, I ask you for comfort that does not turn back and a blessing that does not run out."
"30175","(30175) Ubaidah bin Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, who said: Abdullah bin Rawahih said: Oh God, I ask you for comfort from an eye that will not turn back, and for bliss that will never run out. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He is not one of these two. Something in this world."
"30176","(30176) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace When he finished his food, peace be upon him, he said: Praise be to God, who has been gracious to us and guided us, and praise be to God, who has satisfied us. And He made us clear, and every affliction is good, or good, We made away with it. (Nasa’i 10133. Ibn Hibban 5219)"
"30177","(30177) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Riyah ibn Ubaidah, the client of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate food, he would say: Praise be to God, who has fed us, given us drink, and made us Muslims."
"30178","(30178) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, who said: When Salman Ta’am, he said: Praise be to God who has provided us with sufficient provisions and made sustenance abundant for us."
"30179","(30179) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abi Sa’id, who said: When Abu Sa’id was appointed to Food. He said: Praise be to God who fed us, gave us drink, and made us Muslims."
"30180","(30180) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu al-Ward, on the authority of Ibn Abad, or Ibn Ma`abad, He said, Ali said: Do you know what the right of food is? He said: I said: What is your right? He said: You say: In the name of God, O God, bless us with what You have provided for us. He said: Do you know what he thanked him for? I said: What is his gratitude? He said: You say: Praise be to God who has fed us and given us drink."
"30181","(30181) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Abi al-Najjoud, on the authority of Dhakwan Abi Salih, on the authority of Aisha, She was presented with food and she said: Serve it, so they said: What is edamame? She said: Thank God for it when you have finished."
"30182","(30182) Muhammad bin Bishr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zaydah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Barda, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Indeed, God is pleased with the servant if he eats food.” Then he praises Him for it, or he drinks something and praises Him for it."
"30183","(30183) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, Bishr bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abdullah, on the authority of Atris bin Arqoub, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever says when his food is put out: In the name of God, is the best of names on earth. And in the heavens there is no disease that is harmed by His name. O God, make therein a blessing, well-being, and a cure, so that food will not harm it, whatever it is."
"30184","(30184) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father would not be brought food or drink, not even medicines. So he drinks it, or tastes it, until he says: Praise be to God who has guided us, fed us, given us drink, and bestowed blessings upon us. God is the Greatest. O God, grant us your blessings with all evil, so we spend mornings and evenings with all goodness. We ask you for its completeness and thanks, there is no good. There is no god but Allah, there is no god but Allah, as He wills. God, there is no strength except with God, O God, bless for us what You have provided for us and protect us from the torment of the Fire."
"30185","(30185) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Urwa, that when he put the food in, he would say: Glory be to You. You have done us well. Glory be to You, how well you have given us. Our Lord and the Lord of our forefathers. Then He calls Allah and places His hand."
"30186","(30186) Jarir bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Tamim bin Salama, he said: It was narrated that the man He mentioned the name of God over his food and praised Him for its afterlife. He was not asked about the blessings of that food."
"30187","(30187) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: He was asked: Was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Does he raise his hand? He said: Yes, the people complained to him that Friday and said: O Messenger of God, the rain has failed, the land has become barren, and wealth has perished. He said: Then he raised his hands until I saw the whites of his armpits, and there were no clouds in the sky, so we did not pray until the strong young man The one who is near the house has the task of returning to his house. He said: So a group of people came upon us. He said, so they said, O Messenger of God, the houses were destroyed and he was detained. Al-Rukban, he said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, smiled at the speed of Malālī, the son of Adam, and said: Oh God, protect us, not against us. He said, so the sky became clear."
"30188","(30188) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yassar, on the authority of Hudhayf, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Do not say: What God willed and so-and-so willed, but say: What God willed, then so-and-so willed."
"30189","(30189) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, heard a man say: “Whatever God wills, and so-and-so wills,” so he said: You have made me a justifier for God. Say: “Whatever God wills.”"
"30190","(30190) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim bin Tarfa al-Tai’i, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim said that a man addressed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: He who obeys God and His Messenger has attained sound judgment. And whoever disobeys them has gone astray, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What a miserable preacher you are. Say: And whoever disobeys God And His Messenger. (Muslim 594. Abu Dawud 1092)"
"30191","(30191) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A man proposed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Whoever obeys God and His Messenger has guided him, and whoever disobeys them has gone astray. He said: Then the face of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, changed. He, peace and blessings be upon him, disapproved of that, and he said: Ibrahim: So they disliked that he should say: And who disobeys them? But he said: Who? Disobey Allah and His Messenger."
"30192","(30192) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever supplicates against those who wronged him, has triumphed. (Tirmidhi 3552, Abu Ali 4437)"
"30193","(30193) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, who said: A thief stole her, so she prayed. On him, and he said: To her, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Do not curse him on his behalf. (Abu Dawud 1492; Ahmed 136)"
"30194","(30194) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Uthman bin Abdullah bin Muhib, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Words that if a servant said them, an angel placed them in his wings, then he ascended with them and did not pass by them. A group of angels, except that they send blessings upon us and upon those who speak them, until they are placed in the hands of the Most Gracious: Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and no There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah, and Glory be to Allah, may Allah protect Him from evil. (Tabarani 6741)"
"30195","(30195) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: Ibrahim met Taqiyya, and Mujahid, and they said: A Bedouin came to The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, complained to him of hunger. He said: So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered his homes, then He went out and said: I did not find anything for you in the houses of the family of Muhammad. He said: While he was like that, a prayer came to him. The other said: A bowl of porridge came to him and was placed in the hands of a Bedouin. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: He fed, he said: Then he ate, and he said: O Messenger of God, what has befallen me has befallen me, and God has blessed me at your hands. Have you seen that? It befell me while I was not with you, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Say: Oh God, I ask you of Your bounty. And your mercy, for no one has control over them except you, for God is the one who has provided for you. (Tabarani 10379)"
"30196","(30196) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, Wael bin Dawud narrated to us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan Al-Basri speaking, he said: While a man He saw in a dream that a herald was calling in the heavens, “O people, take the weapons of your fear.” So the people baptized and took the weapons until A man comes, and he does not have a staff. Then a herald calls from the heavens: This is not a weapon. He has terrified you. Then a man from the people of the earth said: What is a weapon? We were terrified, so he said: Glory be to God, praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is greatest."
"30197","(30197) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Surad, that two men touched each other and his anger intensified. One of them, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I know a word that if he said it, his anger would go away: I seek refuge in God from Satan, the accursed. (Muslim 2015, Nasa’i 10224)"
"30198","(30198) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, who said: Two men insulted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and one of them became so angry that It seemed to me that his nose was torn, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I would know a word if he said it like this. Angry people, their wrath has gone: I seek refuge in God from Satan."
"30199","(30199) Qarad Abu Nuh narrated to us, Ikrimah bin Ammar narrated to us, Simak Al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abu Zumail said, Ibn Abbas, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab told me, he said: On the day of Badr, he faced the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and then He extended his hand and then said: O God, fulfill what you promised me, O God, give me what you promised me, O God, if this is yours, The gangs are among the people of Islam, and they will never be worshiped on earth. He continued to seek help from his Lord and pray until his cloak fell off. Then God Almighty revealed: {When you sought help from your Lord, and He responded to you. Indeed, I will assist you with a thousand of the angels in succession}"
"30200","(30200) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: It was one of the supplications of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hunayn: Oh God, if You will, You will not be worshiped after today. (Muslim 1363. Ahmad 121)"
"30201","(30201) Wakī’ narrated to us, Imran bin Hudayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was When he meets the enemy, he says: Oh God, you are my support and my helper, with you I strive, with you I reach out, and with you I fight.\n(Abu Dawud 2425. Tirmidhi 3584)"
"30202","(30202) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa saying: The Messenger of God called May God’s blessings and peace be upon the parties, and he said: O God, who sent down the Book, who is quick to judge, who defeats the parties, defeat them. And he shook them. (Bukhari 6392 and Muslim 1363)"
"30203","(30203) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Atiya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, regarding the Almighty’s saying: {So when he is dug into the fountain} He said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: How was he blessed when the owner of the horn had reached the horn and the bend of his forehead was listening when It was commanded, and it was blown, and the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: How should we say? He said: Say: {Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs} In Allah we put our trust. (Tabarani 12670)"
"30204","(30204) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: When Abraham was thrown Peace be upon him, in Hell, he said: Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs."
"30205","(30205) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, who said: Trusting in God is the combination of faith."
"30206","(30206) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Ask God for the means for me. No believer in this world will ask for it except that it will be his. A witness or an intercessor on the Day of Resurrection. (Bukhari 614, Abu Dawud 530)"
"30207","(30207) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas, that he came to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, Satan came between my prayer and my recitation, so he said: That is the devil, it is said Laha: Hanzab, so when you feel it, spit on your left hand three times and seek refuge in Allah from its evil."
"30208","(30208) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Khutmi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Khatmiy, he used to say: Oh God, grant me your love and the love of those whose love will benefit me with you. O God, grant me what I love and make it a strength for me in what You love, and whatever You remove from me of what I love, make it an empty space for me. You love"
"30209","(30209) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There was a man among us called Hammam bin Al-Harith. He did not sleep unless he was sitting in his mosque during his prayers, and he used to say: O God, heal me from sleep with ease and provide for me. Attentively in your obedience."
"30210","(30210) Muhammad bin Bishr and Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, who said: Ziyad bin Alaqah narrated to us, on the authority of his paternal uncle Qutbah. Ibn Malik, he used to say, “O God, spare me from evil deeds, morals, desires, and medicines.”"
"30211","(30211) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Haytham, on the authority of Talhah, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He used to seek refuge from the lion. And blackness and the spirit of mischief."
"30212","(30212) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Talha Al-Yami, on the authority of Abu Idris, a man from the people of Yemen said: He used to say: O God, make my sight a lesson, my silence a contemplation, and my reason a remembrance."
"30213","(30213) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, that he said in his supplication: Oh God! I ask you to do good things, to abandon evil deeds, and to love the poor, and to turn to me in repentance. And if You intend for Your servants to undergo temptation, then give me something other than Intrigued."
"30214","(30214) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Musa bin Muslim al-Tahan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Sabit, he said: There was a group of people. They were close together. He said: They lost one of them for a few days, then he came to them and said: Where have you been? He said: I was in debt, so he said: Oh God, I have made these supplications: Oh God, the reliever of every distress, the reliever of every worry, and the remover of every grief. And He who responds to the prayers of those in distress is Most Merciful and Most Merciful to this world and the Hereafter. You are Most Merciful to me, so have mercy on me, O Most Merciful, Most Merciful. You will free me from the mercy of anyone else except you."
"30215","(30215) Ubaydah bin Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: We entered upon Rabi’ bin Khathim, and he called With these supplications: O God, all praise is due to You, and in Your hand is all goodness, and to You the whole matter returns, and you are the Lord of it. All of creation, we ask you for all good, and we seek refuge in you from all evil."
"30216","(30216) Zayd bin Harun told us, Ali bin Masadhi told us, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Rumi, he said: We were with Anas. Ibn Malik, and a man said to him: O Abu Hamza, your brothers love that you pray for them, so he said: O God, forgive us. And have mercy on us and give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and protect us from the torment of the Fire. They said: Give us more, O Abu Hamza. So he sent it back. On them, they said: Give us more, O Abu Hamza. He said: God is sufficient for us, O Abu so-and-so. If we give it, then we have given it better. This world and the hereafter."
"30217","(30217) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Tabi’a, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Were it not for the words I say to them: The Jews have made me howl with the braying donkeys and howl with the howling dogs. I seek refuge in Your Generous Face. And in your great name and with your perfect words that no righteous person can pass, nor the ungodly, who does not fear his neighbor from any evil. He descends from the heavens, and from what ascends therein, and from the evil of what He created, He removed and purified."
"30218","(30218) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Aoun, who said: Asma’ bint Abi Bakr said: Whoever read after So, open the Book, and (Say: He is Allah, One) and (Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of creation) and (Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind) Preserve what is between him and between The other Friday."
"30219","(30219) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Muslim, that he used to say At the end of his saying: May God connect your brothers with faith, bring you close with His mercy, strengthen your dignity with His benevolence, and illuminate With the Qur’an your breasts."
"30220","(30220) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar, Sulaiman bin Hayyan, narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Uqba bin Aamer said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No one asks, nor does anyone seek refuge, the like of them. Al-Mu'awwidhatayn. (Abu Dawud 1458, Darami 3440)"
"30221","(30221) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, that Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Abi Talib used to say when the sun rose: The one who hears hears, praise be to God Almighty. He has no partner. To Him belongs the kingdom and to Him. Praise be to Him, and He has power over all things. The one who hears hears, with the greatest praise of God. He has no partner. To Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is He is powerful over all things, the listener hears, praise be to God the Most Glorious, there is no partner to Him. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is over all things. Almighty, he follows this example."
"30222","(30222) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was If he wanted to go on a journey, peace be upon him, he would say: O God, you are the companion in the journey and the successor in the family. O God, I seek refuge in Him. You are free from darkness during travel, and depression during the ups and downs, O God, capture the land for us and make travel easy for us. (Ahmed 2998, Ibn Hibban 2716)"
"30223","(30223) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sargis, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when he sets out as a traveler, he returns from the hardships of travel, the gloom of the downturn, and the bitterness after the darkness, and from the supplication of the oppressed. It is a bad outlook regarding family and wealth. (Muslim 979. Ahmad 83)"
"30224","(30224) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A man wanted On a journey, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Advise me. He said: I advise you to fear God and exalt God above all honour. (Tirmidhi 3445, Ahmad 443)"
"30225","(30225) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: Aoun bin Abdullah narrated to me that a man had intercourse with Ibn Masoud, and he said: I want to travel, so give me advice. He said: When you go, say: In the name of God, God is sufficient for me, and I put my trust in God. You said: In the name of God, the angel said: I have been guided, and when you said: God is sufficient for me, the angel said, I have been preserved, and when you said: I trust in God, The king said: It is enough."
"30226","(30226) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to say in travel: O God, convey the report. Good is Your forgiveness and satisfaction. In Your hand is good. Indeed, You are capable of all things. Oh God, You are the companion on the journey. And the successor to the family. Oh God, expand the earth for us and make travel easy for us. Oh God, we seek refuge in You from the hardships and depression of travel. Upside down and bad outlook regarding one’s family and wealth."
"30227","(30227) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I traveled with Ibn Umar, and when it was dawn, he called out: The listener heard, praise be to God, His grace, and His good affliction with us. O God, be our companion, and bestow upon us three. O God, we seek refuge in you from Hell three times."
"30228","(30228) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace When he wanted to return, meaning from the journey, he would say: Repentant, worshiping our Lord, praising. And when he came to his family, he would say: Repent, repent. Our Lord has a helper who never leaves us."
"30229","(30229) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace When he, peace and blessings of God be upon him, finished a journey, he said: “We are repentant, we are worshipers of our Lord, we are thankful.” (Ahmad 3000, Tayalisi 716)"
"30230","(30230) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Ubaid Allah bin Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when he returned from the army, or the company, or Hajj, or Umrah, he would say, “Whenever I fulfill Then, he said “Allahu Akbar” three times, then said: There is no god but Allah alone. His promise has been fulfilled. We repent, worship our Lord, and give thanks. (Bukhari 1797, Muslim 980)"
"30231","(30231) Abu Osama narrated to us, Ubaid Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He said hello, then he mentioned something similar to it, or something similar."
"30232","(30232) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Saeed bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, that he was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he was at the beginning of the desert, or in the heat, he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, will repent and worship, if God wills, praising our Lord. (Bukhari 30851 Muslim 980)"
"30233","(30233) Hushaym told us, the common people told us, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, he said: When they closed their doors, they would say: “I will return.” God willing, you will repent and give thanks to our Lord."
"30234","(30234) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: Makhoul narrated to us that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. When he entered Mecca, the jinn attacked him with evil and threw evil at him. Gabriel said: “Seek refuge, O Muhammad.” So seek refuge with them. So turn away from it. I seek refuge in the perfect words of God, which neither the righteous nor the immoral can pass, from the evil of what descends from the heavens. And from the evil of what is spread in the earth, and from what comes out of it, and from the evil of the night and the day, and from every one who knocks. Fine, O Most Merciful."
"30235","(30235) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, that Al-Walid bin Al-Walid bin Al-Mughirah Al-Makhzoumi complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the story of a person he found And he said to him: When you come to your bed, say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from His wrath and punishment, and from the evil of His servants, and from The promptings of the devils and that they should come. By the One in whose hand is my soul, nothing will harm you until morning."
"30236","(30236) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zayed, on the authority of Musab, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’adah, He said: Khalid bin Al-Walid used to get terrified at night until he went out, carrying his sword, and he was afraid that he would harm someone. He complained about this to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Gabriel said to me: A demon from the jinn is plotting against you. So say, “I seek refuge in the perfect words of God, which neither the righteous nor the immoral can pass over, from the evil of what descends from the heavens and what passes.” Therein, and from the evil of what He has spread in the earth, and of what comes out of it, and the evil of the temptations of the night and the day, and every one who knocks except one who knocks. Fine, O Most Merciful. Then Khaled said to them, and that went away from him."
"30237","(30237) Abd bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you wakes from his sleep, let him say: In the name of God, I seek refuge in the words of God. Complete from His wrath and the evil of His punishment and the evil of His servants and from the evil of the devils, and what they attend."
"30238","(30238) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, Abu Al-Tayyah narrated to us, he said: A man asked Abdullah bin Khanbash: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do when the devils attacked him? He said: The devils came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the valleys, and descended upon him from the mountains, and they A devil who had a torch of fire with which he wanted to burn the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he was terrified of them, Ja’far said. I think it is. He said: He started to delay. He said: Gabriel came to him and said: O Muhammad, say. He said: What should I say? He said: Say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God, which neither the righteous nor the immoral can pass over, from the evil of what He created, procreated, and acquitted of, and from the evil of what He descends from the heavens, and from the evil of what He ascends therein, and from the evil of what He scatters on the earth, and from the evil of what emerges from it, and from the evil of the temptations of the night. And the Fire, and from the evil of every Tariq except one who knocks with goodness, O Most Merciful. He said: Then the fire of Satan was extinguished. He said: And he defeated them. God"
"30239","(30239) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, who said: Khalid bin The newborn had insomnia, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him, “Shall I not teach you words that if you say them, you will sleep, O God, Lord of the heavens, and what they shade?” Lord of the earths, and what they have diminished, and Lord of the devils, and what they have led astray, be my neighbor from the evil of all of your creation, lest it be too much for me. None of them, or he desires, honor your neighbor, and there is no god but you. (Tirmidhi 3523. Tabarani 984)"
"30240","(30240) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man from the people of Syria, on the authority of Makhoul, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was If he sees the House, he says: O God, increase this House in honor, reverence, and majesty, and increase those who perform Hajj or Umrah in it. Honor, glorification, honor and righteousness. (Bayhaqi 73)"
"30241","(30241) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, When he entered the Kaaba Mosque and looked at the House, he would say: O God, you are peace and from you is peace, so grant us peace, our Lord, with peace."
"30242","(30242) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, he said: The first time you enter a place, you end up there. Al-Hijr, so thank God for His good facilitation and communication."
"30243","(30243) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sa’id, on the authority of his father, that when Omar entered the house, he would say: Oh God, you are peace and from you is peace, so grant us peace, our Lord."
"30244","(30244) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Wahhab bin Wahhab, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar, that He used to say when he touched it, meaning the stone: I believed in God and disbelieved in the tyrant."
"30245","(30245) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, he said: It was When he receives the stone, he says: Oh God, in confirmation of Your Book and the Sunnah of Your Prophet."
"30246","(30246) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid al-Muttab, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When you touch the stone, say: There is no god but God. Except Allah, and Allah is the greatest."
"30247","(30247) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It was desirable to It is said when touching the stone: Oh God, in confirmation of Your Book and the Sunnah of Your Prophet."
"30248","(30248) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Yahya bin Ubaid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Al-Sa'ib said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying between the pillar and the stone: {Our Lord, give us in this world... Good, and in the Hereafter, good, and protect us from the torment of the Fire."
"30249","(30249) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: It was one of the supplications of Ibn Abbas who did not He leaves between the pillar and the maqam to say: O God, satisfy me with what You have bestowed upon me, and bless me therein, and grant me all my absences. I am fine"
"30250","(30250) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abu Shu’abi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He used to say at the pillar or stone: {Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire}"
"30251","(30251) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Hurmuz, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: On the Yemeni pillar is a king. He says, Amen, so when you pass by him, say: Oh God, our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire."
"30252","(30252) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He started with As-Safa and proceeded upon it until he saw the House and declared the Oneness and Greatness of God, and said: There is no god but God alone. Your partner, to Him belongs the dominion, to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. There is no god but Allah alone. He has fulfilled His promise and given victory. He worshiped and defeated Al-Ahzab alone, then he supplicated in between and said: Like this three times, then he came to Al-Marwah and did it upon Ali. Al-Marwah as he did on Al-Safa."
"30253","(30253) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Wahb ibn al-Ajda’, he said I heard Omar saying: When you stand on Safa, say “Allahu Akbar” seven times, and between each two “Allahu Akbar” you should say, “Praise be to God and praise be to Him.” And may God’s blessings be upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and a supplication for yourself, and the like of the Marwa."
"30254","(30254) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Wahhab bin Al-Ajda’ that he heard Omar say: He begins with As-Safa and faces towards the Bayt, then he says “Allahu Akbar” seven times, and between each two “Allahu Akbar” says “Praise be to God.” And blessings be upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a question for yourself, and the narration is like that."
"30255","(30255) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when he ascended Safa He faced the verse, then said “Allahu Akbar” three times, then said: There is no god but Allah alone, without any partner. To Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is upon Him. He has power over all things. He raises his voice with it, then he supplicates a little, then he does that in the narration until he does it. This is done seven times, and the takbeer is twenty-one times. It has hardly finished until it becomes difficult for us and we Youth"
"30256","(30256) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Asbagh bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, because he used to say: A man will stand on Safa and al-Marwah as much as he recites a surah of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"30257","(30257) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: Al-Hakam said to Ibrahim, I saw Abu Bakr ibn Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Harith is based on Al-Safa as much as a man recites twenty and a hundred verses, and he said: Indeed, he is a jurist."
"30258","(30258) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no temporary supplication on Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, so pray for what You want"
"30259","(30259) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I did not hear that there are supplications upon al-Safa and al-Marwah. Temporarily"
"30260","(30260) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: There is no temporary supplication in it, so pray for whatever you want and ask for whatever you want. You want"
"30261","(30261) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Muadh ibn al-Ala’, who said: I witnessed Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzoumi saying: I do not know. A temporary supplication upon Al-Safa and Al-Marwah."
"30262","(30262) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, who said: Whenever Omar passed through the valley between Al-Safa And Al-Marwah he seeks in it and says: My Lord, forgive and have mercy, and You are the Most Mighty, the Most Generous."
"30263","(30263) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: When he ran The depths of the valley. He said: My Lord, forgive and have mercy. Indeed, You are the Most Mighty, the Most Generous."
"30264","(30264) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Haytham ibn Hanash, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that He used to say: Lord, forgive and have mercy, and You are the Most Mighty, the Most Generous."
"30265","(30265) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, that his father used to say, “And he strove between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, O God, this is one, if they are completed, God will complete it, and they will complete it."
"30266","(30266) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Yazeed, on the authority of his father, he said: I continued with Abdullah, so he threw seven pebbles, saying “Allahu Akbar” with each pebble, and he moved further into the valley until, when it was empty, he said: Oh God. Make him an accepted Hajj, and his sins forgiven. Then he said: This is how I saw the one to whom Surat Al-Baqarah was revealed to do."
"30267","(30267) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Haytham ibn Hanash, who said: I heard Ibn Umar when he stoned the stones. He says: Oh God, make him an accepted Hajj and a forgiven sin."
"30268","(30268) Abdul-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I said to Abraham: What should I say if I throw a stone? The ember? He said: Say: O Allah, make it an accepted Hajj and a forgiven sin. He said: I said: Should I say it with every pebble? He said: Yes, if you wish."
"30269","(30269) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no temporary supplication required to stop at the two jamarats. So pray for whatever you want."
"30270","(30270) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: Al-Hasan used to say: He supplicates at the pebbles completely, but not It delays something."
"30271","(30271) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I told Ata’ at the burning coal that it is a temporary thing and will not be increased. Ali? He said: No, except the saying of Jabir."
"30272","(30272) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: I multiply your supplication and the supplications of the prophets before me with your knowledge: There is no god but Allah alone, without any partner. To Him belongs the kingdom and to Him. Praise be to Him, and He has power over all things. Oh God, put light in my heart, light in my hearing, and light in my sight. Oh God, explain to me my chest and make my affairs easy for me, and I seek refuge in You from the whisperings of the chest, the distractions of affairs, and the temptations of the grave. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from The worst of what winds at night, the worst of what winds during the day, and the worst of what winds blow."
"30273","(30273) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Nadhar ibn Arabi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Husayn, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: I multiply your supplication and the supplications of the prophets before me with knowledge: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. To Him belongs the kingdom and to Him. Praise is He who gives life and causes death, and He has power over all things."
"30274","(30274) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Abu Shu’ba, who said: I was beside Ibn Umar with his knowledge, and that My knees touch his knees, or my thighs touch his thigh, and I have never heard him say anything more than these words: There is no god but God. Alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is Able to do all things, to the point that He has bestowed from one known to all."
"30275","(30275) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Shattar, who said: I told Ibn Hanafi: What is the best thing we say about our Hajj? He said: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest."
"30276","(30276) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, similar to this."
"30277","(30277) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Asim, who said: I stood with Salim bin Abdullah with his knowledge, see how he does, and he was in remembrance and supplications until he excelled."
"30278","(30278) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Abu Shu`ba, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that it was He says around the verse: There is no god but Allah alone, there is no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is over all things. Almighty"
"30279","(30279) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abi Labiba, on the authority of Sa`d, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The best of hidden remembrance. (Ahmed 172)"
"30280","(30280) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The hidden remembrance that is not The Book of Memorization is multiplied seventy times over any other remembrance."
"30281","(30281) Ibn Fudayl and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: We were with The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on a journey, and he made the people shout “Allahu Akbar,” and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Four people.” On yourselves, for you do not call upon a deaf person, nor one who is absent. You call upon Him, Hearing and Near, and He is with you."
"30282","(30282) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Sadiqah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. He said: When the praying person prays, he talks to his Lord, so let him know what he is talking to, and do not rebel against one another."
"30283","(30283) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: O people, you do not You call a deaf person, not an absent person, meaning raising one’s voice in supplication."
"30284","(30284) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naseeb, who said: I prayed next to Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and when I sat in the second rak’ah and raised my voice in supplication, and he called me out. When she left, I said to him: What did you dislike about me? He said: I thought that God was not close to you."
"30285","(30285) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Mujahid, that he heard a man raising his voice in supplications. He stoned him with pebbles."
"30286","(30286) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Yazid bin Aban, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan that they He hated that the man sitting with him should hear any of the supplications."
"30287","(30287) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They used to strive hard in supplications, and you would only hear a whisper."
"30288","(30288) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah, on the authority of Ibn Abu Dhabab, on the authority of Sahil bin Saad, who said: I have never seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raising his hand in supplications on a pulpit. And no one else, and I saw his hands calling to him like his shoulders."
"30289","(30289) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was not He raises his hands in any supplication except when praying for rain."
"30290","(30290) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim bin Tarfi, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us and said: Why do I see you raising your hands as if they were tails? Horses of the sun, be still in prayer."
"30291","(30291) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Amr bin Al-Ahwas, who said: Abu Hilal told us, on the authority of Abu Barza, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for two men and he raised his hand."
"30292","(30292) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Hayyan bin Umair, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Samurah, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he raised his hands as he prayed during the eclipse."
"30293","(30293) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: Anas was asked: Was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He raised his hands, meaning in supplication, and said: Yes. The people complained to him about the gathering and said: O Messenger of God, the rain has stopped. And the land became barren and the wealth perished. He said: So he raised his hands until I saw the whites of his armpits."
"30294","(30294) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: I saw the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he raises his hands in supplication until the whites of his armpits can be seen. (Muslim 612. Tayalisi 2047)"
"30295","(30295) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar, he said: I saw The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed the edge of his right elbow on his right thigh and circled the thumb and middle finger and raised the band. He recites the thumb and supplicates with it."
"30296","(30296) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Issam bin Qadamah, on the authority of Malik bin Numayr Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting during prayer, placing his right hand on his thigh and pointing with his finger."
"30297","(30297) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of his father, he said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he sat making supplication, he placed his right hand on his right thigh, and his The left thigh is on his left thigh, and he points with his index finger, and he places his thumb on his middle finger, and he delivers His left palm is his knees."
"30298","(30298) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rashid Abi Saad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, he said: It was When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat in prayer, he would place his hand on his thigh and point with his finger in supplication."
"30299","(30299) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hariri, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, received his sight. May God bless him and grant him peace while he was praying with his fingers and said: O Saad, one of them."
"30300","(30300) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Tamimi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is sincerity."
"30301","(30301) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Alqamiya, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Kathir bin Aflah, he said: I prayed, he said: Then when At the end of the Qa'dah, I said thus, and Ibn Aliyah pointed with his finger, and Ibn Umar grabbed this, meaning the left one."
"30302",""
"30303","(30303) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Alqamiya, on the authority of Aisha, who said: God is a string, and He loves the string. He called like this and she pointed with one finger."
"30304","(30304) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he saw a man He called with both of his fingers, but he finished it, and said: With one finger with the right hand."
"30305","(30305) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abi Yahya, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, favors one another, meaning pointing with a finger in supplication."
"30306","(30306) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: You will pray, The best supplication is like this and pointing with your finger."
"30307","(30307) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ma’bad bin Khalid, on the authority of Qays bin Saad, who said: He would not add such-and-such and he pointed with his finger."
"30308","(30308) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man points with his finger during prayer, then it is good. This is monotheism, but he does not point with his two fingers, for it is disliked."
"30309","(30309) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Khaythama, that he used to hold fifty-three ceremonies, And he points with his finger."
"30310","(30310) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, that he said: The supplications are like this and pointed with a finger. One is the oppressor of Satan."
"30311","(30311) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Whenever they saw a person praying with his two fingers They struck one of them and said: There is only one God."
"30312","(30312) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi al-Sha’athai, on the authority of a man from the Ansar who narrated to him, On the authority of his grandfather, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by him while he was praying with his hands and said: “One, for he is one.” (Musnad 669)"
"30313","(30313) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, that his father used to point his finger during supplications, and he did not He moves it."
"30314","Buqi bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr narrated to us, saying:\n(30314) Waki’ ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: Do not stand up. You pray as the Jews do in their churches."
"30315","(30315) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibn al-Asbaani, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, that he saw a man calling He stood up after he left and insulted him or insulted him."
"30316","(30316) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd ibn Abi Lubab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he hated it."
"30317","(30317) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Two innovations: for a man to stand up facing the direction of prayer after he has finished praying, and to perform the prostration of prostration. Secondly, he believes that it is his right to stick his buttocks to the ground before he gets up."
"30318","(30318) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he hated to stand up after her because he imitated the Jews."
"30319","(30319) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Abdullah, that he had heard that a people They remember God standing. He said: Then he came to them and said: What is this terrible thing?"
"30320","(30320) Abbad bin Al-Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Jamil bin Zayd, who said: I saw Ibn Umar entering the house and praying two rak’ahs. Then I went out and left him standing, calling and saying “Allahu Akbar.”"
"30321","(30321) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I said to Mughirah: When Abraham turned away, he was reluctant to stand up. Does the person facing the qiblah raise his hand? He said: Yes."
"30322","(30322) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: I saw Al-Hasan raising his gaze to the heavens in prayer, supplicating while he was Standing"
"30323","(30323) Sharik bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abu Al-Huray’i, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali said: My grandfather taught me some words that I should say in the Qunut of Witr: O God, guide me among those whom You have guided and protect me. Among those whom You have pardoned, and take care of me among those whom you have taken care of, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed, and bless me in what You have given. Indeed, You decree, and do not You will be judged, for he will not be humiliated by you whom you have appointed. Blessed and exalted are you."
"30324","(30324) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Saleh, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of a sheikh nicknamed Abu Muhammad, that Al-Hussein bin Ali He used to say in the Qunut of Witr: O God, you see, but you do not see, and you are in the highest view, and to you is the return, and indeed to you is The last and the first, O God, we seek refuge in You from being humiliated and disgraced."
"30325","(30325) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Harun bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He used to say in Qunut al-Witr: To You is praise, filling the seven heavens, filling the two earths with seven, and filling what is between them. One more thing, the people of praise and glory are the most deserving of what the servant said, “We are all your servants”: there is no objection to what you have given, and there is no giver of what you have withheld. Seriousness is of no use to someone who is serious than you."
"30326","(30326) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, he said: Ibn Masoud taught us to say In Qunoot, meaning in the Witr prayer: O God, we seek Your help and seek Your forgiveness and praise You for goodness, and we do not disbelieve in You and renounce And we abandon those who deceive you. Oh God, we worship you, and to you we pray and prostrate, and to you we seek and gloat, and we hope for your mercy and we fear. Your punishment is attached to the disbelievers."
"30327","(30327) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Say in the Qunut of Witr: Oh God. We seek your help and seek your forgiveness."
"30328","(30328) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he said: There is nothing in Qunut al-Witr. Temporary, but it is a supplication and seeking forgiveness."
"30329","(30329) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith. Ibn Hisham, on the authority of Ali, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say at the end of his Witr prayer: O God, I seek refuge in Your satisfaction from Your anger, and I seek refuge in You from your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You, I cannot praise You as You have praised Me. yourself"
"30330","(30330) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of His father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray Witr and say at the end of his prayer when he sat: Glory be to the King, the Holy, three times, extending With his voice in the afterlife."
"30331","(30331) Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaidah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of Ubayyah, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say about His last prayer: Glory be to the Holy King, three times."
"30332","(30332) Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: I prayed. Omar ibn al-Khattab came after lunch and said in his voice: O God, we seek Your help, we seek Your forgiveness, and we praise You for what is good. We disbelieve in you, and we renounce and abandon those who disbelieve in you. O God, to You we worship, and to You we pray and prostrate, and to You we seek and glorify. We hope for Your mercy and fear Your punishment. Indeed, Your punishment is attached to the disbelievers."
"30333","(30333) Hushaym told us, Husayn told us, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father He said: He had prayed behind Omar, so he did the same."
"30334","(30334) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, he said: I prayed the morning prayer one day and Uthman bin Ziyad, he said: So I performed the Qunoot in the morning prayer. He said: When I finished my prayer, he said to me: What did you say in your Qunoot? So I said: I mentioned these words: O God, we seek Your help and seek Your forgiveness and praise You for goodness, and we do not disbelieve in You, and we remove And we abandon those who deceive you. Oh God, we worship you, and to you we pray and prostrate, and to you we seek and prostrate, and we hope for your mercy. And we fear Your torment seriously. Indeed, Your torment is attached to the disbelievers. He said: Othman said to me: This is what Omar bin Al-Khattab and Othman used to do. Ibn Affan."
"30335","(30335) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Suwayd al-Kaili, At dawn, Ali recited these two surahs: O God, we seek Your help and seek Your forgiveness, and we praise You with goodness. We disbelieve in you, and we renounce and abandon those who disbelieve in you. O God, we worship you, and to you we pray and prostrate, and to you we seek and glorify. We hope for Your mercy and fear Your punishment. Indeed, Your punishment is attached to the disbelievers."
"30336","(30336) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ja’far bin Burqan narrated to us, on the authority of Maimoon bin Mihran, he said regarding Qara’a, Ubayy bin Ka’b : O God, we seek Your help and seek Your forgiveness and praise You with goodness, and we do not disbelieve in You, and we cast off and leave behind those who deceive You. Oh God, it is to you that we worship, and to you we pray and prostrate, and to you we seek and descend, and we hope for your mercy and fear your torment. Indeed, your torment attached to the unbelievers."
"30337","(30337) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: I heard Omar say Qunoot. At dawn: O God, we seek your help, we believe in you, we trust in you, we praise you for goodness, and we do not disbelieve in you, O God. You are the one we worship, and to you we pray and prostrate, and to you we seek and prostrate, we hope for your mercy and fear your torment. Indeed, your torment is with the disbelievers. Addendum: Oh God, punish the disbelief of the People of the Book who turn away from Your path."
"30338","(30338) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Omar bin Kathir bin Aflah, on the authority of Ibn Omar, in Al-Dhaliya. He performs ablution, prays two rak'ahs, recites the tashahid and says: In the name of God, O guide of the astray, and return the stray. Return to me what I stray. By Your glory and authority, for it is from Your grace and grace."
"30339","(30339) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Aban bin Saleh, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Indeed, Allah Your angels write down the leaves of a tree, as well as His creation, so if one of you is afflicted with lameness while on a journey, let him call out: Help me servants. May God have mercy on you. (Bazzar 3128)"
"30340","(30340) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The offspring of every camel is a devil, so when you mount it, say as God has commanded you {Glory be to God who has subjected to us this and what “We were to Him [along with Him].” And be grateful to Him for yourselves, for it is only the Lamb of God."
"30341","(30341) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hamza bin Amr, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Indeed, upon the top of every camel is a devil, so when you mount it, praise it, and mention the name of God, then Do not fall short of your needs. (Ahmad 494, Darami 2467)"
"30342","(30342) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, Ali The offspring of every camel is a devil, so when you ride, remember the name of God and praise it, for it is only the burden of God."
"30343","(30343) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, that Hussein bin Ali saw a man riding an animal and said: {Glory be to Him who has subjected this to us, and we were not to it.} He said, “Is this what you have been commanded to do?” He said: How should I say? He said: Praise be to God who guided me to Islam. Praise be to God who bestowed upon me Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. Praise be to God. He is the One who made me the best of mothers ever given to people. Then you say: {Glory be to Him who has subjected this to us}"
"30344","(30344) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubayd, on the authority of Murā, who said: Abdullah said: Who among you is cowardly on behalf of the enemy? He strives hard, and the night is that he suffers and is afraid of money to spend it, so let him multiply, Glory be to God, and praise be to God, There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest."
"30345","(30345) Shababih told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, on the authority of Muwarriq al-Ijli, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: You are unable to contend with the night, or with the enemy, with the ability to struggle with it, or with the money, with which you are unable to combat it, so increase yourselves, Glory be to God. Praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is greatest, for they are more beloved to me than gold and silver that you have created."
"30346","(30346) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of the common people, that he heard Ibrahim Al-Taymimi say: When he said: Praise be to God And Glory be to God, the angels say: And praise be to Him. So when he says: Glory be to God and praise be to Him, the angels say: May God have mercy on you. So when he says: God is great, the angels say: Great. So when he says: God is great, the angels say: Have mercy on you. God, so when he says: Praise be to God, the angels say: Lord of the worlds, and when he says: Lord of the worlds, the angels say: May God have mercy on you. God"
"30347","(30347) Hussein bin Ali Al-Ju’fi told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ziyad Al-Musaffar, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace, to Abu Bakr: Shall I not guide you to a truth that will fill what is between the heavens and the earth: Glory be to God and praise be to God, and there is no god but Him. God, God is Great, and there is no power nor strength except in God thirty times a day."
"30348","(30348) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abdul Jalil, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Imran, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Take your garden. They said: O Messenger of God, is there an enemy present? He said: No, but from the Fire. We said: You have not saved us from the Fire. He said: Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is the greatest. There is no power nor strength except with God. Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection, they will come as precedents, those that come back, and those that are avoided, and they are {the lasting} Good deeds}"
"30349","(30349) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Waqa’, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: Omar ibn al-Khattab saw a man reciting the tasbih. With him, and Omar said: May God have mercy on him, the only reward for that is to say: Glory be to God, He filled the heavens and filled the earth and filled whatever He willed with anything. After, and he says: Praise be to God, He has filled the heavens and the earth, and He has filled whatever He wills with anything. After, and He says: God is Great, He has filled the heavens and filled The earth and fill it with whatever He wishes after that."
"30350","(30350) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdul-Malik Ibn Misra, who said: Ibn Masoud and Abdullah met Ibn Amr, Ibn Masoud said: Because I say when I go out until I fulfill my need: Glory be to God, praise be to God, and there is no god but God. And God is more beloved to me than to carry a number of horses on me in the path of God. Abdullah bin Amr said: Because Do I say that I am more beloved to you than spending a number of dinars in the path of God Almighty?"
"30351","(30351) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If one of you, when he wanted to visit his family, said: In the name of God, O God, protect us. Satan and avoid Satan as long as You have provided for us, for if a child is born between them then Satan will never harm him."
"30352","(30352) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, Abu Asid’s client: I got married while I was a slave, so I invited a group of the Prophet’s companions, may God bless him and grant him peace. Among them were Abu Masoud, Abu Dharr, and Hudhayf. They teach me, so he said: When your family enters upon you, pray two rak’ahs, then ask God for the best of what has entered upon you, then seek refuge in Him. Of his evil, then it is your business and the business of your family."
"30353","(30353) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of my nephew Alqamah bin Qais, on the authority of Alqamah, that when Ibn Masoud was cheated by his family and he descended, he would say: Oh God, do not allow Satan to You have bestowed upon me a share."
"30354","(30354) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Bakr, who said: It was said: He will cover what is between the private parts of the children of Adam. And in the eyes of the jinn and the devils, when one of you says, when he puts on his clothes, “In the name of God.” (Tirmidhi 606)"
"30355","(30355) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Amr Ibn Dinar Al-Qaramani, on the authority of Salim Ibn Abdullah Ibn Omar, on the authority of My father, he said: There is no man who sees someone afflicted and says: Praise be to God who has cured me of what He afflicted you with and has favored me over you, and Many of His creation are virtuous, but God has spared them from that affliction, whatever it may be. (Tirmidhi 3431, Ibn Majah 3892)"
"30356","(30356) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: When Moses was sent to Pharaoh, he said: My Lord, what should I say? He said: Say: Hiya, evil, Hiya. Al-Amash said: The interpretation of that: Al-Hayy before everything, and Al-Hayy after everything."
"30357","(30357) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Utba, on the authority of Ibn Hudhayfah, on the authority of His father, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, supplicated for a man, it would afflict him, and afflict his children, and he would afflict his children. (Ahmed 385)"
"30358","(30358) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: The man will be raised By the supplication of his children after him."
"30359","(30359) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Asim bin Badla, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A man’s rank in Paradise will be raised for him, and he will say: O Lord. Why do I have this? It is said: By asking your child for forgiveness. (Ahmed 509)"
"30360","(30360) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: When the ghouls deceive you, call out the call to prayer. (Nasa’i 10791)"
"30361","(30361) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yasir bin Amr, who said: Ghouls were mentioned at the time of Omar, may God have mercy on him. He said: There is nothing that can change God’s creation, but they have magic like your magic. So if You saw something of that, so you announced it."
"30362","(30362) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of his brother Isa bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, that he was in a place of his own and the ghouls were coming, So he complained about her to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: When you see her, say: In the name of God, answer the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: I came to him, and he said: No, so he took her and she said to him: I will not come back, so he sent her, so he came and said to him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: What did your prisoner do? He said: I took it, and she said: I will not come back, so I sent it, and he said: I am returning, so I took it two times, or three times. Then you say: I will not return, and he comes to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and says: What did your prisoner do? He says: I took it, and she says: I will not come back. He says: I am returning. So she took it and said: Send me and I will teach you something that you will say. Nothing can come close to you, namely the Throne. So he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him, and he said: You have told the truth, but it is a lie. (Tirmidhi 2880, Ahmad 423)"
"30363","(30363) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: He who I do not come to from among the people of the Levant narrated to me, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw the crescent, he would say: God is great, God is great. Praise be to God, there is no power nor strength except in God. Oh God, I ask you for the best of this month and I seek refuge in You from the evil of fate, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of destiny. Beware of the evil of the Day of Judgment."
"30364","(30364) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, who said: I left with Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, so we said: This is the crescent, O Abu Muhammad. When he saw it, he said: You believe in Him who created you, and He formed you and made you just. Then he turned to me and said: There was a Messenger of God. When God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sees the crescent, he says thus."
"30365","(30365) Waki’ narrated to us, Zechariah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: Then If one of you sees the crescent, do not raise his head to it. It is sufficient for one of you to say: My Lord and your Lord is God."
"30366","(30366) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that Ali used to say when he saw the crescent: O God, grant us the best. And His victory, blessings, and light, and we seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what comes after it."
"30367","(30367) Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Hajjaj bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He hated to stand up for the crescent, but he objected and said: God is the greatest. Praise be to God who went with such-and-such crescent. And so and so, and he brought the crescent of such and such."
"30368","(30368) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, that the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was when He saw the crescent and said: A crescent of goodness and guidance, a crescent of guidance and goodness, a crescent of goodness and guidance. You have believed in Him who created you as three, praise be to Him. For God's sake, he went with the crescent of such-and-such, and brought with the crescent of such-and-such."
"30369","(30369) Hussein bin Ali told us, he said: I asked Hisham bin Hassan: What did Al-Hassan say when he saw the crescent? He said: He was saying: Oh God, make him a month of blessings, light, reward and well-being. Oh God, you are the divider between your servants. There is good in it, so divide for us in it some of the best that you divide for Your righteous servants."
"30370","(30370) Hussein bin Ali told us, he said: I asked Ibn Juraij and he mentioned about Ata’, that a man granted a crescent a falafel of The earth, he said: Then he heard someone saying: Oh God, bestow upon us security, faith, peace, Islam, guidance, and forgiveness. And success in what you are pleased with and protection from what you displease. My Lord and your Lord is God. He said: He did not complete them until I preserved them, and I did not see anyone."
"30371","(30371) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayedah, on the authority of Mughiriyah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They were amazed when The man saw the crescent moon and said: My Lord and your Lord is God."
"30372","(30372) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Asbagh bin Zaid told us, Abu Al-Ala told us, on the authority of Abu Imamah, He said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab put on a new garment and said: Praise be to God who has clothed me so that I do not cover my private parts with it or beautify myself with it. My life. Then he said, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever wears a new garment and says: Praise be to God who He covered me with it, and I beautified myself with it during my life. Then he went to the garment that he had put on, or he said: he had thrown on. So he gave it in charity. It was in God’s protection, God’s protection, and God’s protection, alive and dead. He said it three times."
"30373","(30373) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of his brother Isa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abu Layla said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you wears a new garment, let him say: Praise be to God. He who has clothed me with what I conceal my private parts with, and with which I beautify myself in front of people."
"30374","(30374) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of a man from Muzain, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Ali Omar saw a washed garment and said: Is this your garment new? He said: Washing, O Messenger of God. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Wear new clothes, live praising the world, and die a martyr’s death. May God give you comfort in this world and the hereafter."
"30375","(30375) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Wahhab, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, he said: If a person wears The new garment, and he said: O God, make it a blessed garment in which we may be grateful for Your blessings, and in which we may improve Your worship. And we will act in it in obedience to you. It will not go beyond his collarbone until he forgives him."
"30376","(30376) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Aoun bin Abdullah narrated to us, he said: A man put on a new garment. So he praised God, and he was admitted to Paradise, or was forgiven. He said: Then a man said to him: Go back to my family so that he may put on new clothes. And I thank God for him."
"30377","(30377) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, who said: They were the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. When they see someone wearing a new garment, they say: It will be worn out, but God will change it."
"30378","(30378) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Al-Jariri informed us, on the authority of Abu Nazrhi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless you and grant you peace. When he wears a new garment, he names it by its name, whether it is a shirt, a garment, or a turban. He says, “O God, be with you.” Praise be to You, You have clothed me with this. I ask You for the good of him and the good of what was done to him, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of him and the evil of what was done to him."
"30379","(30379) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, regarding his saying: (And do not be ungrateful. With your prayers and do not be afraid of them.) She said: Supplication."
"30380","(30380) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid al-Muttab, on the authority of Ibrahim and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak bin Ubaid. On the authority of Ataa, he said: Supplication."
"30381","(30381) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hijri, on the authority of Abu Iyad, who said: The supplication."
"30382","(30382) Bakr bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, saying: Issa bin Al-Mukhtar narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid in This verse: {And do not be bold in your prayer, nor be silent in it.} He said: This is in supplication and begging."
"30383","(30383) Ismail Ibn Aliyah and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Hasan, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque, he would say: In the name of God and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. O God, forgive my sins and open for me the doors of Your mercy. And when he came out, he said: In the name of God and peace be upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. O God, forgive me my sins, and open to me Doors of your grace"
"30384","(30384) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hind, on the authority of Amr bin Amr Al-Madani, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab said that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque, he would say: O God, open for me The doors of Your mercy and facilitate for me the doors of Your provision."
"30385","(30385) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Ali, who said: It was when He entered the mosque and said: O God, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your mercy. And when he left, he said: O God, forgive me. my sins and open for me the doors of Your grace."
"30386","(30386) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: According to Kaab bin Ajra: When you enter the Sacred Mosque, greet the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and say: O God, open for me the doors Your mercy, and when you leave, greet the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and say: Oh God, protect me from the accursed Satan."
"30387","(30387) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, that when Abdullah bin Salam entered the mosque, he greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O God, open I have the doors of your mercy, and when he goes out, he greets the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and seeks refuge from Satan."
"30388","(30388) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Dhu Haddan, on the authority of Alqamiya, that it was When he entered the mosque, he said: Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. May God’s blessings and angels be upon Muhammad."
"30389","(30389) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, when he entered the mosque, he said: In the name of God and peace be upon the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"30390","(30390) Habib bin Abi Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: Whoever hears the caller calling By establishing the prayer, he said: O God, Lord of this perfect supplication and the established prayer, grant Muhammad his request on the Day of Resurrection except He was among those who interceded for him."
"30391","(30391) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you hear the muezzin saying, “The prayer has begun,” then say: Oh God, Lord of this perfect supplication and the established prayer, grant Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, his request on the Day of Resurrection. It is said by a man when the muezzin stands, but God will admit him to the intercession of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace on the Day of Resurrection."
"30392","(30392) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, that when Uthman heard the muezzin, he would say, “The prayer has risen.” Prayer. He said: Welcome to those who speak justice and to prayer, welcome and welcome. Then he got up to pray."
"30393","(30393) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of the one who informed him, on the authority of Mujahid, that when the muezzin said, “Live Upon the blessing, he said: The one who seeks help is Allah. Then when he said: Hail the Falah, he said: There is no power nor strength except in Allah."
"30394","(30394) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Al Harith, on the authority of His father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say something like what the muezzin says, so when he said, “Hayya ala-salaat,” Haya ala. Al-Falah said: There is no power nor strength except with Allah."
"30395","(30395) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah bin Salih narrated to us, saying: Habib bin Ubaid Al-Kala’i narrated to me, On the authority of Jubayr ibn Nufayr al-Hadrami, on the authority of Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja’i, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says about the dead: O God, forgive him, have mercy on him, protect him, pardon him, honor his abode, widen his entrance, and wash him. With water, snow, and hail, and purify it from sins just as a white garment is purified from filth. Oh God, replace it with a better abode. His home, and a husband better than his wife, and a family better than his family, and admit him to Paradise, and save him from Hell, or he said: Protect him from the torment of the Fire, until I wished that I were him."
"30396","(30396) Abu Usama told us, he said: Hisham Al-Dastawai told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Ibrahim Al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, said that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say in the prayer for the dead: O God Forgive our living and our dead, our witnesses and our absent, our males and our females, our young and our old."
"30397","(30397) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of al-Jalās, on the authority of Uthman ibn Shammas, who said: We were with my father. He saw him, so Marwan passed by him and said to him: Some of your hadith on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he went on and then returned. So we said: Now it happens to him, and he said: How did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying over the funeral? He said: I heard him say: You guided her to Islam and you took her soul, you know its secrets and its revelations. We have come to you as intercessors. So forgive her."
"30398","(30398) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of a man from the people of Mecca, on the authority of Abu Salama, who said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in the funeral prayer: O God, forgive our living and our dead, our males and our females. And those of us who are present and those who are absent, our young and our old, O God, whoever of us You have kept alive, let him live in Islam, and whoever You have caused to die. From us, he passed away in Islam."
"30399","(30399) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik, who said: When Abu Bakr prayed for the dead, He said: Oh God, your servant has surrendered his family, wealth, and family, and the sin is great, and You are Forgiving and Merciful."
"30400","(30400) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Omar used to say in the prayer if it was the evening, he said: Oh God, your servant has passed the evening, and if it was the morning, he would say: Oh God, your servant has renounced the world and left it to its people in the morning. And you did not need Him, and He became in need of You. He bore witness that there is no god but You, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger, so forgive him his sins."
"30401","(30401) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, who said: Ali used to say: In prayer for the dead: O God, forgive our living and our dead, and reconcile our hearts, and make peace between us, and make our hearts On the hearts of our best, O God, forgive him, O God, have mercy on him, O God, return him to something better than what he was in, O God Excuse me"
"30402","(30402) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: I was at the funeral of a sheep, and a man told me about him, that, He said: I heard Abu Musa praying over a dead person, so he said “Allahu Akbar” and said: O God, forgive him as he asked for your forgiveness, and give him what he asked of you, and increase him from Thank you"
"30403","(30403) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: Abdullah bin Salam, peace be upon him, said The funeral is to say: O God, forgive our living and our dead, our young and our old, our males and our females, and our witnesses. And those who are absent from us, O God, whoever You cause among us to die, cause him to die in faith, and whoever You spare among us, cause him to die in Islam."
"30404","(30404) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Zaid Al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq Al-Naji, he said: I asked Abu Sa’id, about The funeral prayer, and he said: We used to say: O God, our Lord and His Lord, You created him, provided for him, gave him life, and sufficed him, so forgive us. And do not deprive us of his reward, and do not lead us astray after him."
"30405","(30405) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Awan narrated to us, he said: Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Amr bin Ghaylan, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, that he used to say in prayer for the dead: O God, forgive our living And our Muslim dead, O God, forgive the believing men and believing women, the Muslim men and Muslim women, and reconcile the affairs between them. And reconcile their hearts, and make their hearts like the hearts of the best of them. O God, forgive so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, his sin, and grant him justice. By His Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, O God, raise his rank among the righteous and succeed him in his succession among those who left behind. And put his book in the heavens, and forgive us and him, O Lord of the worlds. O God, do not deprive us of his reward, and do not lead us astray after him."
"30406","(30406) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to say during the funeral When he prays upon him: O God, bless him, bless him, forgive him, and place him in the basin of Your Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said, “There is a lot of standing and a lot of talking, of which I did not understand anything other than that.”"
"30407","(30407) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hariz, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Awf, on the authority of Ibn Luhayy. Al-Hawzani said that he witnessed the funeral of Sharhabeel bin Al-Samat, and Habib bin Muslim Al-Farii came to it and came. He is like one who supervises us from his long standing, and he said: Strive hard for your brother in supplication, and let it be of what you supplicate for him. O God, forgive. For this Hanafi, Hanafi, Muslim soul, and make it among those who repent and follow your path, protect it from the torment of Hell, and seek victory against Him. Your enemy"
"30408","(30408) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not permit us. And peace be upon him, nor did Abu Bakr nor Omar say anything about praying over the dead."
"30409","(30409) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of thirty of the companions of the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, they did not do anything regarding the funeral prayer."
"30410","(30410) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There are no temporary supplications in praying for the dead."
"30411","(30411) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab and Al-Shu’bi, who said: There are no supplications for the dead. Timing"
"30412","(30412) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, who said: I asked Muhammad about praying for the dead, and he said: We do not know about it. Something temporary, pray for the best of what you know."
"30413","(30413) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, who said: There is nothing in praying over the dead. Temporarily"
"30414","(30414) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Musa Al-Jinni, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi and Al-Hakam, and Ata’ and Mujahid in Is praying for the dead a temporary thing? They said: No, but you are an intercessor, so intercede with the best of what you know."
"30415","(30415) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Mughith bin Sumayy, he said: He was a man who was Before you, he used to commit sins, so he thought one day and said: Oh God, your forgiveness is your forgiveness, so he was forgiven."
"30416","(30416) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Saksaki, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: He came A Bedouin went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, teach me something from the Qur’an that will be sufficient for me, for I do not The best part of the Qur’an. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Say, Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God. And God is the Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except with God. So the Bedouins counted them as five in his hand, then he turned away, then He came back and said: O Messenger of God, this is for my Lord, so what is mine? He said: Say: O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, provide for me, protect me, and guide me. So the Bedouin counted them in his hand as five, then he went off and said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The Bedouin has filled his hands with goodness if he fulfills what he said."
"30417","(30417) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: A man from the Ansar was stung, and when In the morning, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said, “O Messenger of God, yesterday I was still awake from a scorpion sting,” so the Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: If you had said in the evening, “I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from the evil of what He has created, not even a scorpion would have harmed you.” In the morning, Abu Saleh said: I taught it to my daughter and son, and she bit them, but it did not harm them in the least. (Nasa’i 10433)"
"30418","(30418) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever says “in the evening” three times, I seek refuge With the perfect words of God, from the evil of what He created, no harm was caused by the sting of that night. Suhail said: So his people were accustomed to They said: A woman was stung but she found no pain in her. (Tirmidhi 3400, Ahmed 290)"
"30419","(30419) Abd al-Rahman bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Tariq bin Abi Makhashin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: A man was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who had been stung by a scorpion. He said: If only he had said, “I seek refuge in the words of God.” He is completely free from the evil of what he created, neither was he bitten, nor was he harmed by it."
"30420","(30420) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Ali, He said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying one night, he put his hand on the ground and a scorpion stung him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took it with his sandals and killed it. When he left, he said: May God disgrace the scorpion. Do not call it a praying person. And no one else, or a believer, and no one else. Then he called for salt and water and put it in a vessel and poured it on his finger where it She stung her, and he wiped her and sought refuge with her with the two exorcists."
"30421","(30421) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The ruqyah for a scorpion is to use salt on its horns. Sea of Qafta."
"30422","(30422) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I showed it to Aisha. She said: These are covenants."
"30423","(30423) Mu’awiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Qadamah bin Hamata, on the authority of Ziyad bin Hudayr, he said: I heard Al-Alaa bin Al-Hadrami speaking to his uncle, that one of his supplications when he waded into the sea was: O God, O Forbearing, O Ali. Oh great"
"30424","(30424) Qutaybah bin Sa’id narrated to us, saying: Laith bin Sa’d narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When you hear the cockroach, ask God for His bounty, for it has seen A king, and when you hear the braying of a donkey, seek refuge in God from the accursed Satan, for it has seen a Satan. (Bukhari 3303. Muslim 2092)"
"30425","(30425) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: If you hear the barking of dogs, or the braying of a donkey, night, so seek refuge in God, for they see what you do not see. (Bukhari 1234, Ahmed 306)"
"30426","(30426) Waki’ ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Amr, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whenever Ibn Abbas heard the crowing of a donkey He said: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. I seek refuge in God, the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, from the accursed Satan."
"30427","(30427) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Amr, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There is no servant who asks God the jinn three times, but the jinn says: Oh God, admit him to the jinn, and no servant They seek refuge in God from the Fire three times, but the Fire says, “O God, protect him from it.” (Tirmidhi 2572. Ibn Hibban 1014)"
"30428","(30428) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-A’la al-Taymi, who said: The jinn and hell have taught the people of Adam, when a man asks the jinn, the jinn says: O God, let him enter me, and when he seeks refuge from the Fire, it says: O God, grant him protection. From me"
"30429","(30429) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Aamir ibn Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Abdullah did not witness a gathering, nor did He is polite and stands until he praises God and sends blessings upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, even if he is among those who follow, he neglects a place. In the market, he sits there and praises God and sends blessings upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"30430","(30430) Talaq ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hibba al-Arni, on the authority of Ali, who said: Who He said when he heard every sneeze, “Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds,” for every condition, as long as there was no toothache or earache. Never"
"30431","(30431) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of Ubayyah, he said: He delayed Omar’s The news of Nahavand and the news of Al-Numan bin Muqrin, so he began to ask for help."
"30432","(30432) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Jahl, on the authority of a man who narrated to him on the authority of Ali, He said: Whoever recites after Fajr {Say: He is God, One} ten times, no sin will befall him on that day, even if you strive. The devils"
"30433","(30433) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Hilal, who said: Whoever recites {Say: Allah is One} ten times, it will be built for him. A tower in heaven."
"30434","(30434) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Sa’id, who said: Nafi’ ibn Jubayr joined me when I left Morocco, so I said: What is the matter with you? He said: When you pass by the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Peace be upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and may God have mercy on him. Satan says: No, keep him company. So when you enter your family, say: Peace be upon you. Satan says: No, spend the night. So when you bring your dinner, say: In the name of God, for Satan gives you a despicable friend. He says to his companions: Neither overnight nor dinner."
"30435","(30435) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He will not sleep until he recites: {Al-Maam Revelation} and {Blessed is He in Whose Hand is the dominion}. (Bukhari 1209, Darmi 3411)"
"30436","(30436) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: I preferred: {Al-Laam Revelation} and {Blessed is He in Whose Hand is Kingdom over the rest of the Qur’an with sixty good deeds. (Tirmidhi 2892, Darmi 3412)"
"30437","(30437) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abu Yunus, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Whoever recites in Laylat: {Then the prostration was revealed} and {Blessed is He in whose hand is the dominion} was like the reward of Laylat al-Qadr. He said: Then Ata passed So we said to a man among us: Come and ask him, and he said: He is right, I have not abandoned them since I heard them."
"30438","(30438) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us on the authority of Aban bin Salih, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: If one of you’s animal or camel drives away a piece of land that no one can see, let him say: Help the servants of God, for He will help. (Abu Ali 5247)"
"30439","(30439) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Dhikwan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Muslim’s claim It is answered unless he supplicates for injustice, or severing ties of kinship, or says: I supplicated but I did not answer."
"30440","(30440) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ubaid, a servant of Abu Rum, who said: It was passed. With Abu Hurairah on a palm tree, he said: O God, feed us with dates that the sons of Adam do not enjoy."
"30441","(30441) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It was said: If a man leaves the mosque, he should say: In the name of God, I put my trust in God. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from the evil that I have committed."
"30442","(30442) Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Ezriya ibn Qais, the food companion, narrated to me, saying: Umm al-Fayd narrated to me, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever says these words to Allah a thousand times, will not He asks God for something but He gives it to him. There is no sin in it, nor severing ties of kinship. Glory be to God, whose throne is in the heavens. Glory be to God, whose resting place is on earth, Glory be to God, whose path is in the sea, Glory be to God, whose mercy is in Paradise, Glory be to God, whose authority is in the fire. Glory be to God, whose mercy is in the air. Glory be to God, whose judgment is in the graves. Glory be to God. God is the one who raised the heavens, Glory be to God who laid the earth, Glory be to God from whom there is no refuge except in Him. (Abu Ali 3544. Tabarani 412)"
"30443","(30443) Ahmad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad, who said: Abd al-Rahman bin Ziyad narrated to me, saying: A sheikh from Quraysh told me, on the authority of Ibn Ukaym, who said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said to me: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him. He said: O Ibn Al-Khattab, say: O God, make my secrets better than your public ones, and make my public good ones.\n(Tirmidhi 3586)"
"30444","(30444) Ja’far ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: It was one of the supplications of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. O God, help me in remembering You, thanking You, and worshiping You well. (Abu Dawud 1517, Ahmed 247)"
"30445","(30445) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Salma bin Wardan narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas, he said: She came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. A woman was complaining to a pilgrim, and he said: I will guide you to something better than that. May God bless you thirty-three times. When you sleep, and you say “Tasbeehani” thirty-three times, and “thank You” thirty-four times, He said: That is a hundred times better than this world. And what is in it?\n (Bukhari 635)"
"30446","(30446) Mus’ab bin Al-Miqdam narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Sinan Dirar bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Salih Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri and Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, God He lined up four words: Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is greatest. Then he said: Whoever says Glory be to God, Twenty good deeds are recorded for him, and twenty bad deeds are removed from him. And whoever says: Allah is the greatest, the like of that, and whoever says: There is no god Except Allah, then the like of that. And whoever says, Praise be to Allah, Lord of the Worlds, on his own behalf, thirty good deeds are recorded for him and removed from him. Thirty bad days (Abdul Razzaq 310)"
"30447","(30447) Ja`far bin Aoun told us, he said: Hisham bin al-Ghaz told us, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: He who says there is neither power nor strength. Except in God, and there is no refuge from God except in Him. God has protected him from seventy types of harm, the least of which is poverty."
"30448","(30448) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Sharik bin Abdullah bin Abi Nimr told us, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque, and a man was saying: Oh God, there is no god but You, and your promise is true, and meeting you Truth, and Paradise is truth, and Hell is truth, and the prophets are truth, and Muhammad is truth, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Ask You give him (Tabarani 8419)"
"30449","(30449) Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Samimi narrated to us, saying: Hisham Al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Many, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Three supplications are answered. There is no doubt about them: the supplication of the oppressed, the supplication of the traveler, and the supplication of a father for his children. (Ahmad 258, Abu Dawud 1531)"
"30450","(30450) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Asla’ bin Hayy, who said: I was in Medina seeking blood for myself, so I said: To Abu Hurairah, I pray to God to help me. He said: O God, if he is oppressed, help him, and if he is unjust, help him. Aliyah"
"30451","(30451) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A Jewish man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted you and said: Pray to God for me. He said: May God multiply your wealth and your children, make your body healthy, and prolong your life."
"30452","(30452) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in saying to a Jew or a Christian: “He has guided you.” God"
"30453","(30453) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his leaders, that a Jew in Aleppo belonged to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted a she-camel and said: Oh God, make him beautiful, so his hair turned black."
"30454","(30454) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, who said: There is no harm in a Muslim believing in The monk’s supplication, and he said: They are answered in us, but they are not answered in themselves."
"30455","(30455) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that He used to stand up for the soul of his child who had committed no sin, and say: Oh God, protect him from the torment of the Fire."
"30456","(30456) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ziyad Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Mughirah Ibn Shu`ba, he said: The miscarriage prays for his parents’ well-being and forgiveness."
"30457","(30457) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: Oh God, make it for us Abundance, resource and reward."
"30458","(30458) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: Al-Jalas Al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali bin Jahash, he said: I heard Samurah. Bin Jundub, and a young son of his died, so he said: Go and bury him, and do not pray for him, for there is no sin on him, and pray to God. For his parents to make it abundant and rewarding for them, or something similar."
"30459","(30459) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, he said: Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Your praise is in Ramadan is better than a thousand other days."
"30460","(30460) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was When the dead person is placed in the grave, he greets him and says: In the name of God, by God, and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of God."
"30461","(30461) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: When you place your dead in their graves, say: In the name of God, and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of God."
"30462","(30462) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to say a parable: That"
"30463","(30463) Sharik and Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Mudrik, on the authority of Omar, that he used to say, “When he entered The dead person is his grave, and Abu Al-Ahwas said: When they treat him poorly: Oh God, grant him his money, his family, his family, and his sins. Great, so forgive him."
"30464","(30464) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Khaythami, he said: They used to prefer it. When the dead are placed in the grave, they are to say: In the name of God, and in the way of God, and upon the religion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, O God. Protect him from the torment of the grave, the torment of the Fire, and the evil of Satan."
"30465","(30465) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he used to say: In the name of God and in the way of God. And upon the family of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. O God, make his grave spacious for him and enlighten him therein, and grant him peace. By His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and you are satisfied with him, not angry."
"30466","(30466) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, who said: If you place the dead person in his grave, do not Say: In the name of God, but say: In the path of God, and upon the religion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and upon the religion of Abraham An upright Muslim, and he was not of the polytheists. O God, make him steadfast with firm words in the Hereafter. O God, put him in something better than It was about him, O God, do not deprive us of his reward, and do not test us after him. He said: And these verses were revealed about the companion of the grave: {Allah makes those who believe firm with the firm word in the life of this world and in the hereafter}"
"30467","(30467) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, he said: He used to say In a dream when he sleeps: In the name of God and in the path of God and upon the religion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he says when a man enters His grave"
"30468","(30468) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: When you place the dead person in the grave, say: In the name of God. And according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"30469","(30469) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Jubayr bin Adiy, he said: I was informed, that Ali bin Abi Talib used to say when the dead person was placed in his grave: In the name of God, and upon the family of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace and the truth of Your Book and Your Messengers and the certainty of resurrection after death. O God, grant him peace upon his grave, and give him good tidings. In heaven"
"30470","(30470) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: If the dead person is placed In the grave, say: In the name of God and to God, and according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"30471","(30471) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Bakr, who said: When Anas Ibn Malik used to treat Ali The dead person is in his grave. He rose over him, then said: Oh God, your servant has returned to you, so be kind to him and have mercy on him. Oh God, dry the earth from Beside him and open the gates of heaven to his soul, and accept it from you with good acceptance. O God, if he is a doer of good, multiply his reward. His good deeds, and if he is an evildoer, then ignore his bad deeds."
"30472","(30472) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed, that Ali said “Allahu Akbar” to Yazid bin Mukaffaf. Four times, then he stood on the grave and said: Oh God, your servant and the son of your servant have descended upon you today, and you are the best one to be descended with. Oh God. Enlarge his entrance and forgive his sins, for we only know what is good, and you know it best."
"30473","(30473) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulki, who said: When the grave of Abdullah was finished Ibn Al-Sa'ib Ibn Abbas stood over the grave, stood over it, then made supplication, then left."
"30474","(30474) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, saying: I saw Ayoub standing at the grave and praying for the dead, and perhaps I saw him praying. And he was in the grave before he came out."
"30475","(30475) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: We entered upon Khabab and he had been stabbed by seven people. He cried out in his stomach and said: Had the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, not forbidden us from praying for death, I would have prayed for it. (Bukhari 5672, Muslim 2064)"
"30476","(30476) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar. He said: He heard a man He wished for death. He said: Then Ibn Umar raised his gaze to him and said: Do not wish for death, for you are dead, but ask God for well-being."
"30477","(30477) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No. One of you wishes for death because of harm that has befallen him in this world."
"30478","(30478) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, she said : I was next to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I lost him and sought him out, when he was in Al-Baqi’, raising his hand. He called and said: O daughter of Abi Bakr, you are afraid that God and His Messenger will be unfair to you. Indeed, God will come down in this matter. The night, the night of the middle of Sha`ban, in which more sins are forgiven than the number of hairs of the goat of a dog. (Tirmidhi 739. Ahmad 238)"
"30479","(30479) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Kathir ibn Muriya Al-Hadrami, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: God descends on the night of the middle of Sha’ban and forgives sins therein, except for a polytheist or quarrel. (Abdul Razzaq 7923)"
"30480","(30480) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Anas ibn Malik, he said: It was He had Magians working for him in his land, and he used to say to them: May God prolong your lives and increase your wealth. So they were They rejoice in that."
"30481","(30481) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Suqi narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Whenever Ibn Umar came as a pilgrim, or He performed Umrah, circumambulated the Kaaba and prayed two rak’ahs, and his sitting therein was longer than his standing, praising his Lord and asking Him. When he finished his two rak'ahs, he used to say between As-Safa and Al-Marwah: O God, protect me with Your religion, obedience to You, and obedience to Him. Your Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, Oh God, spare me your limits[corrupt] Oh God, make me among those who love You and Your angels, Messengers, and righteous servants. Oh God, make me love You and yours. Your angels and messengers, O God, give me the best of what You give your righteous servants in this world and the hereafter, O God, make me happy. for the ease and spare me the hardship, and forgive me in the hereafter and the first, O God, enable me to fulfill Your promise which You promised me, O God, make me one of the pious Imams, and make me one of the heirs of the Garden of Bliss, and forgive me. My sin on the Day of Judgment."
"30482","(30482) Ali told us, he said: Othman bin Hakim told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd Abi Al-Sha’athai, he said: If you come On the day of Friday, sit at the door of the mosque and say: O God, make me today the most direct of those who turn to You, and the closest to those who turn to You. He approached you, and he who supplicated and asked succeeded, then enter and ask and it will be given to him."
"30483","(30483) Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Asim, a servant of Qariba bint Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr, who said: I heard Qariba. It was narrated on the authority of Aisha that she said: Do not say to the poor: “Bless you in it,” for he asks the righteous and the ungodly, but Say: May God bless us and you."
"30484","(30484) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Subih, the client of Banu Marwan, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: I heard him say about The bond: In the name of God, you are the protector, you are the healer, and you are the lasting. Then it is tied with new hemp thread, or hair, then An animal is tied to it for paving the way."
"30485","(30485) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saeed, or Saeed bin Muhammad, he said: It was one of the supplications Peacock, saying: Oh God, protect me from wealth and children, and grant me wealth and work."
"30486","(30486) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Fitr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Sabit, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He invokes these words and glorifies them: O God, O reliever of grief, remover of distress, and responder. Those in need, and Most Merciful of this world and the Hereafter and Most Merciful to them, have mercy on me today with His mercy, by which you will free me from His mercy from siwak (Tabarani 558, Bazzar 3177)"
"30487","(30487) Waki’ and Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Ja'd, on the authority of Thawban, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Fate only averts supplications, and life is only increased by Righteousness (Ahmad 280, Hakim 493)"
"30488","(30488) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Ummila, on the authority of Samra bin Jundub, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The most beloved words to God are four: Glory be to God, Praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is great. It will not harm you whichever way you begin. (Muslim 1685. Ahmad 10)"
"30489","(30489) Waki’ and Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Samarra, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The best words are four: Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is great. You don't care which one you start with. (Ibn Majah 3811. Ahmed 11)"
"30490","(30490) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of a concubine of Abdullah bin Ja’far, who said: I passed by Ali while I was pregnant, so he wiped My stomach, and said: Oh God, make him a blessed male. She said: She gave birth to a boy."
"30491","(30491) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Sufyan bin Umayyah narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Shabur, he said: A man said To Tawus: Pray for us. He said: I do not find any fear in my heart now."
"30492","(30492) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Mahdi ibn Maimun narrated to us, on the authority of Ghaylan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that when The crow croaked and said: O God, there is no bird except Your bird, and there is no good except Your good, and there is no god but You."
"30493","(30493) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya ibn Wathhab, he said: I heard him saying in his silence: Oh God Punish the infidels of the People of the Book. Oh God, make their hearts like the hearts of infidel women."
"30494","(30494) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, he said: Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: We used to call for people to stand up. Sitting and praising God, bowing and prostrating."
"30495","(30495) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, who said: A man came complaining about his wife to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted them, took their heads, and said: Oh God, protect them between them."
"30496","(30496) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Salih ibn Hayyan, who said: I heard Abu Wa’il say: He gave me four years of life. He gave it to you in his hand, and said: “Allahu Akbar is better than this world and all that is in it.”"
"30497","(30497) Suleiman bin Harb narrated to us, saying: Shuabi bin Al-Hajjaj narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khumayr, he said: I heard Abd Allah bin Busr said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came down and brought him food. Suwaiq and Hays, so he ate, and a drink was brought to him, so he drank, then he ate from the one on his right, and whenever he ate dates, he would throw away the stones. Thus - and he pointed with his two fingers on their backs - he said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, rode, his father stood up and took With his bridle, he said: O Messenger of God, pray to God for us. He said: O God, bless them in what You have provided for them, and forgive them. And have mercy on them. (Ahmed 187)"
"30498","(30499) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Abu Aqeel narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Khalid narrated to us, saying: I heard Zayd bin Ali. He narrates on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: When he saw a star descending, he would say: O God, straighten it, protect it, and protect us from evil. What follows?"
"30499","(30499) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: Abu Aqeel told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, he said: Whenever Ibn Masoud bought a property, he would say, “O God, bless it for us, and grant it a long life and abundant provision.”"
"30500","(30500) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Abu Aqeel narrated to us, on the authority of a sheikh who narrated to him, who said: I asked Ibn Sirin: What should I say? About lightning if you see it? He said: Close your eyes and remember God."
"30501","(30501) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Ziyad, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Who said if he said Muezzin: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, protect me from my father, and I bear witness with whoever bears witness will have a reward. Who witnessed and who did not bear witness?"
"30502","(30502) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, the food seller, who said: Abu Ja`far used to say: I seek refuge in God from the evil of Satan and the Sultan, and the evil of the Nabatean when he Arabizes, and the evil of the Arab when he Arabizes, so it was said: How does the Arab Arabize? He said: If he takes them and their uniform."
"30503","(30503) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of a man from the people of Basra, who said: A gift was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while Aisha was standing praying, and he liked that you would eat with him, so he said: O Aisha, gather me together and be brief. He said: Say: Oh God, I ask you of goodness, all of it, both now and in the future, and I seek refuge in you. Beware of all evil, both present and future, and whatever decree I have made, bless me for it, and make its outcome good."
"30504","(30504) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umayr, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Makhoul He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no man who has a bath and bathes for three consecutive days. He says: Washing: In the name of God, O God, I only washed to seek Your healing and to confirm the truth of Your Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. about him"
"30505","(30505) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of the blind Zaid, he said: When he saw Yusuf, the dear of Egypt, said: Oh God, I ask you for the best of your goodness and I seek refuge in your strength from the evil of it."
"30506","(30506) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hamid, that Saeed bin Abi Al-Hassan used to say: Oh God We have put on the marks of faith and clothed us with the garb of piety."
"30507","(30507) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: We were in a place where animals could not penetrate, so I got up and I I recite these verses: “He forgives sins and accepts repentance, severe in punishment.” He said: An old man passed by a young mule, and he said: Say: O Forgiver of sins, forgive my sins, O One who is capable of repentance, accept my repentance, O One who is severe in punishment, pardon me from my punishment, O One who is long-lasting. Ali was fine. He said: So I told her, then I looked and did not see him."
"30508","(30508) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid, that Gabriel was appointed With needs, when a believer asks his Lord, he says: Hold it, hold it, for the sake of his supplication being increased. And when a disbeliever asks, he says: Give him, give him, in spite of his supplication."
"30509","(30509) Affan told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: Anas used to say: I have left behind me old women. They often pray to God to lead them to the Basin of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"30510","(30510) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, saying: Musa ibn Ubaidah informed us, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Hakam al-Ansari, he said: I asked him: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray in Al-Fath Mosque, which is called Al-Ahzab Mosque? He said: He did not pray there, but he made supplication, and it was part of his supplication that he said: O God, praise be to You. There is no guide for whom You have led astray, nor one who misleads. To whom you have guided, and there is no humiliator to whom you have honored, and there is no honor to whom you have insulted, and there is no supporter of whom you have let down, and there is no deserter to whom you have helped, and there is no comforter To whom You have humiliated, and no humiliator to whom You have made honorable, nor a provider to whom You have deprived, nor a deprive to whom You have provided, no one who withholds what You have given, and no giver of what It prevented, and there is no one to lift up what it has reduced, nor to cover what it has broken, nor to penetrate what it has covered, nor to bring it closer to what it has distanced, and no to distance it from what it has brought near, then He supplicated for them, and in the morning there was not a single one of the partisans or of the polytheists in the city, except that God destroyed him, not living. Ibn Akhtab and Qurayzah were killed and dispersed by God. (Ahmed 393)"
"30511","(30511) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Al-Muhallab narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jadali, said: David the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from a neighbor whose eyes see me. And his heart cares for me. If he sees good, he buries it, and if he sees evil, he spreads it."
"30512","(30512) Saeed bin Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ma’mal, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, he said: It was Ibn Abbas. When breaking the fast is brought, he supplicates before that, and we have learned that supplications before that are answered."
"30513","(30513) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim al-Wasiti, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: Whoever says when he has finished his ablution: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, I bear witness that there is no god but You, I seek your forgiveness and I repent to you. It was sealed with a seal, then raised under the throne, and it was not broken until the Day of Resurrection."
"30514","(30514) Abdullah bin Numayr and Abdullah bin Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Salem bin Abu al-Ja`d said: When Ali had finished his ablution, he used to say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad His servant and Messenger, my Lord, make me among those who repent, and make me among those who purify themselves."
"30515","(30515) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Wahb al-Nakha’i narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever performs ablution and says: I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, without any partner. And I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger three times, and eight gates of Paradise were opened for him through which he enters. I wish"
"30516","(30516) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, who said: Zahra bin Ma’abad Abu narrated to me. Aqeel, that his cousin told him, that he heard Uqba bin Amir say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who He performed ablution and completed his ablution, then he raised his head to the heavens and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Eight gates of Paradise were opened for him through which he may enter as he pleases."
"30517","(30517) Abd al-Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of al-Dahhak, he said: When his hudhafi was purified, he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Oh God, make me among those who repent and make me among those who repent. The purified ones."
"30518","(30518) Hushaym told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace, when he enters the private room, he says: I seek refuge in God from wickedness and evil things."
"30519","(30519) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Qasim Al-Shaibani, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: This house is dying, so if one of you enters the toilet Let him say: O God, I seek refuge in You from evil and evil things."
"30520","(30520) Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Aziz bin Omar, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muslim bin Yannaq narrated to me, On the authority of a man from Abdullah bin Masoud’s companions, who said: Abdullah said: If you enter the excrement and want to uncover yourself, say: O Allah, I seek refuge. Free from abomination, impurity, wickedness, evil things, and the accursed Satan."
"30521","(30521) Abduh bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: When Hudhaifi entered the toilet, he said: I seek refuge in God from Satan, the accursed, the unclean, the vile, the vile, the accursed Satan."
"30522","(30522) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, would say when he entered the shelter, “In the name of God, O God, I seek refuge in You from wickedness and evil things.”"
"30523","(30523) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan Al-Abdi, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: When you enter private rooms, say: Oh God I seek refuge in You from the impurity, the unclean, the vile, the vile, the accursed Satan."
"30524","(30524) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, he said: Israel told us, he said: Yusuf bin Abi Burda told us, He said: I heard my father saying: I entered upon Aisha and I heard her saying: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left He defecated. He said: Your forgiveness."
"30525","(30525) Hushaym bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, that Noah the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was... He finished defecating and said: Praise be to God who has removed harm from me and healed me."
"30526","(30526) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Awam informed us, saying: It was narrated that Noah, peace be upon him, used to say: Praise be to God who He gave me a taste of its pleasure, kept me in its benefit, and kept away from its harm."
"30527","(30527) Abd ibn Sulaiman and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ali, that Abu Dharr When he left the toilet, he would say: Praise be to God who has removed harm from me and healed me."
"30528","(30528) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Salama bin Wahram, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When one of you goes out of privacy, let him say, “Praise be to God, who has removed from me that which harms me and has retained from me that which will benefit me.”"
"30529","(30529) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Huraim narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, he said: Abu When Al-Darda' came out of the toilet, he said: Praise be to God who removed harm from me and healed me."
"30530","(30530) Abduh bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: Hudhayfy used to say when he came out: Praise. To God who removed harm from me and healed me."
"30531","(30531) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: Abu Aqeel told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, he said: Whenever Ibn Masoud bought a property, he would say: Oh God, bless it and give it a long life and abundant provision."
"30532","(30532) Abu Bakr bin Abi Shayba told us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Arabicize the Qur’an and seek its strange things. (Abu Ali 6529. Ahmed 445)"
"30533","(30533) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Arabize The Qur’an."
"30534","(30534) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Omar bin Zaid, who said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa: As for what follows? So understand the Sunnah, understand Arabic, translate the Qur’an into Arabic, for it is Arabic, and multiply it, for it is you. Contagious people"
"30535","(30535) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, saying: Wasil the client of Abi Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Aqeel, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, said: Learn Arabic as you learn memorization. The Qur’an."
"30536","(30536) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Arabicize the Qur’an."
"30537","(30537) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Uqba al-Asadi, on the authority of Abu al-Ala, who said: Abdullah said: Arabize the Qur’an. It is Arabic."
"30538","(30538) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Suhayb, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: It is more beloved to me to recite such-and-such verses with syntactic syntax than to recite such-and-such verses without syntactic syntax."
"30539","(30539) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to beat his son in tune."
"30540","(30540) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: A man said to Al-Hasan: O Abu Saeed, by God, I do not see you. He composed, and he said: O son of my brother, I excelled in the melody."
"30541","(30541) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza, he said: Salem told me that Zayd bin Thabit consulted Omar about gathering The Qur’an, but he refused and said: You are a people who compose music. He consulted Othman and he gave him permission."
"30542","(30542) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Raja’, who said: I asked Muhammad about the points of the Qur’an, and he said: I fear that you will add to the letters or subtract from them. I asked Al-Hasan and he said: Have you not learned the Arabic about what was written by Umar? And be good servants and understand the religion."
"30543","(30543) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mu’awiyah bin Yahya, on the authority of Yunus bin Misra al-Jublani, on the authority of Umm Al-Darda' said: I would love to recite it as it was revealed, meaning the parsing of the Qur'an."
"30544","(30544) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Hazim, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar. He said: Omar came to a people who were reciting prayers to one another. When they saw Omar, they remained silent, and he said: You were not reviewing. We said: It was. We recite to one another, so he said: Recite, but do not compose."
"30545","(30545) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Tha’labiya, on the authority of Muqatil ibn Hayyan, who said: The words of the people of the Arabian heavens, then he recited: (Ham By the Clear Book, We have made it an Arabic Qur’an that you may understand, and indeed, in the Mother of the Book with Us, Ali is All-Wise.)"
"30546","(30546) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Muwarriq, who said: Omar said: Learn the tune and the religious duties, for they are part of your religion."
"30547","(30547) Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, saying: Ja’far Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Sawadah bin Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Abu Jafar said: Part of a man’s jurisprudence is his awareness of the tune."
"30548","(30548) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Khalid Al-Asri, who said: When Salman came to us, we came to him. Let us recite the Qur’an, and he said: The Qur’an is Arabic, so they recited it to an Arab man, so we recited Zayd bin Suhan, and it was then Salman made a mistake and was blamed for it. When he was correct, he said: I swear by God."
"30549","(30549) Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Abd al-Rahman, he said: narrated to us who was We read from the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that they used to recite from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He recited ten verses, and they should not consider the other ten until they know what is in these of work and knowledge. He said: So we knew. Work and knowledge. (Ahmad 410. Ibn Saad 172)"
"30550","(30550) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, who said: Learn the Qur’an five verses by five verses. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to take it five by five. (Bayhaqi 1958)"
"30551","(30551) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman used to teach us five by five."
"30552","(30552) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abjar, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Qays bin He remained silent. He said: Abdullah said: Learn the Qur’an, for for every letter is written ten good deeds, and ten bad deeds are expiated thereby. However, I do not say: (lam), but I say: alif is ten, lam is ten, and meem is ten. (Hakim 555)"
"30553","(30553) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, he said: Muhammad bin Ka’b narrated to us, on the authority of Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever reads a letter from the Book of God, a good deed will be recorded for him. I do not say: That is the Book} but the letters are cut off from the Alif, Lam and Meem. (بزار ۲۳۲۳۔ طبرانی ۳۱۶)"
"30554","(30554) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Learn the Qur’an. And recite it, for God will reward you for reciting it with ten good deeds for every letter. As for me, I do not say: (lam), but alif, lam, and meem."
"30555","(30555) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Sulayman al-Dhabi, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, or al-Aswad. On the authority of Abdullah, he said: Whoever recites the Qur’an seeking the face of God will have ten good deeds for him, with every letter erased, ten good deeds. Bad deeds."
"30556","(30556) Hafs bin Ghayath and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Bara’. Ibn Azib said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Beautify the Qur’an with your voices."
"30557","(30557) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque and heard a man reciting it and said: Who is this? It was said: Abdullah bin Qais, and he said: This was given to me from the Psalms of the family of David. (Ahmad 354, Nasa’i 1092)"
"30558","(30558) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The Ash’ari was given a psalm from the psalms of the family of David. (Bukhari 1087, Muslim 546)"
"30559","(30559) Shababah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abu Musa when he heard him reciting the Qur’an: Your brother has been given some of the Psalms of the family of David."
"30560","(30560) Abu Bakr narrated to us, he informed me, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, or something similar to it. (Darimi 1489, Ahmad 167)"
"30561","(30561) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar said: Improve your voices. By the Qur’an."
"30562","(30562) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Nahik, on the authority of Saad, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He is not among us who does not sing the Qur’an."
"30563","(30563) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, in a narration: He said: God has not given permission to anything like His permission. For a servant who recites the Qur’an."
"30564","(30564) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: It used to be said: The people with the best voice in the Qur’an are those who fear Allah."
"30565","(30565) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Tawoos, he was asked: Who is the most intelligent among people? He said: He who, when he recites his vision, fears God. He said: And he was divorced from those."
"30566","(30566) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, he said: We were with Abu Musa and we went mad at night. To a ruined orchard. He said: So he got up during the night and recited the Qur’an beautifully."
"30567","(30567) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that Abu Musa was He was reciting one night, and the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, were listening, and it was said to him, and he said: If I had known, I would have been blessed. In love with excitement, or with excitement."
"30568","(30568) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Imran bin Abdullah bin Talha told us, that a man recited In the mosque of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Ramadan, he rejoiced, but he disapproved of that decree, and said, God Almighty says: {And indeed, it is For a Mighty Book: falsehood does not come to it from before it nor from behind it - a revelation from the All-Wise, the Praiseworthy}"
"30569","(30569) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, that a man recited with Anas and his mind was cheered up. That was Anas."
"30570","(30570) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Abi Bakr told us that Zaid Al-Numayri came with the Qur’a scholars to Anas bin Malik and was told: Read. He raised his voice, and it was a high voice, so Anas revealed the He put the rag on his face, and there was a black rag on his face, and he said: What is this? This is what they used to do, and whenever he saw something he would deny it, he would uncover the rag from his face."
"30571","(30571) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, who said: One of them was inserting verses into the stomach. The night"
"30572","(30572) Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Sadoosi told us, on the authority of Mufas bin Imran, on the authority of Umm Al-Darda’, who said: I entered upon Aisha, So I said: What is the superiority of one who recites the Qur’an over one who does not recite it over those who enter Paradise? Aisha said: The number of levels of Paradise is greater than Ali. The number of verses in the Qur’an, no one who enters Paradise is better than the one who reads the Qur’an."
"30573","(30573) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Rafi’ told us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: Whoever reads The Qur’an is as if prophecy was included between two parts of it, except that there is no revelation to it. (Hakim 552)"
"30574","(30574) Waki’ told us, he said: Imran Abu Bishr Al-Halabi told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: There is no superior to a servant who recites the Qur’an, and there is no need for him after him."
"30575","(30575) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: Whoever reads the Qur’an and follows what is in it, God will guide him from misguidance and protect him from a bad reckoning on the Day of Resurrection, and that is Because God says: {So whoever follows my guidance will not go astray, nor will he be miserable}"
"30576","(30576) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Amr bin Qays, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: God guarantees that whoever recites the Qur’an will not go astray in this world or He will be miserable in the Hereafter. Then he recited: {So whoever follows Your guidance shall neither go astray nor be miserable}"
"30577","(30577) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Hisham, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Umayr, he said: It was said: If he stays Reasonable people read the Qur’an."
"30578","(30578) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Whoever reads the Qur’an will not be returned to the wretchedness of life, then He recited: {so that he does not know anything after knowing}."
"30579","(30579) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, who said: Whoever reads the Qur’an, it is as if he saw The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then recited: {And whoever reaches it, let us bear witness}."
"30580","(30580) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Zayd, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: Whoever seeks protection The Qur’an has a supplication that, if He wishes, He hastens it for this world, and if He wishes, it may take it for the next."
"30581","(30581) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Ansari told us, he said: Ibn Shihab told us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Sabbaq, that Uthman said: It was revealed in the language of Quraysh, meaning the Qur’an."
"30582","(30582) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Salama bin Nabit narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: The Qur’an was revealed in every language."
"30583","(30583) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra, he said: The Qur’an was revealed in every language."
"30584","(30584) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Saif, he said: I heard a mujahid saying: The Qur’an was revealed on the tongue of Quraysh, and with it Their words"
"30585","(30585) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: {Al-Ma’un} in the language of Quraysh: money."
"30586","(30586) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, who said: The Qur’an was revealed with our tongue, meaning Quraysh"
"30587","(30587) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein ibn Waqid, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah: that Jurham’s language was Arabic."
"30588","(30588) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`d bin Iyad: {Kamishkaya} He said: Kakuwa In the Ethiopian language"
"30589","(30589) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: (Taha) in Ethiopian: O man."
"30590","(30590) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubair, who said: It is in the language of the Ethiopians: If he rises, he will rise."
"30591","(30591) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abu Musa {He gives you I will be assured of Your mercy. He said: I will be rewarded in the language of the Ethiopians."
"30592","(30592) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Abd God {Indeed, the one who arises during the night} said: This is the Abyssinian’s night prayer."
"30593","(30593) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Mujahid, in his saying: {Weigh with a straight balance} He said: Justice according to the Romans."
"30594","(30594) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ikrimah {and you will be steadfast}. He said: It is singing. With donkeys."
"30595","(30595) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: {Al-Qastas} is justice in the Roman language."
"30596","(30596) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: (Taha) in Nabataean:"
"30597","(30597) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qur’a bin Khalid, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: (Taha), O man of Nabatiyya."
"30598","(30598) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: (Taha) O man of Nabatiyya."
"30599","(30599) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Salamah bin Sabour, on the authority of Atiyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {May you be blessed}, he said: In Nabataean: Come on."
"30600","(30600) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas {stones made of shale} he said: In Persian it means “your age”, and every stone and clay."
"30601","(30601) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ibn Sabit {stones of shale} who said: In Persian."
"30602","(30602) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas {One of them would like to He will live for a thousand years."
"30603","(30603) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Umamah, who said: The angels who They carry the throne and speak deep Persian."
"30604","(30604) Jarir told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The speech of the people on the Day of Resurrection will be Syriac."
"30605","(30605) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Musma’ ibn Malik, who said: I heard Ikrimah. He said: Ibn Abbas was when He was asked about which part of the Qur’an he recited one of their poems."
"30606","(30606) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I did not know what His saying: {Our Lord Open between us and our people with the truth} until I heard the daughter of Dhu Yazan say: Come, I will open with you."
"30607","(30607) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of a statement, on the authority of Amir: {And when they were walking around} He said: On the earth, then he recited verses. For Umayyah: It contains the flesh of animals and sea animals."
"30608","(30608) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Furat, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: The contented one who asks, then he recited verses to Al-Shamakh: \nA person’s wealth is good for him and enriches him, and his poverty is more chaste than contentment."
"30609","(30609) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Abi Safiyya, on the authority of a sheikh nicknamed Abu Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The vile, clinging bastard, then he recited this verse: \nA sin that men treat as an increase, just as the width of the feet has been increased."
"30610","(30610) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mu’ali, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he used to recite: (Darsat), which is represented by: Daras is like the taste of soap and talc."
"30611","(30611) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Kahf, on the authority of his father: {And among them are those whose love has died} He said: He vowed, The poet said: She finished her weeping from Yathrib and continued."
"30612","(30612) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: The example of the Qur’an is that of a saddled camel, if its owner mounts it, it keeps it, and if it leaves it, it goes away."
"30613","(30613) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ali, who said: I heard my father saying: He said: I heard Uqba ibn Amir. He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Learn the Qur’an and acquire it, and the one in whose hand my soul is is more detailed. From the labor of her mind."
"30614","(30614) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Familiarize yourself with the Qur’an, for by the One in whose hand my soul is, it is more detailed than the hearts of men. Of camels, of their calves."
"30615","(30615) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Abdullah said: Be accustomed to these Qur’ans, and perhaps he said: The Qur’an is more detailed than the hearts of men, and more blessings than their minds."
"30616","(30616) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: Abdullah said: Be familiar with this Qur’an and it will be He is more detailing of blessings than his mind. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: How miserable it is for anyone to say: I forgot. Many verses and many other verses, but he forgot them. (Bukhari 5032. Tirmidhi 2942)"
"30617","(30617) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Issa bin Faid, who said: So-and-so narrated to me, on the authority of Saad bin Ubadah said: He told me, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: No one recites the Qur’an and then If he forgets it, he will meet God while he is a leper. (Ahmad 284. Tabarani 5387)"
"30618","(30618) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawad, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: No man learned the Qur’an and then forgot it without With a sin, then Al-Dahhak recited: {And whatever calamity befalls you is because of what your hands have earned} Then Al-Dahhak said: And what? A greater calamity than forgetting the Qur’an."
"30619","(30619) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Talq ibn Habib, he said: Who learned The Qur’an, then he forgot it without excuse, and every verse was dropped from him in degrees, and on the Day of Resurrection he will come as a judge."
"30620","(30620) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdullah bin Abi Mughith, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Sins were presented to me, but I did not see anything greater in them than the one who carries the Qur’an and abandons it. (Abu Dawud 462. Tirmidhi 2916)"
"30621","(30621) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Waqid, on the authority of Zazan, who said: Whoever recites the Qur’an so that people may learn from it will find By God, there is not a trace of flesh on His face."
"30622","(30622) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Omar said: Read the Qur’an and ask God through it. Before people read it, they ask people about it."
"30623","(30623) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Firas, who said: Omar said: He may There has come a time when I thought that whoever reads the Qur’an meant God, but now it has occurred to me that I will see a people who have... People recite it, so seek God by your recitation, and desire God by your deeds."
"30624","(30624) Al-Zubayri Muhammad bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythami, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran Ibn Husayn said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever reads the Qur’an should ask God about it, for There will come a people who will recite the Qur’an and ask the people about it. (Tirmidhi 2917 and Ahmad 439)"
"30625","(30625) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Omar said: Read the Qur’an and seek With it is what God has, before people read it, seeking what people have with it."
"30626","(30626) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Read The Qur’an, and ask God for it, for it will be recited by people who will perform it in the proper manner. You will hasten it, but you will not postpone it.\n(Abu Dawud 827. Ahmed 338)"
"30627","(30627) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Walid told us, he said: Omar bin Ayyub told me, he said: Abu Iyas Muawiyah ibn Qurayh told me, saying: I was staying with Amr ibn al-Nu`man ibn Muqrin, and when Ramadan came, he came to him. A man with two thousand dirhams from Musaab bin Al-Zubayr, and he said: The prince greets you and says: We have not left an honorable reader except A favor has come to him from us, so seek help from these people at the expense of this polytheist of yours. Amr said: Convey your greetings to the prince and say: To him: By God, we have not read the Qur’an with the intention of this world, but to return it to him."
"30628","(30628) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jaafar, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abu Shurayh Al-Khuza’i said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us and said: Rejoice, rejoice. Do you not bear witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God? They said: Yes, he said: Indeed, this Qur’an is the origin of one end of it, and one end of it is in the hand of God, and the end of it is in your hands, so hold fast to it, for you will never You will go astray and you will never perish after him. (Ibn Hibban 122 and Abd bin Hamid 483)"
"30629","(30629) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of Abu al-Mukhtar al-Tai’i, on the authority of my nephew al-Harith al-A’war, On the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: The Book of God, in which is the news of what came before you. And the news of those after you and the ruling of what is among you. It is the decisive factor, not a joke. It is the one from which the minds do not deviate, nor do Scientists are satisfied with Him, and He does not create a response due to much, and His wonders do not end. He is the one who has abandoned Him among the mighty. God has judged him, and whoever seeks guidance in other than that, God will lead him astray. It is the strong rope of God, and He is the Wise Reminder. And it is the straight path. It is the one on which whoever acts upon it will be rewarded, whoever rules by it is just, and whoever calls to it will be called to a straight path. Take it to you, O one-eyed man. (Tirmidhi 2906. Ahmad 91)"
"30630","(30630) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Hijri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: This Qur’an is God’s instruction, so learn from God’s instruction as much as you can. Indeed, this Qur’an is God’s rope. He is the clear light, the beneficial cure, protection for whoever clings to it, and salvation for whoever follows it. It cannot be crooked or straightened, nor He deviates and is reproached, and his wonders will not end, and he will not be created due to much response. (Hakim 555)"
"30631","(30631) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Aban bin Ishaq told us, he said: A man from his generation told me, he said: A grasshopper came out Al-Bajlili was on a journey, and he said: Some of his people went out with him until they were at the place where they were bidding farewell to one another. He said: O my people, you must fear God, you must adhere to this Qur’an, so adhere to it for all your effort and understanding. For he is a light in the dark night and a guide in the day."
"30632","(30632) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, he said: Abu Al-Bakhtari Al-Tai’i said to me: Follow this Qur’an. He will guide you."
"30633","(30633) Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Harun ibn Antar, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of His father, he said: Abdullah said: These hearts are weak, so occupy them with the Qur’an, and do not occupy them with anything else."
"30634","(30634) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, who said: Abd Allah said: Indeed This Qur’an is the training of God, so whoever enters it is safe."
"30635","(30635) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shihab, who said: Omar said: Learn the Book of God, become familiar with it, and act upon it. Be among its people."
"30636","(30636) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, on the authority of Abu Iyas, on the authority of Abu Kinana, on the authority of Abu Moses, he said: Indeed, this Qur’an is present for you as a reminder, or there is a reward for you, or there is a burden upon you, so follow them. The Qur’an, and do not follow you the Qur’an, for whoever follows the Qur’an will land therein on the gardens of Paradise, and whoever follows it will The Qur’an is thrown into the back of his mouth and thrown into Hell."
"30637","(30637) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, he said: Al-Akhnas ibn Abi Al-Akhnas narrated to us, on the authority of Zubaid. Al-Muradi, he said: I witnessed Ibn Masoud, and he stood up as a preacher and said: Commit to the Qur’an and adhere to it, until he started clenching his hands. All as if he was taken because of something."
"30638","(30638) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, who said: A woman passed by Isa, and she said: Blessed is the womb of your burden. And to the breast that breastfed you. He said: Then he said: Jesus. Blessed is he who reads the Qur’an and follows what is in it."
"30639","(30639) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A woman passed by Isa ibn Maryam, then he mentioned something similar to it."
"30640","(30640) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya bint Hassan, who said: I heard Anas say: {He held you by the loop. Al-Wathaqi}, he said: The Qur’an."
"30641","(30641) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Murra, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Whoever desires knowledge Let him read the Qur’an, for in it is knowledge of the ancients and the last."
"30642","(30642) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Abdullah said: May you be blessed. With the two cures: the Qur’an and honey."
"30643","(30643) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Honey is a cure for all. A disease, and the Qur’an is a cure for what is in the breasts."
"30644","(30644) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid (a healer for people) who said: Healing is in the Qur’an."
"30645","(30645) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The House The one in which the Qur’an is not recited is like a ruined house that has no repair."
"30646","(30646) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abbad, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The house in which the Qur’an is recited is one you should attend. The angels and the devils come out of it, and it expands with its family and its goodness multiplies, and the house in which it is not read Satans invade the Qur’an, angels come out of it, its people are distressed, and its goodness is diminished."
"30647","(30647) Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zaara’i, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: I heard Ibn Masoud say: It is yellow. The houses that are zero from the Book of God."
"30648","(30648) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, who said: The houses in which the Qur’an is recited To illuminate for the people of the heavens just as the heavens illuminate for the people of the earth. He said: And indeed, the house in which the Qur’an is not recited is distressed. And the devils will come to it and the angels will flee from it. Indeed, the yellowest of houses is the zero of the Book of God."
"30649","(30649) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair said: Whenever Abd al-Rahman bin Awf entered his house, he would recite the verses of the Kursi in his corner."
"30650","(30650) Affan told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Thabit told us, he said: Abu Hurairah was He says: In a house, when the Book of God is recited, it expands with its people, its goodness increases, and the angels attend it and come out. Among them are the devils, and if the Book of God is not recited in the house, it is distressed by its people, its goodness is diminished, and the devils are present in it."
"30651","(30651) Abu Muawiyah and Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Abdullah said: Indeed, I have listened to the Qur’an. I found them close together, so recite it as you know, and beware of extravagance and disagreement. Abu Muawiyah added: It is only as a saying One of you, may He be exalted and exalted."
"30652","(30652) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, he said: Read The Qur’an is childish, so do not be foolish about it."
"30653","(30653) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Hakim, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Hudhayfy said: Indeed, the most hypocritical person among people The one who does not leave out a waw or an alif, and leaves out the tongues just as cows twist their tongues, it does not go beyond his collarbone."
"30654","(30654) Abu Asama told us, he said: Al-Thawri informed me, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim: They were They hate to teach a child the Qur’an until he understands."
"30655","(30655) Abu Asama narrated to us, Al-Thawri narrated to me, he said: Aslam Al-Manqari narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy, he said: The Book of God: whatever is made clear of it, act upon it, and whatever is made clear to you, believe in it. And he entrusted it all to his scholar."
"30656","(30656) Ali told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Zubaid, he said: Abdullah said: Indeed, the Qur’an has a lighthouse like the lighthouse of the path. Whatever you know, adhere to it, and whatever is suspected of you, leave it."
"30657","(30657) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Khathim, who said: They were forced This Qur’an belongs to Allah and His Messenger."
"30658","(30658) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on the authority of Muadh, that he said: The Qur’an is a beacon like the beacon of the path, it is not hidden from anyone. So whatever you know of it, do not ask anyone about it, and whatever you doubt about it. So tell him to his scholar."
"30659","(30659) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, On the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who recites the Qur’an and is skilled at it is with the honorable traveler. The righteous, and he who recites it while it is hard for him will have a reward. (Bukhari 4937, Muslim 244)"
"30660","(30660) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’: The one for whom the Qur’an is made easy along with the honorable travel, And the one who escapes from it and is difficult for him will have a reward with God."
"30661","(30661) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, that when the gathering of his family was concluded, he"
"30662","(30662) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, who said: It is mentioned that the funeral prayer is prayed upon him when Seal"
"30663","(30663) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: He was Mujahid, and Abdah bin Abi Lubab and others. They were displaying the Qur’an, but when the day came that they wanted to seal it, they sent it to me and to Salama bin Kuhayl, and they said: We We were displaying the Qur’an, and we wanted to conclude the day, and we loved for you to bear witness to us. It used to be said: When the Qur’an was concluded, it would be revealed. Mercy at the end of it, or the presence of mercy at the end of it."
"30664","(30644) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, that he used to conclude The Qur’an is in three days, and the day on which one concludes one’s fast becomes the day."
"30665","(30665) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Mercy descends at the seal of The Qur’an."
"30666","(30666) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiyyah, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, that when He wanted to complete the Qur’an at the end of the day, he delayed it until evening, and if he wanted to complete it at the end of the night, he delayed it. Until morning."
"30667","(30667) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: On the Day of Resurrection, the Qur’an will represent a man, and another man will be brought to him. He has carried him, but he has disobeyed him in his affairs, so he appears as an adversary to him, and says: O Lord, you have carried him to me, so evil is a pregnant woman who has transgressed the limits of me and has been humbled. My duties, and he continued to disobey Me and abandoned my obedience, and he continues to hurl arguments at him, until it is said: What is the matter with you? Then He will take him by the hand, and he will not send him until he throws him on a rock in the fire, and brings him a righteous man who has carried him. And he kept his command, and he imitated an adversary besides him, and said: O Lord, You have carried him for me, so he is the best carrier. He has kept my borders and done what I have prescribed. He avoided disobeying me and followed my obedience, and he continues to hurl arguments at him until it is said: What is the matter with him? Then he takes In his hand, he did not send him until he had clothed him with a robe of brocade, placed upon him the royal crown, and given him a cup of wine to drink."
"30668","(30668) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Bashir bin Al-Muhajir narrated to us, he said: Abdullah bin Buraida narrated to me, On the authority of his father, he said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I heard him say: The Qur’an will meet its companion on the day Resurrection is when his grave opens like a pale man, and he says to him: Do you recognize me? So he says: I do not know you. So he says to him: I am the companion of your Qur’an. I made you thirsty in the hot days and kept you awake at night. Every merchant is for the sake of his trade, and today you are for the sake of every trade. He said: So he will be given the kingdom with his oath and eternity. With his left hand, and a crown of reverence will be placed on his head, and his parents will be clothed with two robes, and the people of this world will not stand up to them. They say: Why are we covered with this? He said: Then it will be said to them: By having your son take the Qur’an, then it will be said to him: Recite and ascend the stairs of Paradise and its chambers, so it is There is an ascension as long as this is recited, or as a recitation. (Ibn Majah 3781 and Ahmad 352)"
"30669","(30669) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Ubaidy al-Rabadi narrated to us, saying: Sa’id ibn Abi Sa’id narrated to us. Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ka’b, that he said: The Qur’an will be represented to those who used to act upon it in this world today. Resurrection is like the best form he has seen, the most beautiful face, and the most fragrant smell, so he stands beside his companion whenever he comes to him. His splendor calmed him down, calmed him down, and extended his hope to him, and he said to him: May God reward you with the best of a companion, so how beautiful is your appearance. And your scent is pleasant, and he says to him: Do you not know me? Come and ride with me, for as long as I have ridden with you in this world, I am your work. It was beautiful, and you will see my appearance beautiful, and it was good, and you will see my fragrance is pleasant, so he will carry it and bring it to the Lord, blessed be He. And God Almighty says: O Lord, this is so-and-so, and he is more knowledgeable about him than he is. You have occupied him during his days and in his life in this world. His day was thirsty and his night was sleepless, so grant me intercession for him, and the crown of kingship will be placed on his head, and he will be clothed with robes. Kingdom, and he says: O Lord, I desired this for him, and I hope for him something better than this from you, and he is given immortality. with his right hand and the blessing in his left, so he says: O Lord, every merchant has entered upon his family due to his trade, so he will be interceded for. His relatives, and if he is an unbeliever, his deeds will appear to him in the ugliest form he has ever seen, and he will stink, so the more he is horrified, the more he will be horrified. Awesome, and he says: May God make you ugly to a friend, so how ugly is your appearance, and how foul is your scent? Then he says: Who are you? He said: Do you not know me? I am your work. It was ugly and you would see my face as ugly, and it was smelly and you would see my smell as smelly. So he says: Come, so that I may ride with you, for as long as You have made me ride in this world. Then he rides with you and brings him to God, but he will not be able to stand for him. Weight"
"30670","(30670) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Yes. The intercessor is the Qur’an on the Day of Resurrection. He said: He says: O Lord, I used to prevent his lusts in this world, so honor him. He said: So he puts on a garment of honor. He said: And he says: Oh, my Lord, increase him. He said: Then he puts on a garment of honor, and he says: Oh, my Lord, increase him. He said: Then he is clothed with a crown of honor. He said: Then he says: O Lord, increase him. He said: If he is satisfied with him, then he is not after God’s satisfaction with him. Something (Tirmidhi 2915)"
"30671","(30671) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: The Qur’an will intercede for its companion on the Day of Resurrection, and He will be clothed with the robe of honor, and He will say: Oh Lord, increase it. Indeed, it is. He said: Then he is clothed with a crown of honor. He said: Then he says: O Lord, increase him, so surely it is, so he says: Your satisfaction."
"30672","(30672) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Mujahid, that he said: The Qur’an intercedes for its companion. On the Day of Resurrection, he will say: O Lord, You placed me in his belly, so I kept him awake all night and kept him from many of his desires. And every worker has his own workers, and it will be said to him, “Spread out your hand.” He said, “And you will be filled with the pleasure of God, and there will be no wrath upon him after him.” Then It is said to him: Read and incantate it. He said: Then his rank will be raised for every verse and his rank will be increased for every good verse."
"30673","(30673) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, he said: Mansour said: It was narrated on the authority of Mujahid, he said: The Qur’an will come. On the Day of Resurrection, he will be in the hands of his companion, until when they come to their Lord. The Qur’an says: O Lord, indeed, there is no one who acts. Except for him there is a share of his deeds, and indeed You placed me in his belly, so I forbade him from his desires. He said: Then it will be said to him: Extend your right hand. He said: It will be filled with God’s pleasure. Then it will be said to him: Extend your left hand. It will be filled with God’s pleasure. So no. God will never be displeased with him after that."
"30674","(30674) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, in his saying: {And he who brought the truth and believed in it}, he said: those who They will bring the Qur’an on the Day of Resurrection and say: This is what you gave us. We have certainly followed what is in it."
"30675","(30675) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Jafar, on the authority of Zazan, he said: It is said: The Qur’an is an intercessor. interceded and approved."
"30676","(30676) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Asim bin Badallah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: The Qur’an will come on the Day of Resurrection and will intercede for its companion, and he will be led to Paradise, or it will bear witness against it, and it will be He will lead him to Hell."
"30677","(30677) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Qais, on the authority of Zubaid, who said: Abdullah said: The Qur’an is an intercessor and an intercessor. And the solution is confirmed, so whoever makes him an Imam will lead him to Paradise, and whoever makes him behind his back will lead him to Hell.\n(Bazzar 122. Ibn Hibban 122)"
"30678","(30678) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, or on the authority of Abu Hurairah. Al-Amash said: It will be said to the Companion of the Qur’an: On the Day of Resurrection, recite and recite it, for your final destination will be at the last verse you recite."
"30679","(30679) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, with something similar, and he added to it: And recite as you used to recite in this world. (Abu Dawud 1459. Tirmidhi 2914)"
"30680","(30680) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: It is said to the companion of When he enters Paradise, recite the Qur’an, recite it in degrees, and recite as you used to recite in this world, for verily, your place of rank is at The last thing you read."
"30681","(30681) Ghandar narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: It is said: Read and perform ruqyah, he said: So his status will be raised for him with every verse and his goodness will be increased with every verse."
"30682","(30682) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Dahhak, who said: Al-Dahhak bin Qays used to say: O people. Teach your children and your family the Qur’an, for for whomever it is written for as a Muslim, God will admit him to Paradise. Two angels will be given to him. So they concealed him and said to him: Read and ascend the stairs of Paradise until he descends, where his knowledge of the Qur’an had ended."
"30683","(30683) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of his leaders, he said: I heard Anas say: Muadh, Ubayy, and Sa`d recited it, And Abu Zaid, he said: I said: From Abu Zaid, one of my cousins from the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.\n(Bukhari 3810, Muslim 1914)"
"30684","(30684) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: They recited the Qur’an during the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Ubayy, Mu`adh, Zayd, Abu Zayd, Abu al-Darda` and Sa`id ibn Ubaid accepted it, and none of the caliphs read it. The companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, except for Uthman, and Majma’ Ibn Jariyah recited it except one or two surahs.\n(Ibn Saad 355. Tabarani 2092)"
"30685","(30685) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Muadh came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Messenger of God, make me read. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Abdullah, make me read. So I recited to him what he had with me, then he and I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Muadh, who was a teacher, recited it. Among the teachers at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"30686","(30686) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Khumayr ibn Malik, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: I read from... The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has seventy surahs, and Zayd bin Thabit has two chapters in the Book. (Ahmed 389)"
"30687","(30687) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I gathered the ruling on The era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, meaning the detailed one. (Bukhari 5036. Ahmad 337)"
"30688","(30688) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Our companions did not differ, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died and none of his companions recited the Qur’an except four, all of them from the Ansar: Muadh bin Jabal, Ubayy ibn Ka'b, Zayd, and Abu Zayd."
"30689","(30689) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, regarding the saying of God Almighty (Say, by the grace of God And by Your mercy, in that let them rejoice. He said: (By the grace of God) the Qur’an, (and by His mercy) that you are made among His family."
"30690","(30690) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, in his saying: {Say, by the grace of God And by Your mercy, in that let them rejoice. It is better than what they gather. He said: The Book of God and Islam is better than what they gather."
"30691","(30691) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, regarding the saying of God, “Say, by the grace of God.” And by His mercy, he said: By the grace of God: Islam, and by His mercy: that He made you among the people of the Qur’an."
"30692","(30692) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Qur’an."
"30693","(30693) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, who said: By the grace of God and by His mercy, Islam And the Qur’an."
"30694","(30694) Shababah bin Siwar told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, he said, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, On the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Uthman, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best of you are those who learned the Qur’an and taught it. (Bukhari 5027, Abu Dawud 1447)"
"30695","(30695) Ahmad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of al-Nu’man bin Saad, on the authority of Ali, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best of you are those who learn the Qur’an and teach it.\n(Tirmidhi 2909. Darami 3337)"
"30696","(30696) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Would any of you like, when he returned to his family, to find within him three calves with fat bones? He said: We said: Yes. He said: Three verses that one of you recites in his prayer are better for him than three successive verses full of bones.\n(Muslim 552, Ahmed 466)"
"30697","(30697) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ali narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating, on the authority of Uqba bin Amer, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us while we were in the class and said: Which of you likes to go out in the morning? A day to Bathan, or Al-Aqiq, and from there he will bring two heaped she-camels, without any sin or severing ties of kinship. We said: Oh. The Messenger of God, we all love that. He said: If one of you goes to the mosque in the morning and teaches, or recites two verses from The Book of God is better for him than two she-camels, and three are better for him than three, and four are better for him than four, and the same number of camels. (Abu Dawud 1451, Ahmed 154)"
"30698","(30698) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: If five qaylas were given to someone, if he prayed the morning prayer in the Qur’an, he would say to his family: “I am about to go, by God, to sit.” If one of you learns five verses from the Book of God, they are better for him than five short verses, and five short verses."
"30699","(30699) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaydah, on the authority of his father, He said: He used to recite the Qur’an and pass by the verse and say to the man: Take it, for by God it is better than anything on the earth. He said: The man will think that he only means that verse until he does it to all the people. (Abdul Razzaq 5992)"
"30700","(30700) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: I have left among you what you will never go astray after that if you hold fast to the Book of God."
"30701","(30701) Affan told us, he said: Hassan bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Yazid bin Hayyan, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Arqam, he said: We entered upon him and said to him, “You have seen goodness. I accompanied the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and prayed.” He succeeded him, and he said: Yes, and he addressed us, and he said: Indeed, he left among you the Book of God, which is the rope of God. Whoever follows him will be upon him. Guidance and whoever abandons it has gone astray. (Muslim 1874. Ahmad 366)"
"30702","(30702) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Jarir told us, he said: Sulayman bin Shurahbil Al-Jabalani told us, he said: I heard Abu Imamah say: Read the Qur’an and do not be deceived by these suspended copies of the Qur’an, for God has not punished a conscious heart. The Qur’an."
"30703","(30703) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazeed, he said: Abd said: God: Whoever reads the Qur’an, let him give good tidings."
"30704","(30704) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Zakaria narrated to us, he said: Atiya narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: I am leaving among you two burdens, one of them greater than the other. The Book of God is a rope stretched from the heavens to the earth. (Ahmad 14. Tarzi 3788)"
"30705","(30705) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, he said: Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Yahnas Abu Musa, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, brother of Umm al-Darda’, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever recites a hundred verses in one night will not be recorded as one of the heedless, and whoever recites two hundred verses will be written as one of the obedient and He recited five hundred verses to a thousand verses, and a quintal of reward became for him, and a qirat of it was like a great hill. (Abdullah bin Hamid 200)"
"30706","(30706) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Muadh, that he said: Whoever recites A night with three hundred verses written by the obedient, and whoever recites a thousand verses will have two quintals of Qirat better than On the earth of anything."
"30707","(30707) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Damra, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Whoever reads On the night of a hundred verses were written from the obedient ones."
"30708","(30708) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. He said: Whoever recites a hundred verses in one night will not be recorded as one of the heedless, and whoever recites two hundred verses will be written as one of the devout.\n(Ibn Khuzaymah 1143. Hakim 308)"
"30709","(30709) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Who He recited on the night of fifty verses that were not written as one of the heedless, and whoever recites a hundred verses will be written as one of the obedient ones, and whoever recites Three hundred verses are written for a quintal, and whoever recites nine hundred verses, it will be opened for him. (Dharmi 3446)"
"30710","(30710) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Who He recited a hundred verses during the night, which were not written as one of the heedless, and whoever recited two hundred verses was written as one of the obedient ones."
"30711","(30711) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of al-Jadli, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Whoever recites ten verses in the night will not He will be written among the heedless. (Abu Dawud 1393; Ibn Hibban 2572)"
"30712","(30712) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Mansour, who said: Abdullah said: If only a man had spent the night carrying Ali. Striving in the path of God, and a man spent the night reciting the Book of God, God would have remembered the best of them. He said: And Abdullah bin Amr said: If A man spent the night spending one dinar after another and one dirham after another, and he mounted horses in the path of God until it was accepted by Him. And I continued to recite the Book of God until it was accepted from me. I did not like that I should have his deeds for my deeds."
"30713","(30713) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, he said: Al-Taymi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, he said: If a man spent the night giving And another person spent the night reciting the Qur’an and remembering God, you would have seen that the one who remembers God is better."
"30714","(30714) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Reciting the Qur’an is more beloved to me than fasting."
"30715","(30715) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: A man said to Hubba ibn He was one of Abdullah’s companions. He said: I read the entire Qur’an. He said: And I did not understand it."
"30716","(30716) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that it was He hates to say: I have read the entire Qur’an."
"30717","(30717) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salama, he said: Hudhayfy said: You do not read a quarter, meaning Baraa’."
"30718","(30718) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar disliked to say: Al-Mufassal, and he said: The Qur’an. Everything is detailed, but say: The Qur’an is brief."
"30719","(30719) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: Omar asked me, how much of the Qur’an do you know? I said: Ten surahs. Then he said to Ubaid Allah bin Omar: How much of the Qur’an do you have? He said: A surah. Abdullah said: He did not prohibit us, nor command us, other than that. He said: If you learn anything from it. So you should do this in detail, for it is better preserved."
"30720","(30720) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Do not say a short surah, nor a light surah. He said, so how should I say? He said: A simple surah. For God, Blessed and Most High, said: {And We have certainly made the Qur’an easy for the remembrance, so is there any who will remember?} And do not say it is light; For God said, “We will cast upon you a heavy word.”"
"30721","(30721) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, who mentioned something similar to it, but he differed from it in some words."
"30722","(30722) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Farwa bin Nawfal, he said: Khabbab said Ibn Al-Art and I went with him from the mosque to his house, and he said to me: If you can get close to God, then you cannot get close to Him. With something more beloved to him than his words."
"30723","(30723) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Ubaidah, about A verse in the Book of God? He said: You must fear God and be faithful, for those who knew about what the Qur’an was revealed have departed from."
"30724","(30724) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: A man asked Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab about a verse from The Qur’an, and he said: Do not ask me about the Qur’an, but ask about it whoever claims that nothing of it is hidden from him. Ikrimah"
"30725","(30725) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever speaks about the Qur’an Without knowledge, let him take his place in the Fire."
"30726","(30726) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, who said: Abraham hated to speak about the Qur’an."
"30727","(30727) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I met the companions of Abdullah and the companions of Ali, and they are not for any knowledge more deserving of interpretation of the Qur’an than them. He said: And Abu Bakr used to say: What heavens? You will provide me with shade and no land will shelter me when I say in the Book of God what I do not know."
"30728","(30728) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Abdullah bin Habib bin Abi Thabit narrated to me, he said: I asked Tawoos, about Interpretation of these verses: {A witness among you when death approaches one of you} and he wanted to be brutalized until this was said. Ibn Habib disliked the interpretation of the Qur’an."
"30729","(30729) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Humayd told us, on the authority of Anas, that Omar recited on the pulpit: {And a fruit and a father} Then he said: We know this fruit, so what is the father? Then he returned to himself and said: This is haughtiness, O Omar."
"30730","(30730) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: A man wrote a Qur’an and wrote down every verse. He interpreted it, so he called Omar for it and he loaned it to him with the lenders."
"30731","(30731) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam bin Hawshab, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, that Abu Bakr was asked about (And my father and father) Then he said: Which heaven will shade me and which earth will shelter me when I say in the Book of God what I do not know?"
"30732","(30732) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Whenever he was asked about something From the Qur’an, he said: God has accomplished what He intended."
"30733","(30733) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Shuaib, who said: Abu Al-Aaliyah used to read the Qur’an to the people, so if he wanted to change it The man did not say: It is not such-and-such, but he said: Recite such-and-such verse. So I mentioned it to Abraham, and he said: I think. Your friend has heard that whoever disbelieves in one letter of it has disbelieved in all of it."
"30734","(30734) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: I caught Abdullah in the Qur’an and he said: How did you see? I said: I read it as it is in the Qur’an except for one letter like this. I read it like this and like this."
"30735","(30735) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, saying: I used to recite to Abraham, and if I passed by a letter that he disavowed, he did not He says to me: It is not such-and-such, and he says: His scholar used to recite such-and-such."
"30736","(30736) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: Abraham said to me: Indeed, Ibrahim Al-Taymi wanted you to read it. Reciting Abdullah. I said: I cannot. He said: Yes, he wanted that. He said: When I saw him, he had disappeared. I said: So this will be in your presence, and we will remember the letters of Abdullah. He said: Enough of this for me. I said: What do you dislike about this? He said: I hate to say something is like this and not like this, or to say “wow” to it but not “wow” to it."
"30737","(30737) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: A man asked Ibn Masoud: {And those who believed and I followed them. Your descendants} Then the man started saying: Their descendants, so the man started repeating it and repeating it, and not saying: It is not like that."
"30738","(30738) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Indeed, I hate to witness the presentation of the Qur’an and say such-and-such and not. That's it"
"30739","(30739) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He used to hate it when he recited the Qur’an, avoiding a matter. The world."
"30740","(30740) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, who said: Whenever my father saw any matter of the world, he would be amazed. He said: Do not direct your eyes to what We have entertained a couple of them with."
"30741","(30741) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Ayyub, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The Qur’an was revealed in seven letters, whichever one you recite is correct. (Ahmad 433, Hamidi 340)"
"30742","(30742) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Qur’an was revealed to seven people. The letters are kul shaf kaf. (Tabari 19)"
"30743","(30743) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The Qur’an was sent down in seven letters, All-Knowing, All-Wise, Forgiving, and Merciful.\n(Ahmad 332. Ibn Hibban 743)"
"30744","(30744) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, he said: Abdullah bin Issa told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla said, Ubayy ibn Ka`b informed me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: My Lord has sent to me: to recite the Qur’an in seven harfs. (Muslim 562. Ibn Hibban 740)"
"30745","(30745) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Abi Ibn Ka'b, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Gabriel came to him and said: God has commanded you to teach your nation to recite the Qur’an. There are seven letters, so whichever letter they recite to, they got it right. (Muslim 562. Abu Dawud 1473)"
"30746","(30746) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hijri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: The Qur’an was revealed in seven letters. (Ibn Hibban 75. Tabari 12)"
"30747","(30747) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud’an, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abu Bakr, on the authority of his father, that Gabriel said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Read the Qur’an in one letter, so he said to him: Mika'il: Ask for more, and he said: On two letters, then he said: Ask for more, until he reached seven letters, all of which are clear and sufficient. Like your saying: Come and come, unless He ends a verse of mercy with a verse of torment, or signs of torment with mercy. (Ahmed 41)"
"30748","(30748) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Ubayy, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said Recite the Qur’an in seven letters, each one is clear and sufficient. (Ahmad 114. Ibn Hibban 742)"
"30749","(30749) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Suqayr al-Ubadi, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Surad On the authority of Ubayy, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Recite it in seven harfs. (Abu Dawud 1472; Ahmad 124)"
"30750","(30750) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The Qur’an was revealed in three letters. (Ahmad 16. Tabarani 6853)"
"30751","(30751) Khalid bin Majliz narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Aziz al-Ansari, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa Ibn Al-Zubair, on the authority of Al-Miswar Ibn Makhramah, and Abd Al-Rahman Ibn Abd Al-Qari, who said: We heard Omar Ibn Al-Khattab say: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, the Qur’an was revealed in seven letters, so read what you can of it.\n(Bukhari 2419, Muslim 560)"
"30752","(30752) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ubay, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted him: Gabriel met him and said: Tell them, let them recite it in seven syllables. (Tirmidhi 2944. Ibn Hibban 739)"
"30753","(30753) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Take the Qur’an from four people: Abdullah bin Masoud, Muadh bin Jabal, Ubayy bin Ka’b, and Salim. The servant of Abu Hudhayfah. (Bukhari 3760, Muslim 1914)"
"30754","(30754) Ibn Numir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: I recited to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said to me: Well done. (Muslim 551, Ahmad 424)"
"30755","(30755) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said Omar addressed us and said: Ali made us judge and Ubayy made us read, but we leave out some things from what Ubayy reads, and Ubayy says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I will not abandon the words of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for anything, and it was revealed after The father of a book."
"30756","(30756) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Jabir, who said: What I saw someone who had read the Book of God, but had no understanding of the religion of God, and had no knowledge of God in my life."
"30757","(30757) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Shabur, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: We used to be proud of the people about our reciter Abdullah. Ibn Al-Sa'ib"
"30758","(30758) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Dawud bin Shabur, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I was the proudest of people. By memorizing the Qur’an, until I prayed behind Muslimah ibn Mukhlid, and he opened Al-Baqarah, but he did not miss a “wa” or an “alif” in it."
"30759","(30759) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever is pleased to recite the Qur’an in a clear manner as it was revealed, let him recite as Ibn Umm Abd recited."
"30760","(30760) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Issa bin Dinar, the client of Amr bin Al-Harith, narrated to us, saying: Ubayy narrated to us. He said: I heard Amr bin Al-Harith say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who is pleased to read the Qur’an as it was revealed? Unfortunately, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd. (Bukhari 192)"
"30761","(30761) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Ammar bin Abi Ammar, he said: I heard Abu Habib Al-Badri said: When the verse “Those who disbelieve are not among the People of the Book” was revealed, etc., Gabriel said: O Messenger of God, your Lord has commanded you to recite it to Ubayyah, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ubayy: Indeed, Gabriel He commanded me to recite this surah to you. My father said: Did he remind me, O Messenger of God? He said: Yes. (Ahmad 489. Musnad 723)"
"30762","(30762) Muawiyah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: Whoever likes to read the Qur’an fresh, as it was revealed, let him read it as it was read by Ibn Umm Abd. (Ahmad 445. Ibn Hibban 7066)"
"30763","(30763) Mus’ab bin Al-Miqdam narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mughirah, that he heard Ibrahim say: Abdullah recited the Qur’an. On the back of his tongue."
"30764","(30764) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Abu Bakr died, and Omar and Ali died. They did not compile the Qur’an."
"30765","(30765) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: It was revealed and opens the Book. In the city."
"30766","(30766) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: Whatever was of Hajj or obligatory prayer, it was revealed. In Medina, and whatever mention of nations and generations and torment was revealed in Mecca."
"30767","(30767) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Al-Dahhak: O you who have believed in Medina."
"30768","(30768) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: Everything is in the Qur’an, O you who have believed. It was revealed in Medina, and everything in the Qur’an, O people, was revealed in Mecca."
"30769","(30769) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: We recited Al-Mufassal as proof while we were in Mecca but not there, O you who have believed."
"30770","(30770) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Every surah contains a O you who have believed, it is a city."
"30771","(30771) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. It was revealed In the city."
"30772","(30772) Qubaysah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shahr, who said: Al-An’am is Meccan."
"30773","(30773) Abu Ahmad narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Nadr ibn Qays, on the authority of Urwa: What was {O people} in Mecca? And “O you who have believed” was not in Medina."
"30774","(30774) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: They mentioned, according to Al-Sha’bi, his saying: “And a witness from his children witnessed.” Israel is like him} Then it was said: Abdullah bin Salam, and he said: How can Ibn Salam be when this surah is Meccan?"
"30775","(30775) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: Indeed, I know best what was revealed of the Qur’an in Mecca, and what It was revealed in Medina, so as for what was revealed in Mecca, he gave parables and mentioned the centuries, and as for what was revealed in Medina, it is the duties and punishments. And jihad."
"30776","(30776) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of his leaders, who said: I asked Anas about his recitation of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: He extends his voice with it."
"30777","(30777) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: She was a reciter of the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: {Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds} So I mentioned, letter by letter."
"30778","(30778) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Al-Aqma used to recite to Abdullah, and he said: Recite: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, for verily, the Qur’an is beautified."
"30779","(30779) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Whenever Ibn Sirin recited, he would continue with his recitation."
"30780","(30780) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata’ that they were these two Qara’ites. This"
"30781","(30781) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama ibn Kuhail, on the authority of Hujr ibn Anbas, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajr, he said: I heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {And not those who go astray} and said: Amen, extending his voice with it."
"30782","(30782) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, he said: Abdullah said, “Do not read the Qur’an like this poetry, nor You will scatter it as a scattering of dirt."
"30783","(30783) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid: {And recite the Qur’an in a recitation} He said: Part of it after Some"
"30784","(30784) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: {And recite The Qur’an is a recitation. He said, “I make it clear.”"
"30785","(30785) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid al-Muttab, who said: Mujahid was asked about two men, one of whom read Al-Baqarah and the last of them recited Al-Baqarah and the family of Imran, so their bowing, prostration and sitting were all the same. Which of them is better? He said: The one who recited Al-Baqarah, then Mujahid recited: {And a Qur’an which We have separated so that you may recite it to the people over a period of time, and We have sent it down in a revelation}"
"30786","(30786) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ubaidullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Muhab narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad bin Ka’b. Al-Qurazi says: Because reciting: {If you are shaken} and {Al-Qari’i} repeating them and contemplating them is more beloved to me than reciting the Qur’an."
"30787","(30787) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Qais, who said: I heard Omar bin Abdulaziz recite “Taslal”. Reading it"
"30788","(30788) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, that some people from the people of Kufa came to Abu al-Darda’. They said: Indeed, you are brothers from the people of Kufa. Convey your greetings to them, and they command you to recommend them. He said: So convey your greetings to them. And tell them, let them give the Qur’an to those who trust it, for it encourages them to do what is right and easy, and protects them from injustice. And the sad one."
"30789","(30789) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, he said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: You will not understand all of the jurisprudence until you see it. The Qur’an has many faces."
"30790","(30790) Dhudha bin Khalifa narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Mikhraq, on the authority of Abi Kinanani, on the authority of Abu Musa said: Give the Qur’an its secrets, and it will take away from you harshness and affliction and protect you from oppression and sorrow."
"30791","(30791) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Saad A servant of Amr ibn al-Aas. He said: Two men quarreled over a verse and went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Do not quarrel. Therein, indeed, dissent in it is disbelief. (Ahmad 204, Bayhaqi 2266)"
"30792","(30792) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Yazid informed me, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Thawban, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Leave hypocrisy regarding the Qur’an, for The nations before you were not cursed until they disagreed about the Qur’an. Indeed, dissimulating the Qur’an is disbelief."
"30793","(30793) Malik narrated to us, Abu Qadamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Imran Al-Junai narrated to us, on the authority of Jundub bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Recite the Qur’an as long as your hearts agree, and if you disagree about it, stand up.\n(Bukhari 5061, Muslim 2053)"
"30794","(30794) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Do not multiply the Qur’an one part with another, for that is It creates doubt in the hearts."
"30795","(30795) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Disputing the Qur’an is blasphemy. (Ahmad 478 and Abu Ali 5990)"
"30796","(30796) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, who said: I heard al-Nazzal saying: Abd said: God: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Those before you disagreed about it, so He destroyed them, so do not disagree. In it means in the Qur’an. (Bukhari 2410, Ahmed 393)"
"30797","(30797) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The parable of the one who combined faith and combined The Qur’an is like a citron with good taste, and the likeness of one who has not united faith and has not combined the Qur’an is like an evil colocynth. Taste and foul smell. (Dharmi 3362)"
"30798","(30798) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: His leaders narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, that Abu Musa narrated to him, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: The example of a believer who does not recite the Qur’an is like a date whose taste is good but has no fragrance. The example of a believer who reads the Qur’an is like a citron, which has a good taste and a pleasant smell, and the example of an immoral person who does not read. The Qur’an is like coconut, its taste is bitter and it has no fragrance. (Bukhari 5020 and Ibn Hibban 770)"
"30799","(30799) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, who said: The Qur’an is brutal, and is not suitable for confusion."
"30800","(30800) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham al-Dastawai told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, who said: The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, disliked raising the voice at the time of dhikr."
"30801","(30801) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, disliked raising the voice when reciting the Qur’an."
"30802","(30802) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: You came to him. While he was looking at the Qur’an, he said: I said: What do you read from the Qur’an? He said: My party with which I stand tonight."
"30803","(30803) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, who said: Abdullah said: Always look at the Qur’an."
"30804","(30804) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They entered upon Uthman and the Qur’an was in his lap."
"30805","(30805) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: One of the characteristics of the ancients was to look at the Qur’an, and Al-Ahnaf ibn Qais was When he was alone, he looked at the Qur’an."
"30806","(30806) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Suriyat Al-Rabi’, she said: Al-Rabi’ used to recite from the Qur’an. So when a person enters, he covers him and says: This man does not see that I read about it every hour."
"30807","(30807) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, saying: Abraham was reading from the Qur’an, and when a person entered upon him, He covered it and said: This one does not think that I read it every hour."
"30808","(30808) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: I will recite my part, or Partial year, while I was lying on my bed."
"30809","(30809) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, he said: I heard my father. He said: I caught Fadalah bin Servants of the Qur’an until it is completed."
"30810","(30810) Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Hilal told us, he said: Abu Salih Al-Uqaili told us, he said: Abu Al-Ala’ Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir reads from the Qur’an until he faints."
"30811","(30811) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, who said: I saw Talhi reading from the Qur’an."
"30812","(30812) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim who disliked to say: The reading of so-and-so and he said: As So-and-so reads."
"30813","(30813) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Qur’an was sent down in a sentence from the heavens. From the highest heaven to the lowest heaven in Ramadan, so if God wanted to happen something, He caused it to happen."
"30814","(30814) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: The Torah was revealed when Ramadan was empty, and it was revealed The Qur’an is twenty-four."
"30815","(30815) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, he said: All the books were revealed. The night of the twenty-fourth of Ramadan."
"30816","(30816) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Ammar bin Ruzaiq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Hassan bin Abi Al-Ashras, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, regarding his saying: Indeed, We sent it down in the Night of Decree. He said: It was delivered to Gabriel. For Laylat Al-Qadr in its entirety, he was placed in the House of Glory and then he made its descent."
"30817","(30817) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: He who heard Abu Al-Aliyah mentioned informed me, on the authority of my father. He said: The Scrolls of Abraham were revealed on the first night of Ramadan, and the Psalms were revealed on six, and the Gospel on eighteen. And the Qur’an is in twenty-four verses."
"30818","(30818) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Wasil bin Hayyan, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: How will you do if he is taken captive according to the Book of God and taken away with him? He said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, how about what is in the insides of men? He said: God sends a pleasant fragrance, so I was satisfied with everything. A believer"
"30819","(30819) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abdul-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Shaddad bin Maqil, he said: Abdullah said: This The Qur’an which is before you is about to be taken away from you. He said: I said: How can it be taken away from us when God has established it in Our hearts and We confirmed it in Our Qur’an. He said: It will be spread upon him in one night, and He will take away what is in the hearts and go away. What is in the Qur’an? And the people become poor from it. Then he recited {And if We willed, We would surely carry that which We have revealed to you}"
"30820","(30820) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: There will be people from my nation who will recite the Qur’an, who will leave Islam just as an arrow leaves a target. (Ibn Majah 171, Ahmed 256)"
"30821","(30821) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yusir bin Amr, he said: I asked Sahil bin Hanif: What Did you hear the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mention these Kharijites? He said: I heard him, and he pointed with his hand towards the east: From there will emerge a people who will recite the Qur’an with their tongues, and no one will go beyond it. Their throats, they will be thrown away from debt as an arrow leaves an arrow. (Bukhari 6934 and Muslim 750)"
"30822","(30822) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Qur’a bin Khalid Al-Sadusi narrated to me, saying: Abu Al-Zubayr narrated to me, on the authority of Jabir. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There will come a people who recite the Qur’an but it will not go beyond their throats. Religion is like an arrow that shoots from the target on top of it. (Muslim 142. Ahmad 353)"
"30823","(30823) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: At the end of time there will emerge a people of young teeth and foolish dreams who will recite the Qur’an but it will not go beyond their throats. (Tirmidhi 2188 and Ahmad 404)"
"30824","(30824) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Azraq bin Qais, on the authority of Sharik bin Shihab Al-Harithi. On the authority of Abu Barza, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A people will emerge from the East who recite the Qur’an without It goes beyond their collars and they are devoid of religion[corrupt] Just as an arrow shoots out of an archer, they will not be returned to it. (Ahmad 421, Hakim 146)"
"30825","(30825) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ziyad bin Labid, he said: He mentioned The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said something and said: And that was at the time of the disappearance of knowledge. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, how? Knowledge is disappearing, and we read the Qur’an, and we teach it to our children, and our children read it to their children, until this day. Resurrection. He said: May your mother Ziyad be bereaved of you. I wish I could see you as one of the wisest men in Medina, or not one of these Jews. Christians read the Torah and the Gospel, but do not act on anything that is in them. (Ahmad 1601. Tabarani 5291)"
"30826","(30826) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abu Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He who deems unlawful what is unlawful for him does not believe in the Qur’an. (Abdullah bin Hamad 1003)"
"30827","(30827) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Sinan, on the authority of Abu Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Suhayb, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. In the same way (Tirmidhi 2918)"
"30828","(30828) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, who said: I said to Ubayy: Ibn Masoud does not write. Al-Mu'awwidhatain in the Qur’an, and he said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about them, and he said: I was told, so I said: and he said: Ubayy: We say as we were told. (Bukhari 4976 and Ibn Hibban 4429)"
"30829","(30829) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The two exorcists are from the Qur’an."
"30830","(30830) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, in a similar manner."
"30831","(30831) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: I saw Abd Allah narrating The two who seek refuge from the Qur’an, and he said: Do not mix in it what is not from it. (Ahmad 1291. Tabarani 9148)"
"30832","(30832) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I said to Al-Aswad: What are they from the Qur’an? He said: Yes, meaning the two seek refuge."
"30833","(30833) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Rafi’, who said: I heard Suleiman the client of Ali’s mother, Mujahid used to hate reciting Al-Mu'awwidhat alone, to the point of adding another surah with it."
"30834","(30834) Muttalib bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salim, who said: I said to Abu Ja`far: Ibn Masoud wiped out the Mu’awwidhatin from... The Qur’an, and he said: Read from it."
"30835","(30835) Affan told us, he said: Abu Hilal told us, he said: Mansour Al-Qassab told us, he said: I asked Al-Hasan, I said: O Abu Sa’id. Should I recite the Mu'awwidhatin in the Fajr prayer? He said: Yes, if you wish, two blessed and good surahs."
"30836","(30836) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mu’awiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr, on the authority of his father On the authority of Uqba bin Amir, that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the Mu’awwidhatin. He said: So the Messenger of God believed in them. May God bless him and grant him peace in the Fajr prayer. (Abu Ali 1728, Hakim 240)"
"30837","(30837) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, on the authority of Sulaiman ibn Musa, on the authority of Uqba ibn Amir, who said: I was with The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on a journey, and when dawn came he called the call to prayer and said the Iqama, then he made me stand on his right and recited “Bal-Mu’awwidhatin” When he left, he said: How did you see? I said: I have seen, O Messenger of God. He said: So recite them whenever you sleep and whenever you get up."
"30838","(30838) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Masoud did not write. Al-Mu'awwidhatayn."
"30839","(30839) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said, it is the last surah that was revealed in its entirety. An innocence, and the last verse revealed in the Qur’an: {They ask you for a fatwa. Say, “Allah gives you a fatwa concerning the truth}"
"30840","(30840) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Suddi, who said: The last verse to be revealed was: {And fear the Day Therein you will be returned to God. Then every soul will be paid in full what it has earned, and they will not be wronged.}"
"30841","(30841) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Atiya Al-Awfi, he said: The last verse. It was revealed: {And fear the Day in which you will be returned to Allah; then every soul will be fully paid what it has earned, and they will not be wronged}"
"30842","(30842) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Bashir narrated to us, he said: Malik, on the authority of Abul Safar, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The last verse. It was revealed: {They ask you for a fatwa. Say, “Allah gives you a fatwa concerning the matter}"
"30843","(30843) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The first surah that was revealed: {Read. In the name of your Lord who created} then (n)"
"30844","(30844) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The last verse to be revealed In the Qur’an: {They ask you for a fatwa. Say, “Allah gives you a fatwa concerning the matter}."
"30845","(30845) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Ubaid ibn Umair saying: The first thing that was revealed was From the Qur’an: (Read in the name of your Lord who created) then (n)"
"30846","(30846) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Abu Raja’, who said: I learned from Abu Musa: {Recite in the name of your Lord who created} It is the first surah that was revealed to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"30847","(30847) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz did not make it obligatory except for those who recited The Qur’an, he said: My father was one of those who read the Qur’an and it was made obligatory for him."
"30848","(30848) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yasir ibn Amr, who said: Sa’d wanted to catch up with someone He recited the Qur’an to two thousand people, and Omar wrote to him: You will be given a reward according to the Book of God."
"30849","(30849) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: People collected the Qur’an until they reached their number, so Abu Musa wrote to Omar. Therefore, Omar wrote to him: Some people narrated to him more than others, and perhaps some of those who read it will do better than others. His last recitation is the last of what he has done."
"30850","(30850) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali, that he disliked the Qur’an being written in The small Qur’an."
"30851","(30851) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali, with something similar except that he said: The Qur’an"
"30852","(30852) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It used to be said: Magnify the Qur’an. Meaning: Enlarge the Qur’an."
"30853","(30853) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Shaddad al-Azdi narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Sulaiman al-Abdi, on the authority of Abi Hakimah Al-Abdi said: We used to write the Qur’an in Kufa, and Ali would pass by us while we were writing, and he would stand up. So he says: How beautiful is your pen? He said: So I left some of it, then I wrote, and he said: Thus, enlighten what God has enlightened."
"30854","(30854) Waki’ told us, he said: Ali bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abu Hakimah Al-Abdi, he said: We used to write The copies of the Qur’an are in Kufa, and someone will pass by us and some people will look and admire our handwriting and say: Thus, enlighten what God has enlightened."
"30855","(30855) Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he disliked it being said: Mushaf."
"30856","(30856) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Abd Khair, who said: Ali said: May God have mercy on Abu Bakr. He was the first to combine the two tablets."
"30857","(30857) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: When Abu Bakr was appointed successor, he sat Ali was in his house, and it was said to Abu Bakr, and he sent to him: I disliked your caliphate. He said: No, I did not dislike your caliphate, but The Qur’an was adding to it, so when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, I was required to not wear anything except for prayer until He collected it for the people, so Abu Bakr said: Yes, as I saw it."
"30858","(30858) Qubaysah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Sa’sa’a, he said: The first to He combined the two tablets and inherited Al-Kalala Abu Bakr."
"30859","(30859) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, he said: My father said: If you Your copies of the Qur’an and the adornment of your mosques, for God’s will be upon you."
"30860","(30860) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Qutbah bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he saw a Qur’an being decorated and said: You will deceive thieves with it."
"30861","(30861) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked to have the Qur’an unraveled."
"30862","(30862) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: Abdullah was brought a Qur’an that had been decorated with gold, and he said: Abdullah: The best thing with which the Qur’an is decorated is its recitation in truth."
"30863","(30863) Abduh told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, he said: I said to Abu Razin: I have a Qur’an that I want to seal with gold. He said: Do not add to it anything of the affairs of this world, whether small or large."
"30864","(30864) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja`far, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abi Sa`id, who said: Abu Dharr said: If you Your mosques and your ornaments of your Qur’an, then the Lord will be upon you."
"30865","(30865) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Abu Imamah, that He hated to change the Qur’an."
"30866","(30866) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I came to Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla turned to Tabar and said: Would you please give him a copy of the Qur’an?"
"30867","(30867) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: There is no harm in opening the Qur’an."
"30868","(30868) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, that He hated tithing in the Qur’an."
"30869","(30869) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, that he disliked tithing in the Qur’an, and that Something else is written in it."
"30870","(30870) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"30871","(30871) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he disliked it being written as ‘ash’ir, or Tafseel, and he says: Surah Al-Baqarah, and he says: The Surah in which the cows are mentioned."
"30872","(30872) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he disliked tithing in the Qur’an."
"30873","(30873) Abduh told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, he said: I said to Abu Razin: I have a Qur’an that I want to seal with gold. At the beginning of the surah, he wrote such-and-such verses, and Abu Razin said: Do not add anything to it from the affairs of this world, nor say anything. A lot"
"30874","(30874) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, that he hated the conquests and the tenths that There is a qāf and a kaaf in it."
"30875","(30875) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked tithing in the Qur’an."
"30876","(30876) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked the dots and the ending of a surah like this. And so on"
"30877","(30877) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of a sheikh, on the authority of Abdullah, that he saw a mistake in the Qur’an and rubbed it, And he said: Do not mix it with anything else."
"30878","(30878) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, that he disliked tithing in the Qur’an, and that Something else is written in it."
"30879","(30879) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Habhab, that Abu Al-Aliyah used to hate him. Al-Awashirah"
"30880","(30880) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Abu al-Za````, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Strip the Qur’an, and do not mix with it what is not part of it."
"30881","(30881) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: Strip the Qur’an."
"30882","(30882) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It used to be said: Strip the Qur’an."
"30883","(30883) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: I said to Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad: What prevents you from Have you asked as Abraham asked? He said: He said: It was said: They stripped the Qur’an."
"30884","(30884) Sa’l bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid al-Tawil, on the authority of Mu’awiyah bin Qurayh, on the authority of Abu al-Mughirah, he said: He read A man was with Ibn Masoud and said: I seek refuge in the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing from the accursed Satan. Then Abdullah said: Strip the Qur’an."
"30885","(30885) Malik narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Habhab, that Abu Al-Aliyah said: Strip The Qur’an."
"30886","(30886) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Ziyad bin Mikhraq, on the authority of Abu Kinana, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari He said: It is a matter of reverence to God to honor the bearer of the Qur’an who is not exaggerated in it, nor one who is unjust about it. (Abu Dawud 4810, Bayhaqi 163)"
"30887","(30887) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by May God’s peace and blessings be upon Bilal while he was reciting part of this surah and part of this surah, and he said: I passed by you, Bilal, and you were She recited from this surah and from this surah, and he said: By my father, O Messenger of God, I wanted to mix the perfume With perfume: He said: Recite the surah in the same way."
"30888","(30888) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Muadh used to mix some of this surah with some of this surah. He was told, and he said: Do you see me mixing in it something that is not part of it?"
"30889","(30889) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zaid bin Yatha’i, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, passed by Bilal, then mentioned something similar to the hadith of Hatim."
"30890","(30890) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muhammad was asked about the one who recited Who is here and who is here? He said: Let him beware. He will not commit a great sin and he will not realize it."
"30891","(30891) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to dislike reciting even two surahs. He concludes the afterlife, then begins the afterlife."
"30892","(30892) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Al-Walid bin Juma’ narrated to me, he said: A man narrated to me, that he is the mother of the people. With confusion, Khalid bin Al-Walid, then he recited from various surahs, then he turned to us when he left and said: We have been distracted by jihad, rather than learning. The Qur’an."
"30893","(30893) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hudhayl, he said: They were They hate to recite some verses and leave others."
"30894","(30894) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, that he disliked that He says: Such-and-such verse was omitted."
"30895","(30895) Affan told us, he said: Saeed bin Zaid told us, he said: Amr bin Malik told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawzai, he said: Moving the stones is easier for the hypocrite than reciting the Qur’an."
"30896","(30896) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, he said: Zayd bin Ali told me, he said: I passed by Abu Ja’far. And he was in his house and he was saying: O God, forgive me with the Qur’an, O God, have mercy on me with the Qur’an, O God, guide me with the Qur’an, O God. Bless me with the Qur’an."
"30897","(30897) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Bakr said: O Messenger God, how old are you? He said: Hud, the reality, and the mursalat have turned gray, and they began to wonder, and behold, the sun was rounded. (Abu Ali 102)"
"30898","(30898) Ibn Mahdi and Qubaisa told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zur, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: They say Surah Al-Tawbah, which is the surah of torment, means acquittal."
"30899","(30899) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: His innocence continues to be revealed to the point that even the companions of it are afraid of it. Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she was called the scandalous one."
"30900","(30900) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, he said: Abdullah said: The length is like a torah, The verses of the Qur’an are like the Gospel, the two verses are like the Psalms, and the rest of the Qur’an is virtue."
"30901","(30901) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr: {And indeed We wrote in the Psalms} He said: The Qur’an and the Torah And the Gospel."
"30902","(30902) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi: {And We have written in the Psalms after the Remembrance} He said: Psalms. David after mentioning Moses."
"30903","(30903) Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: I heard Abu Imran al-Junai, he said: Abdullah bin Rabah told us, He said: I heard Ka'b say: Open the Torah, open Surah Al-An'am, and the conclusion of the Torah is the conclusion of Surah Hud."
"30904","(30904) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: If you doubt The ya’ and the ta’, so make it a ya’, for the Qur’an is a reminder, so remember it."
"30905","(30905) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Abu Nizar Al-Muradi narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Misra, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Salami, he said: If you differ in the Qur’an as to a ya’, or a ta’, then make it a ya’, for the Qur’an was revealed to The letter"
"30906","(30906) Muawiyah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: If you debate about the Qur’an There is a ya’, or a ta’, so make it a ya’ and mention the Qur’an, for it is a reminder."
"30907","(30907) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’dah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: The Qur’an is a remembrance. So remember Him."
"30908","(30908) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: Whenever the boy spoke eloquently, From the children of Abdul Muttalib, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught him these seven verses: {Praise be to God who has not taken A son, and he had no partner in the kingdom, and he had no guardian. He was submissive and arrogant.}"
"30909","(30909) Omar bin Saad Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr: My father brought me to Sa’id bin Jubayr when I was young, and he said: Learn. This Quran?"
"30910","(30910) Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They were They hate to teach their children the Qur’an until they understand."
"30911","(30911) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom God has given wealth, and he spends it with it during the night and during the day, and a man God taught him the Qur’an, and he recites it all night and day. (Bukhari 5025. Muslim 558)"
"30912","(30912) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Yazid bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Saeed said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom God has given the Qur’an, then It is recited at times of the night and during the day, and the man says: If God had given me the like of what He gave so-and-so, I would have done the same as he does, and another man God gave him money, and he spends it on it. Then the man says: If God had given me the like of what He gave so-and-so, I would have done the same as he does. (Ahmad 479, Abu Ali 1080)"
"30913","(30913) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Abdullah said: (ham) is a debaj. The Qur’an."
"30914","(30914) Ja’far ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Sa’d ibn Ibrahim, who said: The whales were called brides."
"30915","(30915) Muhammad bin Bishr and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ma’an bin Abdul Rahman, who said: Abdullah said: If it falls In the family of Ham, I found elegant gardens in which I dressed up."
"30916","(30916) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu al-Darda`, who said: He passed by him while he was building my son. prostrating and said: What is this? He said: This is for the family of Ham."
"30917","(30917) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Shibl, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I showed the Qur’an to him. Ibn Abbas three times."
"30918","(30918) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Salih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I showed the Qur’an to Ibn Abbas from its Fatihah. To its conclusion, there are three pauses, and I stop at each verse."
"30919","(30919) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to recite the Qur’an once every Ramadan, except for the year in which he died, for it was presented to him twice. In the presence of Abdullah, he witnessed what was abrogated from it and what was changed. (Ahmad 362, Abu Ali 255)"
"30920","(30920) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to present the book to Gabriel every Ramadan. The month in which he was destroyed, he was exposed to it twice."
"30921","(30921) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ali narrated to us, saying: I heard my father saying: I retained his surplus. Ibn Ubaid recited the Qur’an until he finished it."
"30922","(30922) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah He said: The recitation that was presented to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year in which he died. People read it today."
"30923","(30923) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Gabriel used to present The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the Qur’an once every year during Ramadan, and when it was the year in which it was revealed, upon him twice.\n(Bukhari 3424, Muslim 1905)"
"30924","(30924) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Zakaria bin Abi Zayed narrated to us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of Fatima, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to present the Qur’an to Gabriel every year. Once upon a time, when the year in which he was arrested came, he proposed to him twice."
"30925","(30925) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: For all Something is a core thing, and indeed the core is the detailed Qur’an."
"30926","(30926) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Misra, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: Salman said To Zaid bin Sohan: How would you be if the Qur’an and the Sultan fought? He said: Then I will be with the Qur’an. He said: Yes, Al-Zuwayd: Then you are."
"30927","(30927) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: The Qur’an fights. And the Sultan said: Then the Sultan steps on the mouth of the Qur’an, so what a calamity, what a calamity, what a curse you will escape from."
"30928","(30928) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Masoud said: A man came to Ibn Masoud and said: O Abu Abdullah bin Masoud, teach me useful comprehensive words. He said, “Worship God, and do not associate anything with Him, and you will cease to exist with the Qur’an wherever it departed.”"
"30929","(30929) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Jabala bin Suhaim, on the authority of Aamir bin Matar, he said: I was with Hudhayfah and he said: How are you, Aamir ibn Matar? If people take a path and the Qur’an is a path, which of them will you be with? So I said: With the Qur’an, will I live with it, or die? He said: Then you."
"30930","(30930) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: A man came to Ibn Masoud and said: Teach me some words. Compounds of benefit. He said: Worship God, and do not associate anything with Him, and they will disappear with the Qur’an wherever they disappear."
"30931","(30931) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah’s companions were the ones who gave fatwas. And they recite the Qur’an: Alqamiya, Al-Aswad, Ubaidah, Masruq, Amr bin Shurahbil, and Al-Harith bin Qais."
"30932","(30932) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah used to recite the Qur’an to us in The mosque, then the people sit still after it."
"30933","(30933) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Humaid narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Ishaq saying: Read Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Salami The Qur’an has been in the mosque for forty years."
"30934","(30934) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: May God bless him and grant him peace: Recite the Qur’an to me. I said: I recite it to you and to you it was revealed. He said: I long to hear it from someone. Other than me, he said: So the women recited to him until she reached: {But how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you to these Shahid} I raised my head, or a man next to me winked at me, so I raised my head and saw his eyes watering.\n(Bukhari 4582, Muslim 551)"
"30935","(30935) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yassaf, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace, similar to the hadith of Al-A’mash. (Ahmad 374, Abu Ali 5128)"
"30936","(30936) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace And he greeted him, and he said to him: Read, so he opened Surah An-Nasa’ until he reached the words of God Almighty: {But how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness? And We have brought you as a witness against these. He said: Then the eyes of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought tears to his eyes. He said: That is enough for you.\n(Nasa’i 8077 and Tabarani 8459)"
"30937","(30937) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Ubayy ibn Ka’b say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have been commanded to show you the Qur’an. He said: Your Lord has named me for you. He said: Yes. He said: I refuse. {By the grace of God and His mercy, so let them rejoice in this. It is better than what they gather}"
"30938","(30938) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: It was said to Abdullah: So-and-so recites the Qur’an backwards, Abdullah said: That is the upside down of the heart."
"30939","(30939) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Harun bin Antar, on the authority of his father, he said, I asked Ibn Abbas: Which work is better? He said: The remembrance of God is the greatest, and no people sit in a house in which they deal with the Book of God among themselves and discuss it without The angels overshadowed them with their wings, and they were guests of God as long as they remained there until they passed away in a different hadith. (Dharmi 356)"
"30940","(30940) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Raja’, who said: I asked Muhammad about the points of the Qur’an? He said: I fear that they will add to the letters, or omit them."
"30941","(30941) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Kharijiya, on the authority of Khalid, who said: I saw Ibn Sirin reading from a dotted Qur’an."
"30942","(30942) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated dots."
"30943","(30943) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hudhali, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in dotting it with red."
"30944","(30944) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, or someone else, who said: I saw Ibn Sirin reading from a dotted Qur’an."
"30945","(30945) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: It was One day, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was prominent among the people, and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of God, what is faith? He said: Faith is that you believe in God, His angels, His books, the meeting with Him, and His messengers, and believe in the final resurrection. He said: O Messenger of God, What is Islam? He said: That you worship God, and do not associate anything with Him, and perform the prescribed prayers, and pay the obligatory zakat, and fast. Ramadan, he said: O Messenger of God, what is ihsan? He said: To worship God as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, then He sees you. (Muslim 5. Ahmad 426)"
"30946","(30946) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Jamra, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the delegation of Abd al-Qais came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: From the delegation, or from the people. They said: Rabi’i. He said: We welcome the people, or the delegation, without any shame or regret. They said: O Messenger of God, we are coming to you from a far-off misfortune. And between us and you is this neighborhood of the infidels of Mudar, and we are not able to come to you except in the sacred month, so let us pass. A decisive matter that We inform of those behind us, with which we will enter Paradise. He said: So he commanded them to do four and forbade them to do four: He commanded them to do four. By faith in God alone, and he said: Do you know what faith in God is? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: This is evidence that there is no god. Except God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, and to establish prayer, and to pay zakat, and to fast Ramadan, and to give a fifth of the spoils, and he said: Preserve it and tell those behind you about it. (Bukhari 87. Muslim 24)"
"30947","(30947) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Atiyya, the client of Banu Amir, on the authority of Zayd bin Bishr al-Saksaki said: I came to Medina and entered upon Abdullah bin Omar, and a man from the people of Iraq came to him. He said: O Abdullah, why do you perform Hajj and Umrah and abandon the campaign for the sake of God? He said: Woe to you, for faith is built on five things: You worship God, perform prayer, pay zakat, perform Hajj to the House, and fast Ramadan. He said: He returned it to him, and said: O Abdullah, You worship God, perform prayer, pay zakat, perform Hajj to the House, and fast Ramadan. He said: He returned it to him, and said: O Abdullah, You worship God, perform prayer, pay zakat, perform Hajj to the House, and fast Ramadan. Likewise, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: May God bless him and grant him peace."
"30948","(30948) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, Umar said: There are four things that are binding on faith: prayer and zakat. And jihad and honesty."
"30949","(30949) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salla, who said: Hudhayfy said: Islam, eight. Ashram: Prayer is a share, zakat is a share, jihad is a share, fasting in Ramadan is a share, enjoining what is right is a share, and prohibition is a share. From evil there is an arrow, and Islam is an arrow, and he who has no arrow has failed."
"30950","(30950) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I heard Urwah ibn al-Nazzal narrating on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: We returned with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from his campaign against Tabuk, and when I saw it empty, I said: O Messenger of God, “Inform me of an act that will make me enter Paradise.” He said: “Abominable. You have asked about a great thing, and it is easy for whomever God makes easy.” Ali: Perform the obligatory prayers, pay the obligatory zakat, and meet God, not associating anything with Him. Should I direct you to the head of The matter, its pillar, and its peak? As for the head of the matter, Islam is whoever embraces Islam. As for its pillar, it is prayer, and as for its peak and height, it is jihad in the path of God."
"30951","(30951) Ubaidah bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Maymun bin Abi Shabib, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, He said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the raid on Tabuk. Then he mentioned something similar."
"30952","(30952) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of a man from Banu Asad, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There are four things that no man will find the taste of faith until he believes in them: There is no god but God alone, and that The Messenger of God sent me with the truth and that he was dead, then he will be resurrected after death and he believes in destiny in its entirety.\n(Tirmidhi 2145. Ahmad 133)"
"30953","(30953) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He came A Bedouin went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Peace be upon you, O boy of Banu Abdul Muttalib, and he said: And upon you, and he said: I am a man from your maternal uncles from the Banu Saad bin Bakr, and I am the messenger of my people to you and their envoy, and I am asking you and seeking you. I asked you, and I appealed to you, so I escalated my appeal to you. He said: Take it, brother of Banu Sa’d. He said: Who created you and He is the Creator Who before you and He is the Creator of those after you? He said: God. He said: I called you to do that. Did He send you? He said: Yes. He said: Who created the seven heavens and the seven earths and distributed the sustenance between them? He said: God. He said: I called upon you to do that. Did He send you? He said: Yes, he said: For we found in your book and your messengers commanded us to pray five prayers day and night. Because of its appointed times, so I appealed to you about that. Did he command you to do so? He said: Yes, he said: We found it in your book and your messengers commanded us to take from our wealth and return it to our poor. So I urged you to do that, or did he command you to do that? He said: Yes, then he said: As for the fifth, I will not ask you about it, and I have no interest in it. He then said: By the One who sent you with the truth I will do it and whoever of my people obeys me. Then he returned and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed at you until his molars became visible. Then he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, if he speaks the truth, they will certainly enter Paradise."
"30954","(30954) Shababah bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: We had We were forbidden to ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about something. We were astonished that a man would come from his family. The wise deserter asked him while we were listening, then a man from the desert came and said: O Muhammad, your messenger came to us and claimed Indeed, God has sent you, and he said: He has spoken the truth. He said: Who created the heavens? He said: God. He said: Who created the earth? He said: God. He said: Who erected these mountains? He said: God. He said: By the One who created the heavens and created the earth and set up the mountains, did God send you? He said: Yes. He said: And your Messenger claimed that we are obligated to perform five prayers in our day and night. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: By the One whom God has sent you, he commanded you to do this. He said: Yes: He said: And he claimed. Your Messenger, that we owe zakat on our wealth. He said he spoke the truth. He said: By the one whom God has sent you, he commanded you to do this. He said yes. He said: Your Messenger claimed that we are obligated to fast during the month of Ramadan. Ramadan in our Sunnah. He said: He has spoken the truth. He said: By the One who created the heavens and created the earth and set up the mountains, did God command you to do this? He said: Yes. He said: Your Messenger claimed that Hajj is on us for whoever is able to make a way to it. He said he spoke the truth. He said: By the One who created the heavens and created The earth and the erection of the mountains. Has God commanded you to do this? He said: Yes, then he turned and said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not add anything to it, nor will I subtract anything from it, so the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: If he speaks the truth, he will enter Paradise. (Muslim 41. Tirmidhi 619)"
"30955","(30955) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ali ibn Masadi, he said: His leaders narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Islam is open and faith is in the heart. Then he pointed to his chest with his hand: Piety is here. Piety is here. (Ahmad 134, Bazzar 20)"
"30956","(30956) Mus’ab bin Al-Miqdam told us, he said: Abu Hilal told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace. There is no faith for one who has no trust. (Ahmad 1351; Ibn Hibban 194)"
"30957","(30957) Abu Asama told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr Ibn Hind Al-Jamli, he said: Ali said: Faith begins as a white dot in the heart. As faith increases, it becomes whiter until the entire heart becomes white. Hypocrisy creates a black dot in the heart. As the hypocrisy increases, it becomes darker until the entire heart becomes black. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you were to separate the heart of a believer, you would find it white; but if you were to separate the heart of a hypocrite You would have found him black-hearted."
"30958","(30958) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Misra, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: Abd said: God: Indeed, a man commits a sin and a black spot is stained in his heart, then he commits the sin and another dark spot is stained on his heart. His heart becomes the color of black sheep."
"30959","(30959) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Hisham said, on the authority of his father: The trustworthiness of a servant was never diminished unless it diminished. His faith"
"30960","(30960) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: Faith is a hope."
"30961","(30961) Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Bishr ibn On the Day of Sacrifice, Suhaim Al-Ghafari will call out to the people, “No one will enter Paradise except a believing soul.”"
"30962","(30962) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, who said: Do not be deceived by anyone’s prayer, nor Fasting. Whoever wishes may fast, and whoever wishes may pray. He who has no security has no religion."
"30963","(30963) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Khutmiy, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Umar bin Habib bin Khamashiya said: Faith increases and decreases. It was said to him: What is its increase and what is its decrease? He said: If If we remember Him and fear Him, that is His increase, and if we are negligent and forgetful and neglectful, that is His decrease."
"30964","(30964) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to say: Oh God, do not take away from me the faith you have given me."
"30965","(30965) Hammad bin Maqil told us, on the authority of Ghalib, on the authority of Bakr, who said: If I were asked about the best people of this mosque, they would say: You bear witness that he is a believer with complete faith, free of hypocrisy. I did not bear witness, and if I had testified, I would have testified that he is in Paradise, even if I was asked about a man, the most evil or wicked, the suspicion of Abu Bakr, a man, and they said: We bear witness that he is a hypocrite, complete with hypocrisy, innocent of I do not bear witness to faith, and if I had testified, I would have witnessed that it will be in Hell."
"30966","(30966) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Fudail bin Ghazwan told us, he said: Othman bin Abi Safiyy told us. Al-Ansari, he said: Abdullah bin Abbas said to one of his boys: Shall I not marry you off? There is no slave who commits adultery without God taking light from him. Faith"
"30967","(30967) Suleiman bin Harb told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: The adulterer does not commit adultery when he commits adultery while he is a believer, and he does not commit theft when he steals while he is a believer. (Bazzar 112)"
"30968","(30968) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Thalabi, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, who said: The Messenger who asked narrated to me. Abdullah bin Masoud said: I ask you by God, do you know that people were in the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? There are three types: the believer in secret and the believer in publicity, the believer in secret is a disbeliever in publicity, and the believer in publicity is an unbeliever. The secret, he said: Then Abdullah said: Oh God, yes. He said: So I adjure you by God: Which of them have you been? He said: Oh God, the believer of the secret. A believer in publicity, I am a believer. Abu Ishaq said: Then I met Abdullah bin Maqil, and I said: Some of the righteous people are criticizing me. To say: I am a believer. Abdullah bin Maqil said: You have failed and lost if you are not a believer."
"30969","(30969) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Muslim Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, he said: And what Is one of you to say: I am a believer? By God, if he were telling the truth, God would not punish him for his truthfulness, but if he were a liar, he would not punish him for his truthfulness. A form of disbelief has entered upon him that is more severe for him than a lie."
"30970","(30970) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: A man said to him: Are you a believer? He said: I hope"
"30971","(30971) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Umair. Al-Zubaidi said: The plague struck Syria, so Muadh stood up in Homs and addressed them, and said: \n This plague is the mercy of your Lord and the supplication of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the death of the righteous before you. Oh God. Swear to the family of Muadh their fullest share of it. He said: When he came down from the pulpit, someone came to him and said: Abd al-Rahman bin Muadh has been injured. He said: To Allah we belong, and to Him we shall return. He said: Then he set off towards him. He said: When Abdul-Rahman saw him coming, he said: Indeed, the truth is from Your Lord, so do not be of those who doubt. He said: Then he said: O my son, you will find me, God willing, among the patient ones. He said: So the family of Muadh died, man by man. Until Muadh was the last of them, he said: Then he was injured, so Al-Harith bin Umairah Al-Zubaidi came to him, he said: Then Muadh fainted. He fainted. He said: Then Muadh woke up and Al-Harith was crying. He said: Then Muadh said: What makes you cry? He said: So he said: Cry over the knowledge that will be buried with you. He said: So he said: If you are inevitably seeking knowledge, then seek it from Abdullah bin Masoud, and from Awaimer Abu Darda, and from Salman Al-Farisi, he said: And beware of the misstep of the scholar, he said: I said: How can I, may God bless you, know it? He said: Indeed, truth has a light by which it is known. He said: Then Muadh died and Al-Harith went out seeking Abd. Allah ibn Masoud in Kufa, he said: Then he went to his door, and at the door was a group of Abdullah’s companions talking, he said: Then the conversation spread between them until they said: O Syrian, are you a believer? He said: Yes, so they said: Who are the people of Paradise? He said: So he said: I have sins that I do not know what God will do about them. If I had known that they have been forgiven, I would have informed you that I am one of The people of Paradise. He said: While they were in that state, Abdullah revolted against them. They said to him: Are you not surprised at this our brother? The Syrian man claims that he is a believer, but he does not claim that he is one of the people of Paradise. He said: Then Abdullah said: If I had said one of them, I would have followed it. The other one, he said: Al-Harith said: {To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return} May God’s prayers and peace be upon Mu’adh, he said: Woe to you, and from Mu’adh, he said: Mu’adh ibn A mountain. He said: What did he say? He said: Beware of the misstep of a scholar, so swear by God that it is your fault, O Ibn Masoud. And faith is only that we believe in God. And His angels, and His books, and His messengers, and the Last Day, and the Garden and the Fire, and the Resurrection, and the Balance, and indeed we have sins, and we do not know what they are. God has done something about her. If we had known that she had forgiven us, we would have said: We are among the people of Paradise. Then Abdullah said: You have spoken the truth, by God. It was an earthquake on my part.\n(Abu Dawud 4596, Hakim 460)"
"30972","(30972) Musab bin Al-Miqdam told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, he said: Abu Zumail told me, on the authority of Malik Ibn Marthad al-Zamani, on the authority of his father, said: Abu Dharr said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: What can save a servant? From the Fire, and he said: Faith in God. He said: I said: O Prophet of God, or with faith there is action, and he said: Submissiveness to what God has provided you, or He is satisfied with what God has provided for him."
"30973","(30973) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Umm Muhammad, that a man said to Aisha: What is faith? She said: Should I explain or beautify? He said: No, but rather beautify it. She said: Whoever makes me happy with my good and whose bad makes me unhappy is a believer.\n(Tirmidhi 2145, Ahmad 446)"
"30974","(30974) Muhammad bin Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The believer is not one who stabs, nor curses, nor is he obscene, nor is he obscene. (Tirmidhi 1977 and Ahmad 404)"
"30975","(30975) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhail, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, on the authority of Sa’d, He said: The believer is marked for all good deeds except betrayal and lying."
"30976","(30976) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The believer covers all good deeds other than betrayal and lying."
"30977","(30977) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, saying: It was narrated to us on the authority of Abu Imamah. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The believer is willing to accept everything except betrayal and lying."
"30978","(30978) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: At the end of time there will be temptations like pieces of a dark night. A man will become a believer in the morning and an unbeliever in the evening. He will be a believer in the evening and become a disbeliever in the morning."
"30979","(30979) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Hilal ibn Abi Maimunah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Al-Hakam Al-Sulami, who said: I had a maid who took care of sheep. In front of Uhud and the inner part, so I looked at it one day and behold, the wolf had gone with a sheep from its sheep. He said: And I A man from the children of Adam is sorry as they are sorry, but I made a mint, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he honored That is on me, so I said, O Messenger of God, shall I not free her? He said: Bring her to me, and he said to her: Is God easy? She said: In the heavens. He said: Who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of God. He said: Free her, for she is a believer. (Muslim 33. Abu Dawud 927)"
"30980","(30980) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Hikam Yarifu’ah, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Indeed, my mother has a believing slave. I have a black, foreign neck. He said: Bring it. He said: Do you bear witness that there is no god but God and that he is the Messenger of God? She said: Yes, he said: So free her. (Bazzar 13. Tabarani 13369)"
"30981","(30981) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The likeness of a believer is like a plant that the wind never ceases to tilt, and the believer never ceases to move it. A calamity will befall him, and the likeness of the disbeliever is like a cedar tree that does not shake until it reaps. (Muslim 2163. Tirmidhi 2866)"
"30982","(30982) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: Ibn Ka’b bin told me Malik, on the authority of Abu Ka’b, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The likeness of a believer is like the raw material of crops warmed by the scent. You grate it once and adjust it another time until it becomes irritated, and the likeness of the disbeliever is like rice that is useless on its root. Anything is fine for her, even if she suffers from pain once. (Bukhari 5643, Muslim 59)"
"30983","(30983) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Bashir bin Nayk, on the authority of Abi He saw, he said: The example of a weak believer is like the raw material of the crop, the wind makes it bitter and makes it bitter, he said: I said: The strong believer said: Like a palm tree that yields its fruit at all times in its shade, and the wind does not move it."
"30984","(30984) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The likeness of a believer is like that of a bee: it eats good and produces good."
"30985","(30985) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Buraid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The believer is to the believer like a building, some of which support others. (Bukhari 4811 Muslim 1999)"
"30986","(30986) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Amr ibn Sharhabeel, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, Ammar was filled with faith to the point of his being."
"30987","(30987) Othman bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hani bin Hani, who said: We were sitting at Ali, so Ammar entered and said: Welcome to the perfumed one. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Ammar is full of faith. Oh my God (Ibn Majah 147)"
"30988","(30988) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Zakaria told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan say: Faith It is not through admiration, nor through wishful thinking, but rather faith is what is established in the heart and confirmed by actions. (Ibn Adi 2290)"
"30989","(30989) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that He said to his servants: Whoever among you wants to have sexual intercourse, We will marry him to him. No adulterer among you commits adultery except that God will remove from him the light of faith. If He wills, To reject it, and if he wants to prevent it, he can prevent it."
"30990","(30990) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said, It is astonishing for our brothers who The people of Iraq call Al-Hajjaj a believer."
"30991","(30991) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’biy, he said: I bear witness that he is a believer in the tyrant but an unbeliever. By God, meaning the pilgrims."
"30992","(30992) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythama, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: He comes upon the people. A long time ago, they gathered together and prayed in the mosques, but there was not a believer among them."
"30993","(30993) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, he said: We said to Talq bin Habib: Describe for us piety. He said: Piety is an act of obedience to God, hoping for God’s mercy upon light from God[corrupt] And piety is abandoning disobedience to God and fearing God with light from God."
"30994","(30994) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, that when he mentioned al-Hajjaj, he would say: May God’s curse be upon the wrongdoers."
"30995","(30995) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Sufficient is he who doubts about Al-Hajjaj because of his beard. God"
"30996","(30996) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masawar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who sleeps full while his neighbor is at his side is not a believer.\n(Abu Ali 2691 Hakim 167)"
"30997","(30997) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talq bin Habib, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: There are three things whoever is in it will find the taste and sweetness of faith: that God and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else, and that He is loved for the sake of God and hated for the sake of God, and he mentioned polytheism."
"30998","(30998) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, and Ibn Abbas. They entered upon Omar when he was stabbed, and they said: Prayer. He said: There is no luck for anyone in Islam who misses the prayer and prays, and is wounded by Yath’ab. Blood (Bayhaqi 357)"
"30999","(30999) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Shabak, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, that he used to say To his companions: Walk with us and we will increase in faith."
"31000","(31000) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal Al-Muharbi, he said: He told me Moaz, sit with us, we will believe in the hour, meaning we will remember God."
"31001","(31001) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mahdi ibn Maymun, on the authority of Imran al-Qusayr, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, he said: Abu Al-Darda’ used to say: Oh God, I ask you for everlasting faith, beneficial knowledge, and valuable guidance. Mu’awiyah said: So we see that those who Faith is faith that is not permanent, and from knowledge is knowledge that is not beneficial, and from guidance is guidance that is not valuable."
"31002","(31002) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Jami’ ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Hilal: He said: Muadh used to say to a man From his brothers: Sit with us, and let us believe soon, and in two sitting they will remember God and praise Him."
"31003","(31003) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Talha, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Zirr, who said: Umar was one of those who took with his hand. The man and two men are among his companions, and he says: Arise, and we will increase in faith."
"31004","(31004) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Misra and Al-Mughirah bin Shibl, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab Al-Ahmasi, on the authority of Salman, said: The example of the five daily prayers is like the arrows of spoils of war, so whoever hits them with five He is better than he who multiplies it by four, and he who multiplies it by four is better than he who multiplies it by three. And whoever hits it with three arrows is better than he who hits it with two arrows, and whoever hits it with two arrows is better. Whoever hits it with an arrow, and God has not made one who has an arrow in Islam like one who has no arrow."
"31005","(31005) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awwam, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, on the authority of Abu Zur’i, on the authority of Abu Huraira said, “Faith is light. So whoever commits adultery, faith will depart from him. So whoever blames himself and returns, faith will return.”"
"31006","(31006) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The most perfect of believers in faith is the one with the best character."
"31007","(31007) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The most perfect of believers in faith, and the best of believers in faith are those with the best character."
"31008","(31008) Hafs told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: The most complete of believers in faith is those who have the best character."
"31009","(31009) Al-Muqri’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The most perfect of the believers are those with the best character."
"31010","(31010) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, he said: My greatest suspicion is that he said On the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: Ibn Omar said: Modesty and faith are all linked, so if one is removed, the other is removed."
"31011","(31011) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: A man with Abdullah said: I am a believer, so he said: Say: I am in Paradise, but we believe in God and His angels and His books and His messengers."
"31012","(31012) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: It was said to him: Are you a believer? He said: I hope."
"31013","(31013) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Simak bin Salamah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Asmah, that Aisha, She said: You are the believers, God willing."
"31014","(31014) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, he said: If one of you is asked: You are a believer, so do not doubt."
"31015","(31015) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ziyad bin Alaqah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, who said: If he is asked One of you: Are you a believer? Let him not doubt his faith."
"31016","(31016) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of a man whom he did not name, on the authority of his father, he said : I heard Ibn Masoud say: I am a believer."
"31017","(31017) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: A man came and said: I met a group of people, so I said: Who are you? They said: We are the believers. He said: Did they not say: We are in Paradise."
"31018","(31018) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mahal, on the authority of Abraham, when they were asked, they would say: We believe in God and His angels and His books and His messengers."
"31019","(31019) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I met Abdullah bin Maqil, and I said to him: Some people from the people of The righteous people criticize me for saying: I am a believer. Abdullah bin Maqil said: You have been disappointed and lost if you are not a believer."
"31020","(31020) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Munabbih, on the authority of Siwar ibn Shabib, who said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: Here are people who testify against me of disbelief, so he said: Don’t you say: There is no god but Allah and deny them?"
"31021","(31021) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd Al-Ansari, He said: Call yourselves by the names that God has named you with Hanafiyyah, Islam and faith."
"31022","(31022) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Salma bin Sabra, he said: Muadh addressed us, and he said: You The believers, and you are the people of Paradise."
"31023","(31023) Omar bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar bin Burqan, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to us: As for what follows, there is The religion and the foundation of Islam are faith in God, establishing prayer, and paying zakat, so pray the prayer at its appointed time."
"31024","(31024) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: “From the Fire will come the one who has said, ‘There is no god but Allah,’ and there is a grain of goodness in his heart.” Then the second one said: There will come out of Hell who said there is no god but Allah, and in his heart there is as much goodness weighing as much as righteousness. Then he said: There will come out of Hell who said No. There is no god but Allah, and there was in his heart as much goodness as an atom’s weight."
"31025","(31025) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of His father, that a group of people came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave them to them, except for one of them, and Saad said: O Messenger of God, I gave them to you and left so-and-so, by God, I see him as a believer. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Or a Muslim. Saad said: By God, I see him as a believer, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Or a Muslim, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. That is three times."
"31026","(31026) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, he said: It is said to him: Ask and it will be given to you, meaning The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, intercede, and you will be interceded, and supplicate, and it will be answered. Then he raises his head and says: My nation, my nation, twice, or three times, and he said Salman intercedes on behalf of everyone who has a grain of wheat’s weight of faith in his heart, or a barley’s weight of faith, or a weight of faith. A mustard seed of faith. Salman said: That is the Praiseworthy Station."
"31027","(31027) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr informed us, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The adulterer does not commit adultery when he commits adultery while he is a believer, and he does not steal when he steals. He is a believer, and he does not drink alcohol when he drinks while he is a believer, and he does not resort to looting while people raise their eyes to it. And he is a believer."
"31028","(31028) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: The adulterer does not commit adultery when he commits adultery. He is a believer, and he does not steal when he steals while he is a believer, and he does not drink, meaning alcohol, when he drinks while he is a believer. So beware of you."
"31029","(31029) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mudrik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The fornicator does not commit adultery when he commits adultery while he is a believer, nor does he steal when he steals while he is a believer, nor does he drink. When he drinks wine, he is a believer, and we do not take away any honorable thing to which Muslims raise their heads, and he is Believer"
"31030","(31030) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, he said: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Mudrik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace. Like it"
"31031","(31031) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: modesty is a part of faith, faith is in heaven, indecency is a part of indecency, and indecency is in Hell."
"31032","(31032) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that he said: It was said: O Messenger of God, which deeds are best? He said: Patience and forgiveness. It was said: Which of the believers is most complete in faith? He said: The best of them in character."
"31033","(31033) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Between a servant and disbelief is abandonment of prayer. (Abu Dawud 4445. Tirmidhi 2620)"
"31034","(31034) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him. Like it (Muslim 88. Tirmidhi 2619)"
"31035","(31035) Yahya bin Wadh narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, who said: I heard Ibn Buraidah saying: I heard my father. He says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The covenant between us and them is the prayer, so whoever abandons it has Infidelity\n(Tirmidhi 2421. Ahmad 346)"
"31036","(31036) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Whoever does not pray has no debt."
"31037","(31037) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawī, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Qalābī, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Buraidah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever abandons the afternoon prayer, his work has been vain."
"31038","(31038) Issa and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abi Qalabi, On the authority of Abu Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Buraidah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Whoever abandons the afternoon prayer, his work has been vain."
"31039","(31039) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Abbad bin Misra Al-Manqari informed us, on the authority of Abu Qulabib and Al-Hasan, that they They were sitting, and Abu Qalaba said: Abu Darda’ said: Whoever neglects the afternoon prayer to the point of missing it without an excuse, his work has been vain. He said: And Al-Hasan said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever neglects an obligatory prayer until you miss it without an excuse, has His work was ruined."
"31040","(31040) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Qasamah bin Zuhayr, he said: There is no faith for the one who does not. His trust is His, and there is no debt to one to whom there is no covenant."
"31041","(31041) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The best of servants is a good opinion."
"31042","(31042) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Maymun, who said: I said to Ata’, “We have received people whom we consider to be righteous people.” If we say, “We are believers,” they will blame us. He said, “Ataa said, “We are the believing Muslims.” And so did the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, they say."
"31043","(31043) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: There are four hearts: a pure heart, so that is the heart of the hypocrite, a uncircumcised heart, so that is the heart of the disbeliever, and a barren heart, as if In it is a lamp that blossoms, so that is the heart of the believer, and a heart in which there is both hypocrisy and faith, so his likeness is like a sore that is spread with it. Pus and blood, and his likeness is like that of a tree that has been watered with bad water and good water, so which water has overcome it, it has been defeated. (Tabari 406)"
"31044","(31044) Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He often said: O converter of hearts, make my heart steadfast in your religion. They said: O Messenger of God: We believe in you and in what you have brought. So do you fear for us? He said: The hearts are between two of God’s fingers. He turns them over."
"31045","(31045) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, saying: Abu Ka’b, the owner of the silk, narrated to us, saying: Shahr bin Hawshab narrated to us, saying: I said: To Umm Salamah: O Mother of the Believers, what was the most frequent supplication of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he was with you? He said: I said: His most frequent supplications were: O converter of hearts, make my heart steadfast in your religion. I said: O Messenger of God, how many are your supplications, O converter of hearts? Hearts: Make my heart steadfast in your religion. He said: O Umm Salama: There is not a single human being who does not have his heart between two of God’s fingers. He stays as long as He wishes, and He deviates as He wishes."
"31046","(31046) Zaid told us, he said: Hammam bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Umm Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: O converter of hearts, make my heart steadfast in your religion. I said: O Messenger of God, you will recite this supplication. He said: O Aisha, did you not know that the heart of the son of Adam is between the fingers of God? If He wants to lead his heart to guidance, then His heart, and if He wants to lead his heart to error, then His heart."
"31047","(31047) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla narrating, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite these supplications: O Converter of hearts, make my heart steadfast in your religion."
"31048","(31048) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Mihanani, who said: Abdullah said: I did not see He who lacks religion and opinion is more likely to be among men who have authority over their affairs than women. They said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, and what a deficiency? Her religion. He said: She left prayer during the days of her menstruation. They said: What is the deficiency in her intelligence? He said: It is not permissible for two women to be witnesses. Except with the testimony of a man."
"31049","(31049) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hasan ibn Ayash, on the authority of Mughirah, who said: Abraham was asked about a man who says to a man: Are you a believer? He said: The answer is an innovation, and I am not pleased that I doubted it."
"31050","(31050) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Habib ibn al-Shahid, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: The adulterer shall not commit adultery. When he commits adultery while he is a believer, and he does not steal while he is a believer, and he does not drink alcohol while he is a believer."
"31051","(31051) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ammar bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Hudhayfa, he said: By God, a man will see in the morning, and then in the evening he will not see with a finger."
"31052","(31052) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Yasar, who said: Umar reported that a man in the Levant claimed He is a believer. He said: So Omar wrote: They brought him to me. So he came to Omar and said: You are the one who claims that you are a believer. He said: Yes. He said: Were people in the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except in three positions: a believer, an unbeliever, and a hypocrite? I am not an unbeliever, nor have I been a hypocrite. He said: Then Omar said to him: Extend your hand. Ibn Idris said: I said: He is satisfied with what he said: He said: He is satisfied with what He said"
"31053","(31053) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Saad bin Sinan, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: There will be temptations at the hands of the Hour like the passage of a dark night, and a man will become a believer in it in the morning. He will be an unbeliever in the evening, and he will be an unbeliever in the morning, and in the evening he will be a believer. (Hakim 438. Tirmidhi 2197)"
"31054","(31054) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Amr Al-Sibani, he said: He said: Hudhaifa: Indeed, I know that the people of two religions, the people of those two religions, are in Hell: they are people of religion who say: Faith is speech. Nor any deed, even if he kills, even if he commits adultery. And the people of religion say: He was our first. I think he mentioned a word that I had neglected, so that they may command us. Five prayers every day, and there are only two prayers: the evening prayer and the dawn prayer."
"31055","(31055) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Harry, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Faith is sixty, or seventy, or a few, or one. The highest of the two numbers is the testimony that there is no god but Allah, and the lowest of them is removing harmful things from the path, and the living is a part of the faith."
"31056","(31056) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: modesty is part of faith. (Muslim 63 Tirmidhi 2615)"
"31057","(31057) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Habba bin Juwayn Al-Arni, who said: We were with Salman and we were in line with the enemy, and he said: These are the believers, these are the hypocrites, and these are the polytheists, so God will grant victory. The hypocrites with the claim of the believers, and God supports the believers with the claim of the hypocrites."
"31058","(31058) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Qurayh, who said: Salman said to a man: If you were to cut off your limbs, you would not attain faith."
"31059","(31059) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The strongest bonds of Islam are love for the sake of God and hatred for the sake of God. (Ahmed 286)"
"31060","(31060) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughul, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The bonds of faith are tied with love. in God and hatred in Him."
"31061","(31061) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Dawud informed us, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Tamim al-Dari, he said: The first thing a servant will be held accountable for on the Day of Resurrection is the obligatory prayer. If he completes it, otherwise it will be said: See if he has any voluntary prayers. Then the obligatory prayer was completed from his voluntary prayers, so if the obligatory prayers were not completed and there was no voluntary prayer for him, then his two ends are taken away and he is thrown away. With Him in Hell.\n(Ibn Majah 1426. Darmi 1355)"
"31062","(31062) Yunus bin Harun told us, he said: Abu Ma’shar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salih Al-Ansari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He met Awf bin Malik and said: How have you become, Awf bin Malik? He said: You have become a true believer, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, every saying has a truth, so what is that? He said: O Messenger of God: Have I not deceived myself? This world, my nights have made me sleepless and I have been thirsty for my work, and it is as if I am looking at the throne of my Lord, and as if I am looking at the people of Paradise, they quarrel therein, and it is as if I were looking at the people of Hell quarreling therein. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: If you know or believe, then stick to it."
